window.IELTS_DATA.items.push(...[{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Your favourite animal, then and now","prompt":"What is your favourite animal and why?\nDo you like the same animal you liked when you were younger?\nWhat can you learn about people from the animals they like?\nWhich animals are popular as pets in your country?","answer":"Q: What is your favourite animal and why?\nA: Dogs are my favourite because they&#x27;re responsive and emotionally expressive. A well-trained dog can become <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a genuine companion</strong>, rather than simply a pet.\n\nQ: Do you like the same animal you liked when you were younger?\nA: Yes. I liked dogs as a child because my grandparents had one, and that&#x27;s probably why I still love them today. I still admire how easily dogs <strong class=\"key-phrase\">build trust with people</strong>.\n\nQ: What can you learn about people from the animals they like?\nA: You might get a small clue about someone&#x27;s lifestyle, but I wouldn&#x27;t read too much into it. An energetic person may prefer dogs, while someone who values quiet may choose cats, but personality is <strong class=\"key-phrase\">far more complex</strong> than a pet preference.\n\nQ: Which animals are popular as pets in your country?\nA: Dogs and cats are the most common pets, while fish and small birds are popular in apartments. The choice often depends on space, cost and how much time the owner can <strong class=\"key-phrase\">devote to daily care</strong>.","topic":"Animals","phrases":[{"en":"a genuine companion","context":"Q: What is your favourite animal and why?\nA: Dogs are my favourite because they're responsive and emotionally expressive. A well-trained dog can become a genuine companion, rather than simply a pet."},{"en":"build trust with people","context":"Q: Do you like the same animal you liked when you were younger?\nA: Yes. I liked dogs as a child because my grandparents had one, and that's probably why I still love them today. I still admire how easily dogs build trust with people."},{"en":"far more complex","context":"Q: What can you learn about people from the animals they like?\nA: You might get a small clue about someone's lifestyle, but I wouldn't read too much into it. An energetic person may prefer dogs, while someone who values quiet may choose cats, but personality is far more complex than a pet preference."},{"en":"devote to daily care","context":"Q: Which animals are popular as pets in your country?\nA: Dogs and cats are the most common pets, while fish and small birds are popular in apartments. The choice often depends on space, cost and how much time the owner can devote to daily care."}],"subtype":"Part 1","summary":"Animal","visual":null,"id":"speaking-part-1-001","_displayNo":"#001","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-001-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-001-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-001-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-001-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"Dogs are my favourite animals because they react to people and show their feelings clearly. If a dog is well trained, it can become a close friend, not just a pet.","phrases":[{"en":"a close friend","meaning":"Someone you know well and care about."}],"question":"What is your favourite animal and why?","html":"Dogs are my favourite animals because they react to people and show their feelings clearly. If a dog is well trained, it can become <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a close friend</strong>, not just a pet."},{"text":"Yes, I still like dogs. My grandparents had one when I was a child, so I grew up liking them. I also like how easily dogs learn to trust people.","phrases":[{"en":"grew up","meaning":"Spent your childhood and became older."}],"question":"Do you like the same animal you liked when you were younger?","html":"Yes, I still like dogs. My grandparents had one when I was a child, so I <strong class=\"key-phrase\">grew up</strong> liking them. I also like how easily dogs learn to trust people."},{"text":"You may learn a little about someone's lifestyle. Active people might like dogs, while quieter people may prefer cats. However, you cannot judge someone's whole personality from their favourite animal.","phrases":[{"en":"judge someone","meaning":"Form an opinion about a person."}],"question":"What can you learn about people from the animals they like?","html":"You may learn a little about someone&#x27;s lifestyle. Active people might like dogs, while quieter people may prefer cats. However, you cannot <strong class=\"key-phrase\">judge someone</strong>&#x27;s whole personality from their favourite animal."},{"text":"Dogs and cats are the most popular pets. People in flats also keep fish and small birds. Their choice depends on their space, budget and the time they have to look after a pet.","phrases":[{"en":"look after","meaning":"Take care of someone or something."}],"question":"Which animals are popular as pets in your country?","html":"Dogs and cats are the most popular pets. People in flats also keep fish and small birds. Their choice depends on their space, budget and the time they have to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">look after</strong> a pet."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-001-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-001-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-001-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-001-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Art lessons, drawing and galleries","prompt":"Did you enjoy doing art lessons when you were a child?\nDo you ever draw or paint pictures now?\nWhen was the last time you went to an art gallery or exhibition?\nWhat kind of pictures do you like having in your home?","answer":"Q: Did you enjoy doing art lessons when you were a child?\nA: No I didn&#x27;t. I was never very good at drawing or painting, and I found art lessons quite slow and boring. I preferred <strong class=\"key-phrase\">language and science lessons</strong>.\n\nQ: Do you ever draw or paint pictures now?\nA: No, I don&#x27;t draw or paint these days, because there&#x27;s never any need for me to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">create art at work</strong>, and I still don&#x27;t enjoy art as a hobby.\n\nQ: When was the last time you went to an art gallery or exhibition?\nA: I honestly can&#x27;t remember the last time I went to any kind of <strong class=\"key-phrase\">art exhibition</strong>; I&#x27;m <strong class=\"key-phrase\">not much of</strong> an art fan, and I tend to go to music concerts, the cinema or the theatre instead of art shows.\n\nQ: What kind of pictures do you like having in your home?\nA: I don&#x27;t have any paintings or artistic images in my home, but I do have photos of family members and some nice photos of landscapes on the walls to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">brighten the place up</strong>.","topic":"Art","phrases":[{"en":"language and science lessons","context":"Q: Did you enjoy doing art lessons when you were a child?\nA: No I didn't. I was never very good at drawing or painting, and I found art lessons quite slow and boring. I preferred language and science lessons."},{"en":"create art at work","context":"Q: Do you ever draw or paint pictures now?\nA: No, I don't draw or paint these days, because there's never any need for me to create art at work, and I still don't enjoy art as a hobby."},{"en":"art exhibition","context":"Q: When was the last time you went to an art gallery or exhibition?\nA: I honestly can't remember the last time I went to any kind of art exhibition; I'm not much of an art fan, and I tend to go to music concerts, the cinema or the theatre instead of art shows."},{"en":"not much of","context":"Q: When was the last time you went to an art gallery or exhibition?\nA: I honestly can't remember the last time I went to any kind of art exhibition; I'm not much of an art fan, and I tend to go to music concerts, the cinema or the theatre instead of art shows."},{"en":"brighten the place up","context":"Q: What kind of pictures do you like having in your home?\nA: I don't have any paintings or artistic images in my home, but I do have photos of family members and some nice photos of landscapes on the walls to brighten the place up."}],"subtype":"","summary":"Art","id":"speaking-part-1-002","_displayNo":"#002","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-002-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-002-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-002-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-002-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"No, I didn't really enjoy them. I wasn't good at drawing or painting, and the lessons felt slow and boring. I liked language and science classes more.","phrases":[{"en":"wasn't good at","meaning":"Did not have much skill in something."}],"question":"Did you enjoy doing art lessons when you were a child?","html":"No, I didn&#x27;t really enjoy them. I <strong class=\"key-phrase\">wasn&#x27;t good at</strong> drawing or painting, and the lessons felt slow and boring. I liked language and science classes more."},{"text":"No, I don't draw or paint now. I don't need to do it for my job, and it is still not a hobby that I enjoy.","phrases":[{"en":"for my job","meaning":"As part of the work I do."}],"question":"Do you ever draw or paint pictures now?","html":"No, I don&#x27;t draw or paint now. I don&#x27;t need to do it <strong class=\"key-phrase\">for my job</strong>, and it is still not a hobby that I enjoy."},{"text":"I can't remember my last visit because I'm not very interested in art. I usually choose a concert, a film or a play instead of an art exhibition.","phrases":[{"en":"instead of","meaning":"In place of something else."}],"question":"When was the last time you went to an art gallery or exhibition?","html":"I can&#x27;t remember my last visit because I&#x27;m not very interested in art. I usually choose a concert, a film or a play <strong class=\"key-phrase\">instead of</strong> an art exhibition."},{"text":"I don't have paintings at home, but I do have family photos and pictures of beautiful places. They make the rooms look brighter and more welcoming.","phrases":[{"en":"more welcoming","meaning":"Making people feel more comfortable and happy to be there."}],"question":"What kind of pictures do you like having in your home?","html":"I don&#x27;t have paintings at home, but I do have family photos and pictures of beautiful places. They make the rooms look brighter and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">more welcoming</strong>."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-002-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-002-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-002-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-002-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"How bicycles are used in your country","prompt":"How are bicycles used in your country?\nHow popular are bicycles in your country?\nAre they used more now than in the past and why?\nWhat do bicycles mean to you?","answer":"Q: How are bicycles used in your country?\nA: Bicycles are mainly used for short journeys, exercise and leisure. In large cities they&#x27;re less common for commuting because motorbikes dominate the roads, although public bicycle schemes are <strong class=\"key-phrase\">gradually gaining ground</strong>.\n\nQ: How popular are bicycles in your country?\nA: They&#x27;re moderately popular, particularly among students and people who cycle for fitness. But the lack of protected lanes prevents cycling from becoming <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a mainstream form of transport</strong>.\n\nQ: Are they used more now than in the past and why?\nA: Recreational cycling is more visible than it was a decade ago, partly because people are more health-conscious. Everyday commuting hasn&#x27;t grown as quickly, since traffic safety remains <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a major concern</strong>.\n\nQ: What do bicycles mean to you?\nA: To me, a bicycle represents independence and uncomplicated exercise. It lets me travel <strong class=\"key-phrase\">at my own pace</strong>, avoid short car journeys and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">clear my head</strong> at the same time.","topic":"Bicycles","phrases":[{"en":"gradually gaining ground","context":"Q: How are bicycles used in your country?\nA: Bicycles are mainly used for short journeys, exercise and leisure. In large cities they're less common for commuting because motorbikes dominate the roads, although public bicycle schemes are gradually gaining ground."},{"en":"a mainstream form of transport","context":"Q: How popular are bicycles in your country?\nA: They're moderately popular, particularly among students and people who cycle for fitness. But the lack of protected lanes prevents cycling from becoming a mainstream form of transport."},{"en":"a major concern","context":"Q: Are they used more now than in the past and why?\nA: Recreational cycling is more visible than it was a decade ago, partly because people are more health-conscious. Everyday commuting hasn't grown as quickly, since traffic safety remains a major concern."},{"en":"at my own pace","context":"Q: What do bicycles mean to you?\nA: To me, a bicycle represents independence and uncomplicated exercise. It lets me travel at my own pace, avoid short car journeys and clear my head at the same time."},{"en":"clear my head","context":"Q: What do bicycles mean to you?\nA: To me, a bicycle represents independence and uncomplicated exercise. It lets me travel at my own pace, avoid short car journeys and clear my head at the same time."}],"subtype":"Part 1","summary":"Bicycle","visual":null,"id":"speaking-part-1-003","_displayNo":"#003","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-003-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-003-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-003-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-003-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"People mainly use bicycles for short trips, exercise and fun. Fewer people cycle to work in big cities because there are so many motorbikes, although public bicycle services are becoming more common.","phrases":[{"en":"short trips","meaning":"Journeys that do not take much time or cover much distance."}],"question":"How are bicycles used in your country?","html":"People mainly use bicycles for <strong class=\"key-phrase\">short trips</strong>, exercise and fun. Fewer people cycle to work in big cities because there are so many motorbikes, although public bicycle services are becoming more common."},{"text":"They are fairly popular with students and people who want to exercise. However, there aren't enough safe cycle lanes, so many people do not use bicycles as their main way of travelling.","phrases":[{"en":"cycle lanes","meaning":"Parts of a road intended for people riding bicycles."}],"question":"How popular are bicycles in your country?","html":"They are fairly popular with students and people who want to exercise. However, there aren&#x27;t enough safe <strong class=\"key-phrase\">cycle lanes</strong>, so many people do not use bicycles as their main way of travelling."},{"text":"More people seem to cycle for exercise than ten years ago because they care more about their health. Cycling to work has not increased as much because people still worry about road safety.","phrases":[{"en":"road safety","meaning":"Keeping people safe when they use roads."}],"question":"Are they used more now than in the past and why?","html":"More people seem to cycle for exercise than ten years ago because they care more about their health. Cycling to work has not increased as much because people still worry about <strong class=\"key-phrase\">road safety</strong>."},{"text":"A bicycle gives me freedom and an easy way to exercise. I can choose my own speed, avoid using a car for short trips and relax my mind while I ride.","phrases":[{"en":"my own speed","meaning":"A speed that I choose and find comfortable."}],"question":"What do bicycles mean to you?","html":"A bicycle gives me freedom and an easy way to exercise. I can choose <strong class=\"key-phrase\">my own speed</strong>, avoid using a car for short trips and relax my mind while I ride."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-003-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-003-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-003-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-003-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Reading in English and where you read","prompt":"What kinds of things do you enjoy reading in English?\nAre you someone who can read anywhere, or do you have a favourite place?\nDo you need peace and quiet to read, or can you concentrate in noisy places?\nHow did you first learn to read?","answer":"Q: What kinds of things do you enjoy reading in English?\nA: I mostly read non-fiction in English — psychology, technology, that kind of thing, and books on <strong class=\"key-phrase\">personal development</strong>. They&#x27;re great for my vocabulary, and they give me ideas I can <strong class=\"key-phrase\">apply in real life</strong>.\n\nQ: Are you someone who can read anywhere, or do you have a favourite place?\nA: I can read almost anywhere, but I concentrate best at a quiet desk by a window. That&#x27;s what helps me <strong class=\"key-phrase\">stay fully absorbed</strong>, without checking my phone every few minutes.\n\nQ: Do you need peace and quiet to read, or can you concentrate in noisy places?\nA: If it&#x27;s something difficult, I need a fairly quiet environment. I can skim an article in a cafe, but serious reading needs enough silence for me to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">process the ideas properly</strong>.\n\nQ: How did you first learn to read?\nA: I first learned by sounding out short words with my parents, then reading picture books at school. Once I found books I genuinely enjoyed, reading didn&#x27;t feel like homework any more — it just became <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a habit of my own</strong>.","topic":"Books","phrases":[{"en":"personal development","context":"Q: What kinds of things do you enjoy reading in English?\nA: I mostly read non-fiction in English — psychology, technology, that kind of thing, and books on personal development. They're great for my vocabulary, and they give me ideas I can apply in real life."},{"en":"apply in real life","context":"Q: What kinds of things do you enjoy reading in English?\nA: I mostly read non-fiction in English — psychology, technology, that kind of thing, and books on personal development. They're great for my vocabulary, and they give me ideas I can apply in real life."},{"en":"stay fully absorbed","context":"Q: Are you someone who can read anywhere, or do you have a favourite place?\nA: I can read almost anywhere, but I concentrate best at a quiet desk by a window. That's what helps me stay fully absorbed, without checking my phone every few minutes."},{"en":"process the ideas properly","context":"Q: Do you need peace and quiet to read, or can you concentrate in noisy places?\nA: If it's something difficult, I need a fairly quiet environment. I can skim an article in a cafe, but serious reading needs enough silence for me to process the ideas properly."},{"en":"a habit of my own","context":"Q: How did you first learn to read?\nA: I first learned by sounding out short words with my parents, then reading picture books at school. Once I found books I genuinely enjoyed, reading didn't feel like homework any more — it just became a habit of my own."}],"subtype":"Part 1","summary":"Book","visual":null,"id":"speaking-part-1-004","_displayNo":"#004","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-004-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-004-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-004-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-004-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"I mainly read books about real subjects, such as psychology, technology and improving myself. They help me learn new English words and give me useful ideas for everyday life.","phrases":[{"en":"everyday life","meaning":"The normal things people do each day."}],"question":"What kinds of things do you enjoy reading in English?","html":"I mainly read books about real subjects, such as psychology, technology and improving myself. They help me learn new English words and give me useful ideas for <strong class=\"key-phrase\">everyday life</strong>."},{"text":"I can read in most places, but my favourite spot is a quiet desk near a window. I can focus there without looking at my phone all the time.","phrases":[{"en":"focus","meaning":"Give your attention to one thing."}],"question":"Are you someone who can read anywhere, or do you have a favourite place?","html":"I can read in most places, but my favourite spot is a quiet desk near a window. I can <strong class=\"key-phrase\">focus</strong> there without looking at my phone all the time."},{"text":"I need quiet when I read something difficult. I can read a short article quickly in a cafe, but I need less noise to understand more serious ideas.","phrases":[{"en":"less noise","meaning":"A smaller amount of unwanted sound."}],"question":"Do you need peace and quiet to read, or can you concentrate in noisy places?","html":"I need quiet when I read something difficult. I can read a short article quickly in a cafe, but I need <strong class=\"key-phrase\">less noise</strong> to understand more serious ideas."},{"text":"My parents first helped me read short words by saying their sounds. Later, I read picture books at school. When I found books I liked, I started reading because I wanted to.","phrases":[{"en":"picture books","meaning":"Books that use pictures to help tell a story."}],"question":"How did you first learn to read?","html":"My parents first helped me read short words by saying their sounds. Later, I read <strong class=\"key-phrase\">picture books</strong> at school. When I found books I liked, I started reading because I wanted to."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-004-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-004-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-004-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-004-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"An interesting building, and preserving old ones","prompt":"Can you tell me about an interesting building in your hometown?\nWhy should we preserve historical buildings?\nHow have architecture and building materials changed in your country?\nWhat type of building do you prefer to live in and why?","answer":"Q: Can you tell me about an interesting building in your hometown?\nA: The Hanoi Opera House is one of the most striking buildings in my city. Its French-inspired façade and central location give it <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a distinctive character</strong> that modern glass towers often lack.\n\nQ: Why should we preserve historical buildings?\nA: Historical buildings preserve evidence of how a city developed and give residents <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a sense of continuity</strong>. Once they&#x27;re demolished, the knowledge and atmosphere they carry can&#x27;t be recreated convincingly.\n\nQ: How have architecture and building materials changed in your country?\nA: New buildings use more steel, glass and prefabricated materials, while older homes relied heavily on brick and timber. Designs have also become more compact and energy-efficient to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">meet urban needs</strong>.\n\nQ: What type of building do you prefer to live in and why?\nA: I&#x27;d prefer a medium-sized apartment with natural light, good soundproofing and access to public transport. I don&#x27;t need luxury, but I value a home that&#x27;s <strong class=\"key-phrase\">easy to maintain</strong> and comfortable throughout the year.","topic":"Buildings","phrases":[{"en":"a distinctive character","context":"Q: Can you tell me about an interesting building in your hometown?\nA: The Hanoi Opera House is one of the most striking buildings in my city. Its French-inspired façade and central location give it a distinctive character that modern glass towers often lack."},{"en":"a sense of continuity","context":"Q: Why should we preserve historical buildings?\nA: Historical buildings preserve evidence of how a city developed and give residents a sense of continuity. Once they're demolished, the knowledge and atmosphere they carry can't be recreated convincingly."},{"en":"meet urban needs","context":"Q: How have architecture and building materials changed in your country?\nA: New buildings use more steel, glass and prefabricated materials, while older homes relied heavily on brick and timber. Designs have also become more compact and energy-efficient to meet urban needs."},{"en":"easy to maintain","context":"Q: What type of building do you prefer to live in and why?\nA: I'd prefer a medium-sized apartment with natural light, good soundproofing and access to public transport. I don't need luxury, but I value a home that's easy to maintain and comfortable throughout the year."}],"subtype":"Part 1","summary":"Building","visual":null,"id":"speaking-part-1-005","_displayNo":"#005","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-005-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-005-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-005-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-005-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"The Hanoi Opera House is an interesting building in my city. It has a French-style front and stands in the city centre. It looks quite different from modern glass buildings.","phrases":[{"en":"city centre","meaning":"The main central area of a city."}],"question":"Can you tell me about an interesting building in your hometown?","html":"The Hanoi Opera House is an interesting building in my city. It has a French-style front and stands in the <strong class=\"key-phrase\">city centre</strong>. It looks quite different from modern glass buildings."},{"text":"Old buildings show us how a city has changed and help people feel connected to its past. If we knock them down, it is difficult to bring back their history and special feeling.","phrases":[{"en":"knock them down","meaning":"Destroy buildings so they no longer stand."}],"question":"Why should we preserve historical buildings?","html":"Old buildings show us how a city has changed and help people feel connected to its past. If we <strong class=\"key-phrase\">knock them down</strong>, it is difficult to bring back their history and special feeling."},{"text":"Modern buildings use more steel, glass and ready-made parts, while older houses used mainly bricks and wood. New designs also save space and energy because cities have different needs now.","phrases":[{"en":"save space","meaning":"Use less room or make better use of it."}],"question":"How have architecture and building materials changed in your country?","html":"Modern buildings use more steel, glass and ready-made parts, while older houses used mainly bricks and wood. New designs also <strong class=\"key-phrase\">save space</strong> and energy because cities have different needs now."},{"text":"I'd like a medium-sized flat with plenty of daylight, little noise and public transport nearby. It doesn't need to be expensive, but it should be comfortable and easy to keep in good condition.","phrases":[{"en":"in good condition","meaning":"Working well and not damaged."}],"question":"What type of building do you prefer to live in and why?","html":"I&#x27;d like a medium-sized flat with plenty of daylight, little noise and public transport nearby. It doesn&#x27;t need to be expensive, but it should be comfortable and easy to keep <strong class=\"key-phrase\">in good condition</strong>."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-005-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-005-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-005-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-005-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Chocolate: what you eat and when","prompt":"Do you like chocolate?\nWhat type of chocolate do you prefer?\nWhen do you usually eat chocolate?\nDo people give chocolate as a present in your country?","answer":"Q: Do you like chocolate?\nA: Yes, I love chocolate. I like the taste, the texture and the feeling that you get when you eat it. And it <strong class=\"key-phrase\">goes really well with</strong> my favourite drink, coffee.\n\nQ: What type of chocolate do you prefer?\nA: I prefer <strong class=\"key-phrase\">dark chocolate</strong> to milk chocolate, because it has <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a stronger taste</strong>. I also like chocolate when it&#x27;s in a cake, and I love drinking hot chocolate too.\n\nQ: When do you usually eat chocolate?\nA: I try not to eat too much, but I probably eat or drink something that contains chocolate <strong class=\"key-phrase\">every couple of days</strong>.\n\nQ: Do people give chocolate as a present in your country?\nA: Yes, it&#x27;s very common to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">give boxes of individual chocolates</strong> as a gift. You can give chocolates on any special occasion really: birthdays, Valentine&#x27;s Day, Easter, Christmas, and so on.","topic":"Chocolate","phrases":[{"en":"goes really well with","context":"Q: Do you like chocolate?\nA: Yes, I love chocolate. I like the taste, the texture and the feeling that you get when you eat it. And it goes really well with my favourite drink, coffee."},{"en":"dark chocolate","context":"Q: What type of chocolate do you prefer?\nA: I prefer dark chocolate to milk chocolate, because it has a stronger taste. I also like chocolate when it's in a cake, and I love drinking hot chocolate too."},{"en":"a stronger taste","context":"Q: What type of chocolate do you prefer?\nA: I prefer dark chocolate to milk chocolate, because it has a stronger taste. I also like chocolate when it's in a cake, and I love drinking hot chocolate too."},{"en":"every couple of days","context":"Q: When do you usually eat chocolate?\nA: I try not to eat too much, but I probably eat or drink something that contains chocolate every couple of days."},{"en":"give boxes of individual chocolates","context":"Q: Do people give chocolate as a present in your country?\nA: Yes, it's very common to give boxes of individual chocolates as a gift. You can give chocolates on any special occasion really: birthdays, Valentine's Day, Easter, Christmas, and so on."}],"subtype":"","summary":"Chocolate","id":"speaking-part-1-006","_displayNo":"#006","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-006-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-006-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-006-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-006-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"Yes, I really like chocolate. I enjoy its taste and how it feels when I eat it. It also tastes good with coffee, which is my favourite drink.","phrases":[{"en":"tastes good with","meaning":"Has a pleasant flavour when eaten or drunk with something else."}],"question":"Do you like chocolate?","html":"Yes, I really like chocolate. I enjoy its taste and how it feels when I eat it. It also <strong class=\"key-phrase\">tastes good with</strong> coffee, which is my favourite drink."},{"text":"I prefer dark chocolate because its flavour is stronger than milk chocolate. I also enjoy chocolate cake and hot chocolate, so I like it in different forms.","phrases":[{"en":"in different forms","meaning":"In several different types or ways."}],"question":"What type of chocolate do you prefer?","html":"I prefer dark chocolate because its flavour is stronger than milk chocolate. I also enjoy chocolate cake and hot chocolate, so I like it <strong class=\"key-phrase\">in different forms</strong>."},{"text":"I try to limit how much chocolate I have. Still, I usually eat or drink something with chocolate in it about once every two days.","phrases":[{"en":"limit","meaning":"Control something so there is not too much of it."}],"question":"When do you usually eat chocolate?","html":"I try to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">limit</strong> how much chocolate I have. Still, I usually eat or drink something with chocolate in it about once every two days."},{"text":"Yes, boxes of chocolates are common gifts in my country. People give them for birthdays and celebrations such as Valentine's Day, Easter or Christmas.","phrases":[{"en":"common gifts","meaning":"Presents that people often give."}],"question":"Do people give chocolate as a present in your country?","html":"Yes, boxes of chocolates are <strong class=\"key-phrase\">common gifts</strong> in my country. People give them for birthdays and celebrations such as Valentine&#x27;s Day, Easter or Christmas."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-006-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-006-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-006-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-006-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Clothes for different situations","prompt":"Are clothes and clothing fashions important to you?\nWhat different clothes do you wear for different situations?\nDo you wear different styles of clothes now compared to 10 years ago?\nDo you think the clothes we wear say something about who we are?","answer":"Q: Are clothes and clothing fashions important to you?\nA: No, clothes and fashion aren&#x27;t really important to me. I tend to wear clothes that are <strong class=\"key-phrase\">comfortable and practical</strong> rather than fashionable.\n\nQ: What different clothes do you wear for different situations?\nA: Well, I have to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">dress quite formally</strong> for work, so I wear a shirt and trousers. At home I prefer to wear jeans and a T-shirt, and on special occasions I might wear a suit.\n\nQ: Do you wear different styles of clothes now compared to 10 years ago?\nA: No, not really, because I don&#x27;t follow fashion. I&#x27;ve dressed <strong class=\"key-phrase\">in a similar way</strong> for the last 10 years.\n\nQ: Do you think the clothes we wear say something about who we are?\nA: Yes, they probably do. Some people are really careful about what they wear because they want to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">be seen as</strong> stylish. Other people wear clothes that <strong class=\"key-phrase\">show wealth or status</strong>, such as clothes by famous designers.","topic":"Clothes","phrases":[{"en":"comfortable and practical","context":"Q: Are clothes and clothing fashions important to you?\nA: No, clothes and fashion aren't really important to me. I tend to wear clothes that are comfortable and practical rather than fashionable."},{"en":"dress quite formally","context":"Q: What different clothes do you wear for different situations?\nA: Well, I have to dress quite formally for work, so I wear a shirt and trousers. At home I prefer to wear jeans and a T-shirt, and on special occasions I might wear a suit."},{"en":"in a similar way","context":"Q: Do you wear different styles of clothes now compared to 10 years ago?\nA: No, not really, because I don't follow fashion. I've dressed in a similar way for the last 10 years."},{"en":"be seen as","context":"Q: Do you think the clothes we wear say something about who we are?\nA: Yes, they probably do. Some people are really careful about what they wear because they want to be seen as stylish. Other people wear clothes that show wealth or status, such as clothes by famous designers."},{"en":"show wealth or status","context":"Q: Do you think the clothes we wear say something about who we are?\nA: Yes, they probably do. Some people are really careful about what they wear because they want to be seen as stylish. Other people wear clothes that show wealth or status, such as clothes by famous designers."}],"subtype":"","summary":"Clothes","id":"speaking-part-1-008","_displayNo":"#007","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-008-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-008-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-008-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-008-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"Not really. I care more about feeling comfortable than looking fashionable. I usually choose clothes that are easy to wear and suitable for what I need to do.","phrases":[{"en":"suitable for","meaning":"Right or useful for a particular situation."}],"question":"Are clothes and clothing fashions important to you?","html":"Not really. I care more about feeling comfortable than looking fashionable. I usually choose clothes that are easy to wear and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">suitable for</strong> what I need to do."},{"text":"I wear a shirt and trousers at work because I need to look formal. At home, I prefer jeans and a T-shirt. For a special event, I might wear a suit.","phrases":[{"en":"a special event","meaning":"An important occasion that is different from an ordinary day."}],"question":"What different clothes do you wear for different situations?","html":"I wear a shirt and trousers at work because I need to look formal. At home, I prefer jeans and a T-shirt. For <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a special event</strong>, I might wear a suit."},{"text":"No, my style has stayed much the same. I don't follow fashion closely, so I have worn similar kinds of clothes for about ten years.","phrases":[{"en":"stayed much the same","meaning":"Changed very little."}],"question":"Do you wear different styles of clothes now compared to 10 years ago?","html":"No, my style has <strong class=\"key-phrase\">stayed much the same</strong>. I don&#x27;t follow fashion closely, so I have worn similar kinds of clothes for about ten years."},{"text":"Yes, clothes can tell us something about people. Some choose them to look fashionable, while others buy famous brands to show that they have money or a high social position.","phrases":[{"en":"famous brands","meaning":"Product names that many people recognise."}],"question":"Do you think the clothes we wear say something about who we are?","html":"Yes, clothes can tell us something about people. Some choose them to look fashionable, while others buy <strong class=\"key-phrase\">famous brands</strong> to show that they have money or a high social position."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-008-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-008-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-008-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-008-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Clothes you dislike, and how your style has changed","prompt":"How important are clothes and fashion to you?\nWhat kind of clothes do you dislike and why?\nHow different are the clothes you wear now from those you wore 10 years ago?\nWhat do you think the clothes we wear say about us?","answer":"Q: How important are clothes and fashion to you?\nA: Clothes matter to me mainly in terms of comfort and appropriateness. I like to look presentable, but I don&#x27;t follow every trend, because style is <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a matter of personal choice</strong>.\n\nQ: What kind of clothes do you dislike and why?\nA: I dislike clothes that are overly tight, heavily branded or difficult to care for. Even if something looks fashionable, I won&#x27;t buy it unless it&#x27;s <strong class=\"key-phrase\">comfortable enough for daily wear</strong>.\n\nQ: How different are the clothes you wear now from those you wore 10 years ago?\nA: My clothes are simpler and more practical now. Ten years ago I experimented with brighter colours, but these days I prefer neutral items that <strong class=\"key-phrase\">work in several settings</strong>.\n\nQ: What do you think the clothes we wear say about us?\nA: Clothing can suggest someone&#x27;s profession, taste or attitude to formality, but it&#x27;s not a complete picture of their character. People sometimes dress to meet expectations rather than to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">express their real personality</strong>.","topic":"Clothes","phrases":[{"en":"a matter of personal choice","context":"Q: How important are clothes and fashion to you?\nA: Clothes matter to me mainly in terms of comfort and appropriateness. I like to look presentable, but I don't follow every trend, because style is a matter of personal choice."},{"en":"comfortable enough for daily wear","context":"Q: What kind of clothes do you dislike and why?\nA: I dislike clothes that are overly tight, heavily branded or difficult to care for. Even if something looks fashionable, I won't buy it unless it's comfortable enough for daily wear."},{"en":"work in several settings","context":"Q: How different are the clothes you wear now from those you wore 10 years ago?\nA: My clothes are simpler and more practical now. Ten years ago I experimented with brighter colours, but these days I prefer neutral items that work in several settings."},{"en":"express their real personality","context":"Q: What do you think the clothes we wear say about us?\nA: Clothing can suggest someone's profession, taste or attitude to formality, but it's not a complete picture of their character. People sometimes dress to meet expectations rather than to express their real personality."}],"subtype":"Part 1","summary":"Clothes","visual":null,"id":"speaking-part-1-009","_displayNo":"#008","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-009-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-009-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-009-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-009-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"Clothes matter because I want to feel comfortable and dress properly for each situation. I like looking neat, but I don't follow every new style. People should choose what suits them.","phrases":[{"en":"what suits them","meaning":"What is right for their needs, taste or appearance."}],"question":"How important are clothes and fashion to you?","html":"Clothes matter because I want to feel comfortable and dress properly for each situation. I like looking neat, but I don&#x27;t follow every new style. People should choose <strong class=\"key-phrase\">what suits them</strong>."},{"text":"I don't like very tight clothes, large brand names or clothes that are hard to wash. Even if they look fashionable, I won't buy them unless they feel comfortable for daily use.","phrases":[{"en":"daily use","meaning":"Regular use in normal everyday situations."}],"question":"What kind of clothes do you dislike and why?","html":"I don&#x27;t like very tight clothes, large brand names or clothes that are hard to wash. Even if they look fashionable, I won&#x27;t buy them unless they feel comfortable for <strong class=\"key-phrase\">daily use</strong>."},{"text":"My clothes are simpler now. Ten years ago, I tried brighter colours, but these days I prefer plain colours that I can wear in different places and situations.","phrases":[{"en":"these days","meaning":"During the present period of your life."}],"question":"How different are the clothes you wear now from those you wore 10 years ago?","html":"My clothes are simpler now. Ten years ago, I tried brighter colours, but <strong class=\"key-phrase\">these days</strong> I prefer plain colours that I can wear in different places and situations."},{"text":"Clothes may suggest someone's job or taste, but they do not tell us everything about their character. Sometimes people dress a certain way because others expect them to.","phrases":[{"en":"a certain way","meaning":"A particular manner or style."}],"question":"What do you think the clothes we wear say about us?","html":"Clothes may suggest someone&#x27;s job or taste, but they do not tell us everything about their character. Sometimes people dress <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a certain way</strong> because others expect them to."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-009-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-009-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-009-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-009-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"What people in your country wear","prompt":"What types of clothes do you like to wear?\nWhat kind of clothes do people in your country usually wear?\nHow important is fashion to you?\nWhat kind of clothes do you dislike?","answer":"Q: What types of clothes do you like to wear?\nA: I usually wear simple shirts, trousers and comfortable shoes. I prefer well-made basics because they&#x27;re easy to combine and don&#x27;t <strong class=\"key-phrase\">go out of style quickly</strong>.\n\nQ: What kind of clothes do people in your country usually wear?\nA: Most people wear casual Western-style clothes in daily life, while traditional dress is reserved for weddings, festivals and formal occasions. Office workers tend to choose smart clothes that <strong class=\"key-phrase\">strike a balance between</strong> comfort and professionalism.\n\nQ: How important is fashion to you?\nA: Fashion doesn&#x27;t play a big part in my life. I want to look neat and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">appropriate for the occasion</strong>, but comfort, durability and fit matter more to me than following every seasonal trend.\n\nQ: What kind of clothes do you dislike?\nA: I avoid clothes that are uncomfortable, covered in large logos or impractical for the weather. I prefer an <strong class=\"key-phrase\">understated appearance</strong> and clothes I can wear again and again.","topic":"Clothes","phrases":[{"en":"go out of style quickly","context":"Q: What types of clothes do you like to wear?\nA: I usually wear simple shirts, trousers and comfortable shoes. I prefer well-made basics because they're easy to combine and don't go out of style quickly."},{"en":"strike a balance between","context":"Q: What kind of clothes do people in your country usually wear?\nA: Most people wear casual Western-style clothes in daily life, while traditional dress is reserved for weddings, festivals and formal occasions. Office workers tend to choose smart clothes that strike a balance between comfort and professionalism."},{"en":"appropriate for the occasion","context":"Q: How important is fashion to you?\nA: Fashion doesn't play a big part in my life. I want to look neat and appropriate for the occasion, but comfort, durability and fit matter more to me than following every seasonal trend."},{"en":"understated appearance","context":"Q: What kind of clothes do you dislike?\nA: I avoid clothes that are uncomfortable, covered in large logos or impractical for the weather. I prefer an understated appearance and clothes I can wear again and again."}],"subtype":"Part 1","summary":"Clothes","visual":null,"id":"speaking-part-1-010","_displayNo":"#009","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-010-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-010-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-010-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-010-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"I like simple shirts, trousers and comfortable shoes. I choose good-quality basic clothes because they are easy to wear together and stay useful even when fashion changes.","phrases":[{"en":"good-quality","meaning":"Made well and likely to last."}],"question":"What types of clothes do you like to wear?","html":"I like simple shirts, trousers and comfortable shoes. I choose <strong class=\"key-phrase\">good-quality</strong> basic clothes because they are easy to wear together and stay useful even when fashion changes."},{"text":"People usually wear casual Western-style clothes every day. Traditional clothes are more common at weddings and festivals. Office workers often choose clothes that look smart but still feel comfortable.","phrases":[{"en":"look smart","meaning":"Look neat and properly dressed."}],"question":"What kind of clothes do people in your country usually wear?","html":"People usually wear casual Western-style clothes every day. Traditional clothes are more common at weddings and festivals. Office workers often choose clothes that <strong class=\"key-phrase\">look smart</strong> but still feel comfortable."},{"text":"Fashion isn't very important to me. I want to look tidy and dress well for the occasion, but I care more about comfort, fit and how long clothes last.","phrases":[{"en":"for the occasion","meaning":"In a way that suits a particular event."}],"question":"How important is fashion to you?","html":"Fashion isn&#x27;t very important to me. I want to look tidy and dress well <strong class=\"key-phrase\">for the occasion</strong>, but I care more about comfort, fit and how long clothes last."},{"text":"I dislike uncomfortable clothes, big logos and clothes that do not suit the weather. I prefer a simple look and things that I can wear many times.","phrases":[{"en":"suit the weather","meaning":"Be appropriate for how hot, cold or wet it is."}],"question":"What kind of clothes do you dislike?","html":"I dislike uncomfortable clothes, big logos and clothes that do not <strong class=\"key-phrase\">suit the weather</strong>. I prefer a simple look and things that I can wear many times."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-010-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-010-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-010-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-010-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Collecting things as a hobby","prompt":"Have you ever collected anything as a hobby?\nWhat kinds of thing do people often like collecting?\nWhy do you think people collect certain objects?\nIs there anything that you would like to collect in the future?","answer":"Q: Have you ever collected anything as a hobby?\nA: Yes. When I was younger I <strong class=\"key-phrase\">used to collect</strong> keyrings. I remember that my favourite was a Lego man keyring that someone bought me as a present.\n\nQ: What kinds of thing do people often like collecting?\nA: Some people collect cheap items like stamps, keyrings or toys. Others collect <strong class=\"key-phrase\">expensive antiques</strong>, watches, jewellery or even cars.\n\nQ: Why do you think people collect certain objects?\nA: Maybe they like the <strong class=\"key-phrase\">constant search</strong> for a new item, or they want to remember past experiences. Others might like the feeling of organising and presenting what they own.\n\nQ: Is there anything that you would like to collect in the future?\nA: Yes. If I could afford it, I&#x27;d love to have <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a collection of guitars</strong> in different colours, shapes and sizes!","topic":"Collecting","phrases":[{"en":"used to collect","context":"Q: Have you ever collected anything as a hobby?\nA: Yes. When I was younger I used to collect keyrings. I remember that my favourite was a Lego man keyring that someone bought me as a present."},{"en":"expensive antiques","context":"Q: What kinds of thing do people often like collecting?\nA: Some people collect cheap items like stamps, keyrings or toys. Others collect expensive antiques, watches, jewellery or even cars."},{"en":"constant search","context":"Q: Why do you think people collect certain objects?\nA: Maybe they like the constant search for a new item, or they want to remember past experiences. Others might like the feeling of organising and presenting what they own."},{"en":"a collection of guitars","context":"Q: Is there anything that you would like to collect in the future?\nA: Yes. If I could afford it, I'd love to have a collection of guitars in different colours, shapes and sizes!"}],"subtype":"","summary":"Collecting","id":"speaking-part-1-011","_displayNo":"#010","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-011-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-011-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-011-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-011-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"Yes, I collected keyrings when I was younger. My favourite was a little Lego man that someone gave me. I remember liking it more than the others in my collection.","phrases":[{"en":"my collection","meaning":"The group of similar objects I have gathered."}],"question":"Have you ever collected anything as a hobby?","html":"Yes, I collected keyrings when I was younger. My favourite was a little Lego man that someone gave me. I remember liking it more than the others in <strong class=\"key-phrase\">my collection</strong>."},{"text":"People collect many things, from inexpensive stamps, keyrings and toys to valuable old objects. Some also collect watches, jewellery or even cars if they have enough money.","phrases":[{"en":"valuable","meaning":"Worth a lot of money or important to someone."}],"question":"What kinds of thing do people often like collecting?","html":"People collect many things, from inexpensive stamps, keyrings and toys to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">valuable</strong> old objects. Some also collect watches, jewellery or even cars if they have enough money."},{"text":"Some people enjoy looking for the next object in their collection. Others collect things to remember experiences, or because they like arranging their objects and showing them to people.","phrases":[{"en":"showing them to people","meaning":"Letting other people see them."}],"question":"Why do you think people collect certain objects?","html":"Some people enjoy looking for the next object in their collection. Others collect things to remember experiences, or because they like arranging their objects and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">showing them to people</strong>."},{"text":"Yes, I'd like to collect guitars if I had enough money. It would be lovely to own several guitars with different colours, shapes and sizes.","phrases":[{"en":"if I had enough money","meaning":"On the condition that I could afford it."}],"question":"Is there anything that you would like to collect in the future?","html":"Yes, I&#x27;d like to collect guitars <strong class=\"key-phrase\">if I had enough money</strong>. It would be lovely to own several guitars with different colours, shapes and sizes."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-011-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-011-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-011-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-011-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Colours you like and how they affect mood","prompt":"What colours do you like?\nDo colours affect your mood?\nDo you wear bright clothes?","answer":"Q: What colours do you like?\nA: I&#x27;m particularly fond of blue because it feels calm and clean. It also works well in clothing and interior design without <strong class=\"key-phrase\">drawing too much attention</strong>.\n\nQ: Do colours affect your mood?\nA: Yes, <strong class=\"key-phrase\">to some extent</strong>. Soft, natural colours help me relax, but extremely bright colours can feel tiring when they cover a large space. The effect is subtle but <strong class=\"key-phrase\">noticeable over time</strong>.\n\nQ: Do you wear bright clothes?\nA: Only occasionally. I may wear one bright item, but I usually combine it with neutral colours so that the overall look remains <strong class=\"key-phrase\">simple and balanced</strong>.","topic":"Colours","phrases":[{"en":"drawing too much attention","context":"Q: What colours do you like?\nA: I'm particularly fond of blue because it feels calm and clean. It also works well in clothing and interior design without drawing too much attention."},{"en":"to some extent","context":"Q: Do colours affect your mood?\nA: Yes, to some extent. Soft, natural colours help me relax, but extremely bright colours can feel tiring when they cover a large space. The effect is subtle but noticeable over time."},{"en":"noticeable over time","context":"Q: Do colours affect your mood?\nA: Yes, to some extent. Soft, natural colours help me relax, but extremely bright colours can feel tiring when they cover a large space. The effect is subtle but noticeable over time."},{"en":"simple and balanced","context":"Q: Do you wear bright clothes?\nA: Only occasionally. I may wear one bright item, but I usually combine it with neutral colours so that the overall look remains simple and balanced."}],"subtype":"","summary":"Colours","id":"speaking-part-1-012","_displayNo":"#011","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-012-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-012-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-012-q03.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"I especially like blue because it makes me think of calm, clean places. It also looks good in clothes and rooms without being too bright or noticeable.","phrases":[{"en":"looks good","meaning":"Has an attractive appearance."}],"question":"What colours do you like?","html":"I especially like blue because it makes me think of calm, clean places. It also <strong class=\"key-phrase\">looks good</strong> in clothes and rooms without being too bright or noticeable."},{"text":"Yes, a little. Soft, natural colours help me feel relaxed, but a large area of very bright colour can make me tired. The effect is small, but I notice it over time.","phrases":[{"en":"over time","meaning":"Gradually, as time passes."}],"question":"Do colours affect your mood?","html":"Yes, a little. Soft, natural colours help me feel relaxed, but a large area of very bright colour can make me tired. The effect is small, but I notice it <strong class=\"key-phrase\">over time</strong>."},{"text":"Sometimes, but not very often. I might wear one bright piece of clothing with plain colours. That way, my clothes still look simple and go well together.","phrases":[{"en":"go well together","meaning":"Look or work nicely when combined."}],"question":"Do you wear bright clothes?","html":"Sometimes, but not very often. I might wear one bright piece of clothing with plain colours. That way, my clothes still look simple and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">go well together</strong>."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-012-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-012-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-012-q03.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Your favourite colour, then and now","prompt":"What is your favourite colour and why?\nDo you like the same colours now as you did when you were younger and why?\nWhat can you learn about people from the colours they like?\nDo colours have special meaning in your culture?","answer":"Q: What is your favourite colour and why?\nA: Navy blue is my favourite colour because it looks calm and professional, and it&#x27;s <strong class=\"key-phrase\">easy to combine with</strong> other colours. I also associate it with the sea and open space.\n\nQ: Do you like the same colours now as you did when you were younger and why?\nA: Not entirely. As a child I preferred bright red and orange, but I now go for blue, grey and dark green. My taste has become <strong class=\"key-phrase\">more understated</strong> as I&#x27;ve grown older.\n\nQ: What can you learn about people from the colours they like?\nA: Colour preferences might give a small clue about whether someone likes bold or quieter styles, but I wouldn&#x27;t read too much into it. Culture, fashion and practical needs can influence choices just as much as personality, so it&#x27;s <strong class=\"key-phrase\">not a reliable test</strong>.\n\nQ: Do colours have special meaning in your culture?\nA: Yes, definitely. Red&#x27;s often linked to luck and celebrations, while white can be linked to mourning, so a colour&#x27;s meaning really can <strong class=\"key-phrase\">depend on the culture</strong>.","topic":"Colours","phrases":[{"en":"easy to combine with","context":"Q: What is your favourite colour and why?\nA: Navy blue is my favourite colour because it looks calm and professional, and it's easy to combine with other colours. I also associate it with the sea and open space."},{"en":"more understated","context":"Q: Do you like the same colours now as you did when you were younger and why?\nA: Not entirely. As a child I preferred bright red and orange, but I now go for blue, grey and dark green. My taste has become more understated as I've grown older."},{"en":"not a reliable test","context":"Q: What can you learn about people from the colours they like?\nA: Colour preferences might give a small clue about whether someone likes bold or quieter styles, but I wouldn't read too much into it. Culture, fashion and practical needs can influence choices just as much as personality, so it's not a reliable test."},{"en":"depend on the culture","context":"Q: Do colours have special meaning in your culture?\nA: Yes, definitely. Red's often linked to luck and celebrations, while white can be linked to mourning, so a colour's meaning really can depend on the culture."}],"subtype":"Part 1","summary":"Colours","visual":null,"id":"speaking-part-1-013","_displayNo":"#012","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-013-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-013-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-013-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-013-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"My favourite colour is navy blue because it looks calm and smart. It matches many other colours, and it also makes me think of the sea and wide, open places.","phrases":[{"en":"matches","meaning":"Looks good together with something else."}],"question":"What is your favourite colour and why?","html":"My favourite colour is navy blue because it looks calm and smart. It <strong class=\"key-phrase\">matches</strong> many other colours, and it also makes me think of the sea and wide, open places."},{"text":"Not exactly. I liked bright red and orange as a child. Now I prefer blue, grey and dark green because I enjoy quieter, less noticeable colours.","phrases":[{"en":"less noticeable","meaning":"Less easy to see or attract attention."}],"question":"Do you like the same colours now as you did when you were younger and why?","html":"Not exactly. I liked bright red and orange as a child. Now I prefer blue, grey and dark green because I enjoy quieter, <strong class=\"key-phrase\">less noticeable</strong> colours."},{"text":"Colours may show whether someone likes a bright or quiet style, but they do not tell us much about personality. Culture, fashion and practical reasons also affect what people choose.","phrases":[{"en":"practical reasons","meaning":"Reasons connected with usefulness or everyday needs."}],"question":"What can you learn about people from the colours they like?","html":"Colours may show whether someone likes a bright or quiet style, but they do not tell us much about personality. Culture, fashion and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">practical reasons</strong> also affect what people choose."},{"text":"Yes. In my culture, red is often used for luck and celebrations, while white can be connected with death and sadness. The same colour can mean different things in different cultures.","phrases":[{"en":"connected with","meaning":"Related to something."}],"question":"Do colours have special meaning in your culture?","html":"Yes. In my culture, red is often used for luck and celebrations, while white can be <strong class=\"key-phrase\">connected with</strong> death and sadness. The same colour can mean different things in different cultures."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-013-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-013-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-013-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-013-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Keeping in touch: phone, email and letters","prompt":"How do you usually keep in touch with members of your family?\nDo you prefer to speak to people by phone or by writing emails?\nDo you ever write letters by hand?\nIs there anything you dislike about mobile phones?","answer":"Q: How do you usually keep in touch with members of your family?\nA: I mostly <strong class=\"key-phrase\">keep in touch with</strong> my family by phone, and I&#x27;ve started using the Internet to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">make video calls</strong>. I also try to visit members of my family in person as often as I can.\n\nQ: Do you prefer to speak to people by phone or by writing emails?\nA: It depends on the situation. I use email and text messages to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">communicate with friends</strong>, but my parents prefer it if I phone them.\n\nQ: Do you ever write letters by hand?\nA: No, I don&#x27;t <strong class=\"key-phrase\">write letters by hand</strong> because it&#x27;s so much easier to send an email that will arrive immediately.\n\nQ: Is there anything you dislike about mobile phones?\nA: Well, I really don&#x27;t like it when someone&#x27;s phone <strong class=\"key-phrase\">goes off</strong> in the cinema or during a lesson, and I&#x27;m not keen on overhearing other people&#x27;s conversations in public either.","topic":"Communication","phrases":[{"en":"keep in touch with","context":"Q: How do you usually keep in touch with members of your family?\nA: I mostly keep in touch with my family by phone, and I've started using the Internet to make video calls. I also try to visit members of my family in person as often as I can."},{"en":"make video calls","context":"Q: How do you usually keep in touch with members of your family?\nA: I mostly keep in touch with my family by phone, and I've started using the Internet to make video calls. I also try to visit members of my family in person as often as I can."},{"en":"communicate with friends","context":"Q: Do you prefer to speak to people by phone or by writing emails?\nA: It depends on the situation. I use email and text messages to communicate with friends, but my parents prefer it if I phone them."},{"en":"write letters by hand","context":"Q: Do you ever write letters by hand?\nA: No, I don't write letters by hand because it's so much easier to send an email that will arrive immediately."},{"en":"goes off","context":"Q: Is there anything you dislike about mobile phones?\nA: Well, I really don't like it when someone's phone goes off in the cinema or during a lesson, and I'm not keen on overhearing other people's conversations in public either."}],"subtype":"","summary":"Communication","id":"speaking-part-1-014","_displayNo":"#013","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-014-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-014-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-014-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-014-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"I usually speak to my family on the phone, and I have also started making video calls. I try to visit them whenever I can because meeting in person is important too.","phrases":[{"en":"in person","meaning":"Being physically together rather than using a phone or computer."}],"question":"How do you usually keep in touch with members of your family?","html":"I usually speak to my family on the phone, and I have also started making video calls. I try to visit them whenever I can because meeting <strong class=\"key-phrase\">in person</strong> is important too."},{"text":"It depends on who I'm speaking to. I often email or text my friends, but my parents prefer a phone call, so I usually call them.","phrases":[{"en":"depends on","meaning":"Is decided or affected by something."}],"question":"Do you prefer to speak to people by phone or by writing emails?","html":"It <strong class=\"key-phrase\">depends on</strong> who I&#x27;m speaking to. I often email or text my friends, but my parents prefer a phone call, so I usually call them."},{"text":"No, I don't usually write letters by hand. Sending an email is much easier, and the other person receives it straight away, so I find it more useful.","phrases":[{"en":"straight away","meaning":"Immediately, without waiting."}],"question":"Do you ever write letters by hand?","html":"No, I don&#x27;t usually write letters by hand. Sending an email is much easier, and the other person receives it <strong class=\"key-phrase\">straight away</strong>, so I find it more useful."},{"text":"I dislike phones ringing during films or lessons because they disturb other people. I also don't enjoy hearing someone's private conversation when they talk loudly on their phone in public.","phrases":[{"en":"disturb","meaning":"Interrupt someone or stop them feeling comfortable or focused."}],"question":"Is there anything you dislike about mobile phones?","html":"I dislike phones ringing during films or lessons because they <strong class=\"key-phrase\">disturb</strong> other people. I also don&#x27;t enjoy hearing someone&#x27;s private conversation when they talk loudly on their phone in public."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-014-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-014-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-014-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-014-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Using computers and their effect on health","prompt":"When did you first use a computer?\nDo you think computers are bad for your health?\nWhich computer software do you use most?\nWhat did you mainly use your first computer for?","answer":"Q: When did you first use a computer?\nA: I first used a desktop computer at primary school. We learned basic typing and simple drawing programs, and I remember being fascinated by how quickly the machine <strong class=\"key-phrase\">responded to instructions</strong>.\n\nQ: Do you think computers are bad for your health?\nA: They can be harmful if people sit for hours with poor posture or stare at the screen without breaks. The problem usually isn&#x27;t the computer itself, but <strong class=\"key-phrase\">the way it&#x27;s used</strong>.\n\nQ: Which computer software do you use most?\nA: I use web browsers, word-processing software and spreadsheets most often. They support almost every part of my work, from lesson preparation to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">organising information efficiently</strong>.\n\nQ: What did you mainly use your first computer for?\nA: My first computer was mainly for school assignments, basic research and educational games. Over time it became an essential tool for communication and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">independent learning</strong>.","topic":"Computers","phrases":[{"en":"responded to instructions","context":"Q: When did you first use a computer?\nA: I first used a desktop computer at primary school. We learned basic typing and simple drawing programs, and I remember being fascinated by how quickly the machine responded to instructions."},{"en":"the way it's used","context":"Q: Do you think computers are bad for your health?\nA: They can be harmful if people sit for hours with poor posture or stare at the screen without breaks. The problem usually isn't the computer itself, but the way it's used."},{"en":"organising information efficiently","context":"Q: Which computer software do you use most?\nA: I use web browsers, word-processing software and spreadsheets most often. They support almost every part of my work, from lesson preparation to organising information efficiently."},{"en":"independent learning","context":"Q: What did you mainly use your first computer for?\nA: My first computer was mainly for school assignments, basic research and educational games. Over time it became an essential tool for communication and independent learning."}],"subtype":"Part 1","summary":"Computer","visual":null,"id":"speaking-part-1-015","_displayNo":"#014","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-015-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-015-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-015-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-015-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"I first used a desktop computer at primary school. We practised typing and used simple drawing programs. I was amazed that it could do things so quickly when we gave it instructions.","phrases":[{"en":"amazed","meaning":"Very surprised by something impressive."}],"question":"When did you first use a computer?","html":"I first used a desktop computer at primary school. We practised typing and used simple drawing programs. I was <strong class=\"key-phrase\">amazed</strong> that it could do things so quickly when we gave it instructions."},{"text":"They can be bad for your health if you sit badly or use them for hours without a break. I think the main issue is how we use them.","phrases":[{"en":"without a break","meaning":"Continuously, without stopping to rest."}],"question":"Do you think computers are bad for your health?","html":"They can be bad for your health if you sit badly or use them for hours <strong class=\"key-phrase\">without a break</strong>. I think the main issue is how we use them."},{"text":"I mainly use internet browsers, programs for writing documents and spreadsheets. They help with most of my work, including preparing lessons and keeping information organised.","phrases":[{"en":"keeping information organised","meaning":"Arranging facts or records so they are easy to use."}],"question":"Which computer software do you use most?","html":"I mainly use internet browsers, programs for writing documents and spreadsheets. They help with most of my work, including preparing lessons and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">keeping information organised</strong>."},{"text":"I mainly used it for homework, finding information and educational games. Later, it became important for talking to people and learning new things on my own.","phrases":[{"en":"on my own","meaning":"Without help from other people."}],"question":"What did you mainly use your first computer for?","html":"I mainly used it for homework, finding information and educational games. Later, it became important for talking to people and learning new things <strong class=\"key-phrase\">on my own</strong>."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-015-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-015-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-015-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-015-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Cooking at home and learning to cook","prompt":"Do you like cooking?\nWho did the cooking in your family when you were a child?\nDo you think that it's important to know how to cook well?\nDo you think that children should be taught cookery at school?","answer":"Q: Do you like cooking?\nA: Sometimes. I like <strong class=\"key-phrase\">preparing a special meal</strong> for family or friends who visit, but everyday cooking&#x27;s <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a bit of a chore</strong> — it has to be done, but it&#x27;s not really fun.\n\nQ: Who did the cooking in your family when you were a child?\nA: My mother almost always did the cooking when I was young. I don&#x27;t think she trusted my father to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">make a nice meal</strong>.\n\nQ: Do you think that it&#x27;s important to know how to cook well?\nA: I&#x27;m not sure whether it&#x27;s important to cook well, but I do think that everyone should <strong class=\"key-phrase\">know the basics</strong>. It definitely isn&#x27;t healthy to rely on pre-prepared meals or fast food.\n\nQ: Do you think that children should be taught cookery at school?\nA: Yes, that&#x27;s probably a good idea. If children learned to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">cook from scratch</strong> — even just a few basic, healthy meals — that would definitely be useful for later in life.","topic":"Cooking","phrases":[{"en":"preparing a special meal","context":"Q: Do you like cooking?\nA: Sometimes. I like preparing a special meal for family or friends who visit, but everyday cooking's a bit of a chore — it has to be done, but it's not really fun."},{"en":"a bit of a chore","context":"Q: Do you like cooking?\nA: Sometimes. I like preparing a special meal for family or friends who visit, but everyday cooking's a bit of a chore — it has to be done, but it's not really fun."},{"en":"make a nice meal","context":"Q: Who did the cooking in your family when you were a child?\nA: My mother almost always did the cooking when I was young. I don't think she trusted my father to make a nice meal."},{"en":"know the basics","context":"Q: Do you think that it's important to know how to cook well?\nA: I'm not sure whether it's important to cook well, but I do think that everyone should know the basics. It definitely isn't healthy to rely on pre-prepared meals or fast food."},{"en":"cook from scratch","context":"Q: Do you think that children should be taught cookery at school?\nA: Yes, that's probably a good idea. If children learned to cook from scratch — even just a few basic, healthy meals — that would definitely be useful for later in life."}],"subtype":"","summary":"Cooking","id":"speaking-part-1-016","_displayNo":"#015","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-016-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-016-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-016-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-016-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"Sometimes. I enjoy making a special meal when family or friends visit. However, cooking every day feels more like a job I have to do than something fun.","phrases":[{"en":"have to do","meaning":"Need to do because it is necessary."}],"question":"Do you like cooking?","html":"Sometimes. I enjoy making a special meal when family or friends visit. However, cooking every day feels more like a job I <strong class=\"key-phrase\">have to do</strong> than something fun."},{"text":"My mother did most of the cooking when I was a child. I don't think she believed my father could prepare a good meal, so she usually did it herself.","phrases":[{"en":"most of","meaning":"The largest part of something."}],"question":"Who did the cooking in your family when you were a child?","html":"My mother did <strong class=\"key-phrase\">most of</strong> the cooking when I was a child. I don&#x27;t think she believed my father could prepare a good meal, so she usually did it herself."},{"text":"I think everyone should be able to cook a few simple meals, even if they are not excellent cooks. Eating ready-made meals or fast food all the time is not healthy.","phrases":[{"en":"ready-made meals","meaning":"Meals prepared in advance that usually only need heating."}],"question":"Do you think that it's important to know how to cook well?","html":"I think everyone should be able to cook a few simple meals, even if they are not excellent cooks. Eating <strong class=\"key-phrase\">ready-made meals</strong> or fast food all the time is not healthy."},{"text":"Yes, I think that would be useful. Children could learn to make a few simple, healthy meals using basic ingredients. Those skills would help them when they are older.","phrases":[{"en":"basic ingredients","meaning":"The main foods used to prepare a dish."}],"question":"Do you think that children should be taught cookery at school?","html":"Yes, I think that would be useful. Children could learn to make a few simple, healthy meals using <strong class=\"key-phrase\">basic ingredients</strong>. Those skills would help them when they are older."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-016-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-016-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-016-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-016-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"A typical weekday and a typical weekend","prompt":"What would you like to change in your daily routine?\nAre all your days the same?\nTell me about a typical weekday and a typical weekend.\nWhat is the balance of work/ study and free time in your normal days?","answer":"Q: What would you like to change in your daily routine?\nA: I&#x27;d like to spend less time looking at screens in the evening. Reading or going for a short walk instead would help me <strong class=\"key-phrase\">wind down properly</strong> before bed.\n\nQ: Are all your days the same?\nA: Weekdays follow a fairly stable pattern, but weekends are much more flexible. I still keep a few fixed habits, such as exercise and meal times, because they <strong class=\"key-phrase\">give my day structure</strong>.\n\nQ: Tell me about a typical weekday and a typical weekend.\nA: On weekdays I work, exercise and prepare for the following day. At weekends I sleep a little later, meet friends or handle personal errands, so the pace is <strong class=\"key-phrase\">far less demanding</strong>.\n\nQ: What is the balance of work/ study and free time in your normal days?\nA: Work takes up most of my weekdays, but I protect time for exercise, meals and family. The balance isn&#x27;t perfect, but I <strong class=\"key-phrase\">make a conscious effort</strong> to maintain <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a sustainable routine</strong>.","topic":"Daily Routine","phrases":[{"en":"wind down properly","context":"Q: What would you like to change in your daily routine?\nA: I'd like to spend less time looking at screens in the evening. Reading or going for a short walk instead would help me wind down properly before bed."},{"en":"give my day structure","context":"Q: Are all your days the same?\nA: Weekdays follow a fairly stable pattern, but weekends are much more flexible. I still keep a few fixed habits, such as exercise and meal times, because they give my day structure."},{"en":"far less demanding","context":"Q: Tell me about a typical weekday and a typical weekend.\nA: On weekdays I work, exercise and prepare for the following day. At weekends I sleep a little later, meet friends or handle personal errands, so the pace is far less demanding."},{"en":"make a conscious effort","context":"Q: What is the balance of work/ study and free time in your normal days?\nA: Work takes up most of my weekdays, but I protect time for exercise, meals and family. The balance isn't perfect, but I make a conscious effort to maintain a sustainable routine."},{"en":"a sustainable routine","context":"Q: What is the balance of work/ study and free time in your normal days?\nA: Work takes up most of my weekdays, but I protect time for exercise, meals and family. The balance isn't perfect, but I make a conscious effort to maintain a sustainable routine."}],"subtype":"Part 1","summary":"Daily Routine","visual":null,"id":"speaking-part-1-017","_displayNo":"#016","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-017-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-017-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-017-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-017-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"I'd like to use screens less in the evening. I could read or take a short walk instead, which would help me relax before going to bed.","phrases":[{"en":"relax","meaning":"Become calmer and less worried or tense."}],"question":"What would you like to change in your daily routine?","html":"I&#x27;d like to use screens less in the evening. I could read or take a short walk instead, which would help me <strong class=\"key-phrase\">relax</strong> before going to bed."},{"text":"No. My weekdays are quite similar, but I have more freedom at weekends. I still keep regular exercise and meal times because they help me organise my day.","phrases":[{"en":"regular","meaning":"Happening at similar times or in a usual pattern."}],"question":"Are all your days the same?","html":"No. My weekdays are quite similar, but I have more freedom at weekends. I still keep <strong class=\"key-phrase\">regular</strong> exercise and meal times because they help me organise my day."},{"text":"On weekdays, I work, exercise and get ready for the next day. At weekends, I get up a little later, meet friends or do personal tasks, so life feels less busy.","phrases":[{"en":"get ready","meaning":"Prepare yourself for something."}],"question":"Tell me about a typical weekday and a typical weekend.","html":"On weekdays, I work, exercise and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">get ready</strong> for the next day. At weekends, I get up a little later, meet friends or do personal tasks, so life feels less busy."},{"text":"Work fills most of my weekdays, but I still make time for exercise, meals and family. The balance could be better, although I try to keep a routine I can manage.","phrases":[{"en":"make time for","meaning":"Arrange to have enough time to do something."}],"question":"What is the balance of work/ study and free time in your normal days?","html":"Work fills most of my weekdays, but I still <strong class=\"key-phrase\">make time for</strong> exercise, meals and family. The balance could be better, although I try to keep a routine I can manage."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-017-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-017-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-017-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-017-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Dancing, and whether traditional dance will last","prompt":"Do you like dancing?\nHas anyone ever taught you to dance?\nDo you think that traditional dancing will be popular in the future?","answer":"Q: Do you like dancing?\nA: No, I don&#x27;t like dancing. I&#x27;m not a big music fan, and dancing just makes me feel <strong class=\"key-phrase\">uncomfortable and self-conscious</strong>.\n\nQ: Has anyone ever taught you to dance?\nA: No, I&#x27;ve never been interested in learning to dance, so I&#x27;ve never <strong class=\"key-phrase\">taken any lessons</strong> or asked anyone to show me how to do it.\n\nQ: Do you think that traditional dancing will be popular in the future?\nA: I&#x27;m afraid I have no idea, because I don&#x27;t <strong class=\"key-phrase\">follow what&#x27;s happening</strong> in the dancing world! I suppose it will always <strong class=\"key-phrase\">be popular with</strong> some people.","topic":"Dancing","phrases":[{"en":"uncomfortable and self-conscious","context":"Q: Do you like dancing?\nA: No, I don't like dancing. I'm not a big music fan, and dancing just makes me feel uncomfortable and self-conscious."},{"en":"taken any lessons","context":"Q: Has anyone ever taught you to dance?\nA: No, I've never been interested in learning to dance, so I've never taken any lessons or asked anyone to show me how to do it."},{"en":"follow what's happening","context":"Q: Do you think that traditional dancing will be popular in the future?\nA: I'm afraid I have no idea, because I don't follow what's happening in the dancing world! I suppose it will always be popular with some people."},{"en":"be popular with","context":"Q: Do you think that traditional dancing will be popular in the future?\nA: I'm afraid I have no idea, because I don't follow what's happening in the dancing world! I suppose it will always be popular with some people."}],"subtype":"","summary":"Dancing","id":"speaking-part-1-018","_displayNo":"#017","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-018-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-018-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-018-q03.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"No, I don't really enjoy dancing. I'm not very interested in music, and I feel uncomfortable when I dance because I worry about how I look.","phrases":[{"en":"worry about","meaning":"Feel nervous or concerned about something."}],"question":"Do you like dancing?","html":"No, I don&#x27;t really enjoy dancing. I&#x27;m not very interested in music, and I feel uncomfortable when I dance because I <strong class=\"key-phrase\">worry about</strong> how I look."},{"text":"No, nobody has taught me. I've never really wanted to learn, so I haven't taken classes or asked anyone to teach me any dance steps.","phrases":[{"en":"dance steps","meaning":"The movements people make when dancing."}],"question":"Has anyone ever taught you to dance?","html":"No, nobody has taught me. I&#x27;ve never really wanted to learn, so I haven&#x27;t taken classes or asked anyone to teach me any <strong class=\"key-phrase\">dance steps</strong>."},{"text":"I'm not sure because I don't know much about dance. However, I think some people will continue to enjoy traditional dancing, even if it isn't popular with everyone.","phrases":[{"en":"continue to","meaning":"Keep doing something."}],"question":"Do you think that traditional dancing will be popular in the future?","html":"I&#x27;m not sure because I don&#x27;t know much about dance. However, I think some people will <strong class=\"key-phrase\">continue to</strong> enjoy traditional dancing, even if it isn&#x27;t popular with everyone."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-018-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-018-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-018-q03.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Learning to dance and traditional dance","prompt":"Do you enjoy dancing and why?\nHas anyone ever taught you to dance?\nTell me about a traditional dance in your country.\nDo you think that traditional dancing will be popular in the future?","answer":"Q: Do you enjoy dancing and why?\nA: I enjoy dancing at social events, although I wouldn&#x27;t call myself skilled. It&#x27;s enjoyable because the atmosphere is relaxed and people are more concerned with having fun than <strong class=\"key-phrase\">performing perfectly</strong>.\n\nQ: Has anyone ever taught you to dance?\nA: No one has taught me formally. I&#x27;ve picked up a few basic steps by watching friends and copying them, so my dancing is <strong class=\"key-phrase\">entirely informal</strong>.\n\nQ: Tell me about a traditional dance in your country.\nA: Vietnam has several traditional dances linked to festivals and regional cultures. They often use coordinated movements, colourful costumes and music to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">tell a cultural story</strong>.\n\nQ: Do you think that traditional dancing will be popular in the future?\nA: I think it&#x27;ll survive, especially if schools and cultural groups present it in an engaging way. It may not become an everyday hobby, but it remains <strong class=\"key-phrase\">worth preserving</strong>.","topic":"Dancing","phrases":[{"en":"performing perfectly","context":"Q: Do you enjoy dancing and why?\nA: I enjoy dancing at social events, although I wouldn't call myself skilled. It's enjoyable because the atmosphere is relaxed and people are more concerned with having fun than performing perfectly."},{"en":"entirely informal","context":"Q: Has anyone ever taught you to dance?\nA: No one has taught me formally. I've picked up a few basic steps by watching friends and copying them, so my dancing is entirely informal."},{"en":"tell a cultural story","context":"Q: Tell me about a traditional dance in your country.\nA: Vietnam has several traditional dances linked to festivals and regional cultures. They often use coordinated movements, colourful costumes and music to tell a cultural story."},{"en":"worth preserving","context":"Q: Do you think that traditional dancing will be popular in the future?\nA: I think it'll survive, especially if schools and cultural groups present it in an engaging way. It may not become an everyday hobby, but it remains worth preserving."}],"subtype":"Part 1","summary":"Dancing","visual":null,"id":"speaking-part-1-019","_displayNo":"#018","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-019-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-019-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-019-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-019-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"Yes, I enjoy dancing at social events, even though I'm not very good at it. People are usually relaxed and want to have fun rather than dance perfectly.","phrases":[{"en":"have fun","meaning":"Enjoy yourself."}],"question":"Do you enjoy dancing and why?","html":"Yes, I enjoy dancing at social events, even though I&#x27;m not very good at it. People are usually relaxed and want to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">have fun</strong> rather than dance perfectly."},{"text":"I've never had proper dance lessons. I have learned a few easy steps by watching my friends and copying them, so I only dance in a casual way.","phrases":[{"en":"copying them","meaning":"Doing the same actions as other people."}],"question":"Has anyone ever taught you to dance?","html":"I&#x27;ve never had proper dance lessons. I have learned a few easy steps by watching my friends and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">copying them</strong>, so I only dance in a casual way."},{"text":"There are several traditional dances in Vietnam, often performed during festivals. Dancers move together, wear colourful clothes and use music and movement to tell stories about local culture.","phrases":[{"en":"local culture","meaning":"The traditions and way of life of people in a particular area."}],"question":"Tell me about a traditional dance in your country.","html":"There are several traditional dances in Vietnam, often performed during festivals. Dancers move together, wear colourful clothes and use music and movement to tell stories about <strong class=\"key-phrase\">local culture</strong>."},{"text":"Yes, I think people will keep doing it, especially if schools and cultural groups make it interesting. It may not become a common hobby, but it is worth keeping.","phrases":[{"en":"worth keeping","meaning":"Important or useful enough to preserve."}],"question":"Do you think that traditional dancing will be popular in the future?","html":"Yes, I think people will keep doing it, especially if schools and cultural groups make it interesting. It may not become a common hobby, but it is <strong class=\"key-phrase\">worth keeping</strong>."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-019-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-019-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-019-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-019-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Remembering dreams and what they teach","prompt":"Do you often remember your dreams?\nCan dreams teach us anything?\nDo you think dreams can come true?","answer":"Q: Do you often remember your dreams?\nA: I remember dreams only occasionally, usually when I wake up during the night. Most details disappear within minutes unless the dream is <strong class=\"key-phrase\">unusually vivid</strong> or <strong class=\"key-phrase\">emotionally intense</strong>.\n\nQ: Can dreams teach us anything?\nA: They may reveal what has been occupying our attention, but I&#x27;d be cautious about treating them as predictions. At most, they can provide <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a useful prompt for reflection</strong>.\n\nQ: Do you think dreams can come true?\nA: Not in a supernatural sense. Occasionally a dream resembles a later event, but that&#x27;s probably coincidence combined with selective memory rather than <strong class=\"key-phrase\">evidence of prediction</strong>.","topic":"Dreams","phrases":[{"en":"unusually vivid","context":"Q: Do you often remember your dreams?\nA: I remember dreams only occasionally, usually when I wake up during the night. Most details disappear within minutes unless the dream is unusually vivid or emotionally intense."},{"en":"emotionally intense","context":"Q: Do you often remember your dreams?\nA: I remember dreams only occasionally, usually when I wake up during the night. Most details disappear within minutes unless the dream is unusually vivid or emotionally intense."},{"en":"a useful prompt for reflection","context":"Q: Can dreams teach us anything?\nA: They may reveal what has been occupying our attention, but I'd be cautious about treating them as predictions. At most, they can provide a useful prompt for reflection."},{"en":"evidence of prediction","context":"Q: Do you think dreams can come true?\nA: Not in a supernatural sense. Occasionally a dream resembles a later event, but that's probably coincidence combined with selective memory rather than evidence of prediction."}],"subtype":"","summary":"Dreams","id":"speaking-part-1-020","_displayNo":"#019","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-020-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-020-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-020-q03.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"Only sometimes, usually if I wake up in the night. I forget most of the details quickly, unless the dream feels very clear or makes me feel something strongly.","phrases":[{"en":"the details","meaning":"The smaller pieces of information about something."}],"question":"Do you often remember your dreams?","html":"Only sometimes, usually if I wake up in the night. I forget most of <strong class=\"key-phrase\">the details</strong> quickly, unless the dream feels very clear or makes me feel something strongly."},{"text":"Dreams may show what we have been thinking about. I wouldn't use them to predict the future, but they can encourage us to think about our feelings and experiences.","phrases":[{"en":"predict the future","meaning":"Say what will happen later."}],"question":"Can dreams teach us anything?","html":"Dreams may show what we have been thinking about. I wouldn&#x27;t use them to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">predict the future</strong>, but they can encourage us to think about our feelings and experiences."},{"text":"I don't think dreams can tell the future. A dream may sometimes be similar to a later event, but that is probably chance. We may simply remember the dreams that seem to match.","phrases":[{"en":"chance","meaning":"Happening without being planned or caused on purpose."}],"question":"Do you think dreams can come true?","html":"I don&#x27;t think dreams can tell the future. A dream may sometimes be similar to a later event, but that is probably <strong class=\"key-phrase\">chance</strong>. We may simply remember the dreams that seem to match."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-020-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-020-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-020-q03.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"How often you dream, and nightmares","prompt":"How often do you have dreams?\nWhat do you dream about?\nWhy do some people have nightmares?\nIs dreaming important to our well-being and health? Why?","answer":"Q: How often do you have dreams?\nA: I probably dream every night, but I remember only one or two dreams a week. I usually recall them when they&#x27;re <strong class=\"key-phrase\">unusually vivid</strong> or when I wake up before the dream has faded.\n\nQ: What do you dream about?\nA: My dreams often combine ordinary places with unrealistic events, such as being late for an exam in a building I&#x27;ve never seen. They seem to reflect fragments of recent experiences rather than <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a hidden message</strong>.\n\nQ: Why do some people have nightmares?\nA: Nightmares can be triggered by stress, disturbed sleep or frightening experiences. When the brain is processing strong emotions, it may create threatening situations that feel <strong class=\"key-phrase\">surprisingly real</strong>.\n\nQ: Is dreaming important to our well-being and health? Why?\nA: Good-quality sleep is essential, but dreaming itself is still difficult to interpret. It may help the brain <strong class=\"key-phrase\">process memories and emotions</strong>, although its precise role remains <strong class=\"key-phrase\">open to interpretation</strong>.","topic":"Dreams","phrases":[{"en":"unusually vivid","context":"Q: How often do you have dreams?\nA: I probably dream every night, but I remember only one or two dreams a week. I usually recall them when they're unusually vivid or when I wake up before the dream has faded."},{"en":"a hidden message","context":"Q: What do you dream about?\nA: My dreams often combine ordinary places with unrealistic events, such as being late for an exam in a building I've never seen. They seem to reflect fragments of recent experiences rather than a hidden message."},{"en":"surprisingly real","context":"Q: Why do some people have nightmares?\nA: Nightmares can be triggered by stress, disturbed sleep or frightening experiences. When the brain is processing strong emotions, it may create threatening situations that feel surprisingly real."},{"en":"process memories and emotions","context":"Q: Is dreaming important to our well-being and health? Why?\nA: Good-quality sleep is essential, but dreaming itself is still difficult to interpret. It may help the brain process memories and emotions, although its precise role remains open to interpretation."},{"en":"open to interpretation","context":"Q: Is dreaming important to our well-being and health? Why?\nA: Good-quality sleep is essential, but dreaming itself is still difficult to interpret. It may help the brain process memories and emotions, although its precise role remains open to interpretation."}],"subtype":"Part 1","summary":"Dreams","visual":null,"id":"speaking-part-1-021","_displayNo":"#020","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-021-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-021-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-021-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-021-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"I probably dream every night, but I only remember one or two dreams each week. I usually remember them if they feel very clear or I wake up soon afterwards.","phrases":[{"en":"afterwards","meaning":"After something has happened."}],"question":"How often do you have dreams?","html":"I probably dream every night, but I only remember one or two dreams each week. I usually remember them if they feel very clear or I wake up soon <strong class=\"key-phrase\">afterwards</strong>."},{"text":"My dreams often mix normal places with strange events, like being late for an exam in an unfamiliar building. I think they come from recent experiences rather than secret messages.","phrases":[{"en":"unfamiliar","meaning":"Not known or recognised by you."}],"question":"What do you dream about?","html":"My dreams often mix normal places with strange events, like being late for an exam in an <strong class=\"key-phrase\">unfamiliar</strong> building. I think they come from recent experiences rather than secret messages."},{"text":"People may have bad dreams when they feel stressed, sleep badly or have frightening experiences. Strong feelings can appear in dreams as scary situations that seem real.","phrases":[{"en":"stressed","meaning":"Feeling worried or under too much pressure."}],"question":"Why do some people have nightmares?","html":"People may have bad dreams when they feel <strong class=\"key-phrase\">stressed</strong>, sleep badly or have frightening experiences. Strong feelings can appear in dreams as scary situations that seem real."},{"text":"Good sleep is important for health, but we still do not fully understand dreaming. Dreams may help us deal with memories and feelings, although their exact purpose is not clear.","phrases":[{"en":"deal with","meaning":"Handle or respond to something."}],"question":"Is dreaming important to our well-being and health? Why?","html":"Good sleep is important for health, but we still do not fully understand dreaming. Dreams may help us <strong class=\"key-phrase\">deal with</strong> memories and feelings, although their exact purpose is not clear."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-021-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-021-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-021-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-021-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Writing by hand or on a computer","prompt":"At work or in your studies, do you often write things?\nHow often do you send emails?\nDo you prefer to write by hand or on a computer?\nDo you think computers might one day replace handwriting?","answer":"Q: At work or in your studies, do you often write things?\nA: Yes, I write a lot of emails <strong class=\"key-phrase\">as part of my job</strong>. I work for a company that has offices in several countries, so we use email to communicate.\n\nQ: How often do you send emails?\nA: I probably write between 5 and 10 work emails every day, and I send emails to friends or family <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a few times a week</strong>.\n\nQ: Do you prefer to write by hand or on a computer?\nA: It depends on what I&#x27;m doing. I prefer the computer for most things because it&#x27;s faster and you can save or copy things, but I still like making notes or <strong class=\"key-phrase\">writing ideas down</strong> by hand.\n\nQ: Do you think computers might one day replace handwriting?\nA: No, I think we&#x27;ll always write by hand as well. I think it&#x27;s <strong class=\"key-phrase\">an important skill</strong>, and schools will continue to teach children to write by hand before they learn to type.","topic":"Emails & Handwriting","phrases":[{"en":"as part of my job","context":"Q: At work or in your studies, do you often write things?\nA: Yes, I write a lot of emails as part of my job. I work for a company that has offices in several countries, so we use email to communicate."},{"en":"a few times a week","context":"Q: How often do you send emails?\nA: I probably write between 5 and 10 work emails every day, and I send emails to friends or family a few times a week."},{"en":"writing ideas down","context":"Q: Do you prefer to write by hand or on a computer?\nA: It depends on what I'm doing. I prefer the computer for most things because it's faster and you can save or copy things, but I still like making notes or writing ideas down by hand."},{"en":"an important skill","context":"Q: Do you think computers might one day replace handwriting?\nA: No, I think we'll always write by hand as well. I think it's an important skill, and schools will continue to teach children to write by hand before they learn to type."}],"subtype":"","summary":"Emails And Handwriting","id":"speaking-part-1-022","_displayNo":"#021","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-022-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-022-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-022-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-022-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"Yes, I write many emails for work. My company has offices in different countries, so email is an important way for us to exchange information and stay in contact.","phrases":[{"en":"stay in contact","meaning":"Continue communicating with someone."}],"question":"At work or in your studies, do you often write things?","html":"Yes, I write many emails for work. My company has offices in different countries, so email is an important way for us to exchange information and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">stay in contact</strong>."},{"text":"I write about five to ten emails for work each day. I also email friends or family a few times a week, although work makes up most of my email use.","phrases":[{"en":"a few times a week","meaning":"On several occasions during a week."}],"question":"How often do you send emails?","html":"I write about five to ten emails for work each day. I also email friends or family <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a few times a week</strong>, although work makes up most of my email use."},{"text":"I usually prefer a computer because typing is faster and I can save or copy my work easily. However, I still like using a pen for short notes and ideas.","phrases":[{"en":"short notes","meaning":"Brief pieces of writing used to remember information."}],"question":"Do you prefer to write by hand or on a computer?","html":"I usually prefer a computer because typing is faster and I can save or copy my work easily. However, I still like using a pen for <strong class=\"key-phrase\">short notes</strong> and ideas."},{"text":"No, I think people will still need handwriting. It is a useful skill, and schools will probably continue teaching children to write with a pen before they learn typing.","phrases":[{"en":"handwriting","meaning":"Writing done by hand with a pen or pencil."}],"question":"Do you think computers might one day replace handwriting?","html":"No, I think people will still need <strong class=\"key-phrase\">handwriting</strong>. It is a useful skill, and schools will probably continue teaching children to write with a pen before they learn typing."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-022-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-022-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-022-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-022-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Describing your family and time together","prompt":"Can you describe your family?\nDo you have a large or a small family?\nHow much time do you spend with your family?\nWhat do you like to do together as a family?","answer":"Q: Can you describe your family?\nA: I come from a small, close family consisting of my parents, one sibling and me. We&#x27;ve got different personalities, but we support one another and maintain a <strong class=\"key-phrase\">close-knit family</strong>.\n\nQ: Do you have a large or a small family?\nA: My immediate family&#x27;s fairly small. That makes it easier for us to stay informed about one another&#x27;s lives and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">resolve disagreements</strong> before they <strong class=\"key-phrase\">become serious problems</strong>.\n\nQ: How much time do you spend with your family?\nA: I see my family regularly, especially in the evenings and at weekends. Even when everyone&#x27;s busy, we try to share at least one meal and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">catch up with</strong> each other.\n\nQ: What do you like to do together as a family?\nA: We usually share a meal, take short trips or simply talk about what&#x27;s happened during the week. None of those activities is unusual, but they give us <strong class=\"key-phrase\">uninterrupted time together</strong>.","topic":"Family","phrases":[{"en":"close-knit family","context":"Q: Can you describe your family?\nA: I come from a small, close family consisting of my parents, one sibling and me. We've got different personalities, but we support one another and maintain a close-knit family."},{"en":"resolve disagreements","context":"Q: Do you have a large or a small family?\nA: My immediate family's fairly small. That makes it easier for us to stay informed about one another's lives and resolve disagreements before they become serious problems."},{"en":"become serious problems","context":"Q: Do you have a large or a small family?\nA: My immediate family's fairly small. That makes it easier for us to stay informed about one another's lives and resolve disagreements before they become serious problems."},{"en":"catch up with","context":"Q: How much time do you spend with your family?\nA: I see my family regularly, especially in the evenings and at weekends. Even when everyone's busy, we try to share at least one meal and catch up with each other."},{"en":"uninterrupted time together","context":"Q: What do you like to do together as a family?\nA: We usually share a meal, take short trips or simply talk about what's happened during the week. None of those activities is unusual, but they give us uninterrupted time together."}],"subtype":"Part 1","summary":"Family","visual":null,"id":"speaking-part-1-023","_displayNo":"#022","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-023-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-023-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-023-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-023-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"There are four people in my family: my parents, my sibling and me. We have different personalities, but we are close and always try to support each other.","phrases":[{"en":"support each other","meaning":"Help one another when needed."}],"question":"Can you describe your family?","html":"There are four people in my family: my parents, my sibling and me. We have different personalities, but we are close and always try to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">support each other</strong>."},{"text":"My immediate family is quite small. We know what is happening in each other's lives, and it is usually easy to talk through problems before they become serious.","phrases":[{"en":"immediate family","meaning":"Your closest family members, such as parents and siblings."}],"question":"Do you have a large or a small family?","html":"My <strong class=\"key-phrase\">immediate family</strong> is quite small. We know what is happening in each other&#x27;s lives, and it is usually easy to talk through problems before they become serious."},{"text":"I spend time with my family regularly, mostly in the evenings and at weekends. Even when we are busy, we try to eat together and talk about our day.","phrases":[{"en":"regularly","meaning":"Often, or following a repeated pattern."}],"question":"How much time do you spend with your family?","html":"I spend time with my family <strong class=\"key-phrase\">regularly</strong>, mostly in the evenings and at weekends. Even when we are busy, we try to eat together and talk about our day."},{"text":"We enjoy eating together, taking short trips and talking about our week. These are simple activities, but they give us time to enjoy each other's company without interruptions.","phrases":[{"en":"each other's company","meaning":"Being together and spending time with one another."}],"question":"What do you like to do together as a family?","html":"We enjoy eating together, taking short trips and talking about our week. These are simple activities, but they give us time to enjoy <strong class=\"key-phrase\">each other&#x27;s company</strong> without interruptions."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-023-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-023-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-023-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-023-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Who you live with and what you do together","prompt":"Who do you live with?\nDo you spend much time with your family?\nIs your family small or quite large?\nWhat do you do when you are all together?","answer":"Q: Who do you live with?\nA: I live with close family members in Hanoi. Sharing a home requires compromise, but it also provides <strong class=\"key-phrase\">practical support</strong> and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a sense of belonging</strong>.\n\nQ: Do you spend much time with your family?\nA: I spend a reasonable amount of time with my family, mainly over dinner and at weekends. We&#x27;re all busy, so those regular conversations help us <strong class=\"key-phrase\">stay closely connected</strong>.\n\nQ: Is your family small or quite large?\nA: My family is <strong class=\"key-phrase\">relatively small</strong>, which means decisions are easier to coordinate and everyone knows what&#x27;s happening in one another&#x27;s lives.\n\nQ: What do you do when you are all together?\nA: We usually eat together, talk about work and occasionally <strong class=\"key-phrase\">take a short trip</strong>. The activity itself isn&#x27;t important; what matters is having uninterrupted time to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">strengthen our relationship</strong>.","topic":"Family","phrases":[{"en":"practical support","context":"Q: Who do you live with?\nA: I live with close family members in Hanoi. Sharing a home requires compromise, but it also provides practical support and a sense of belonging."},{"en":"a sense of belonging","context":"Q: Who do you live with?\nA: I live with close family members in Hanoi. Sharing a home requires compromise, but it also provides practical support and a sense of belonging."},{"en":"stay closely connected","context":"Q: Do you spend much time with your family?\nA: I spend a reasonable amount of time with my family, mainly over dinner and at weekends. We're all busy, so those regular conversations help us stay closely connected."},{"en":"relatively small","context":"Q: Is your family small or quite large?\nA: My family is relatively small, which means decisions are easier to coordinate and everyone knows what's happening in one another's lives."},{"en":"take a short trip","context":"Q: What do you do when you are all together?\nA: We usually eat together, talk about work and occasionally take a short trip. The activity itself isn't important; what matters is having uninterrupted time to strengthen our relationship."},{"en":"strengthen our relationship","context":"Q: What do you do when you are all together?\nA: We usually eat together, talk about work and occasionally take a short trip. The activity itself isn't important; what matters is having uninterrupted time to strengthen our relationship."}],"subtype":"Part 1","summary":"Family","visual":null,"id":"speaking-part-1-024","_displayNo":"#023","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-024-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-024-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-024-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-024-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"I live with close family members in Hanoi. We sometimes need to accept each other's wishes, but living together means we can help one another and feel part of a family.","phrases":[{"en":"part of a family","meaning":"Connected to and included in a family group."}],"question":"Who do you live with?","html":"I live with close family members in Hanoi. We sometimes need to accept each other&#x27;s wishes, but living together means we can help one another and feel <strong class=\"key-phrase\">part of a family</strong>."},{"text":"Yes, I spend a fair amount of time with them, especially at dinner and at weekends. We all have busy lives, so these regular chats help us stay close.","phrases":[{"en":"stay close","meaning":"Keep a strong and caring relationship."}],"question":"Do you spend much time with your family?","html":"Yes, I spend a fair amount of time with them, especially at dinner and at weekends. We all have busy lives, so these regular chats help us <strong class=\"key-phrase\">stay close</strong>."},{"text":"My family is quite small. It is easier to make plans together because there are fewer people, and we usually know what everyone else is doing.","phrases":[{"en":"make plans","meaning":"Decide what you will do in the future."}],"question":"Is your family small or quite large?","html":"My family is quite small. It is easier to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">make plans</strong> together because there are fewer people, and we usually know what everyone else is doing."},{"text":"We usually have meals, talk about work and sometimes go on short trips. What we do matters less than having time together without distractions, which helps us become closer.","phrases":[{"en":"distractions","meaning":"Things that take your attention away from what you are doing."}],"question":"What do you do when you are all together?","html":"We usually have meals, talk about work and sometimes go on short trips. What we do matters less than having time together without <strong class=\"key-phrase\">distractions</strong>, which helps us become closer."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-024-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-024-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-024-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-024-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"The main festivals in your country","prompt":"Can you describe one of the main festivals celebrated in your country?\nWhat can you tell me about the most important festival in your country?\nWhat special food and activities are connected with this festival?\nWhat do you most enjoy about it?","answer":"Q: Can you describe one of the main festivals celebrated in your country?\nA: Tet, the Lunar New Year, is the most important festival in Vietnam. Families reunite, clean and decorate their homes, and prepare for a fresh start, so the celebration <strong class=\"key-phrase\">brings people together</strong>.\n\nQ: What can you tell me about the most important festival in your country?\nA: Tet matters because it marks a new beginning and gives everyone a proper break from work. Beyond the celebrations, it&#x27;s a time to honour ancestors and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">renew family connections</strong>.\n\nQ: What special food and activities are connected with this festival?\nA: Traditional foods include traditional sticky-rice cakes, candied fruit and various family dishes. People also visit relatives, give lucky money to children and pay respect to ancestors, which helps <strong class=\"key-phrase\">preserve local identity</strong>.\n\nQ: What do you most enjoy about it?\nA: I enjoy the slower pace and the chance to spend uninterrupted time with family. The atmosphere&#x27;s festive, but the most valuable part is the <strong class=\"key-phrase\">sense of renewal</strong>.","topic":"Festivals","phrases":[{"en":"brings people together","context":"Q: Can you describe one of the main festivals celebrated in your country?\nA: Tet, the Lunar New Year, is the most important festival in Vietnam. Families reunite, clean and decorate their homes, and prepare for a fresh start, so the celebration brings people together."},{"en":"renew family connections","context":"Q: What can you tell me about the most important festival in your country?\nA: Tet matters because it marks a new beginning and gives everyone a proper break from work. Beyond the celebrations, it's a time to honour ancestors and renew family connections."},{"en":"preserve local identity","context":"Q: What special food and activities are connected with this festival?\nA: Traditional foods include traditional sticky-rice cakes, candied fruit and various family dishes. People also visit relatives, give lucky money to children and pay respect to ancestors, which helps preserve local identity."},{"en":"sense of renewal","context":"Q: What do you most enjoy about it?\nA: I enjoy the slower pace and the chance to spend uninterrupted time with family. The atmosphere's festive, but the most valuable part is the sense of renewal."}],"subtype":"Part 1","summary":"Festival","visual":null,"id":"speaking-part-1-025","_displayNo":"#024","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-025-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-025-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-025-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-025-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"Tet is the Lunar New Year and Vietnam's most important festival. Families come together, clean and decorate their homes, and get ready for a new year. It is a time for being together.","phrases":[{"en":"come together","meaning":"Meet and spend time as a group."}],"question":"Can you describe one of the main festivals celebrated in your country?","html":"Tet is the Lunar New Year and Vietnam&#x27;s most important festival. Families <strong class=\"key-phrase\">come together</strong>, clean and decorate their homes, and get ready for a new year. It is a time for being together."},{"text":"Tet marks the start of a new year and gives people a break from work. It is also a time to remember family members who have died and reconnect with relatives.","phrases":[{"en":"reconnect with","meaning":"Become close to or communicate with someone again."}],"question":"What can you tell me about the most important festival in your country?","html":"Tet marks the start of a new year and gives people a break from work. It is also a time to remember family members who have died and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">reconnect with</strong> relatives."},{"text":"People eat sticky-rice cakes, sweet preserved fruit and special family dishes. They visit relatives, give children lucky money and remember their ancestors. These customs help keep Vietnamese traditions alive.","phrases":[{"en":"ancestors","meaning":"Family members from generations before your parents or grandparents."}],"question":"What special food and activities are connected with this festival?","html":"People eat sticky-rice cakes, sweet preserved fruit and special family dishes. They visit relatives, give children lucky money and remember their <strong class=\"key-phrase\">ancestors</strong>. These customs help keep Vietnamese traditions alive."},{"text":"I most enjoy having a slower, quieter few days with my family. The celebrations are fun, but I especially like the feeling of starting again with fresh energy.","phrases":[{"en":"starting again","meaning":"Making a new beginning."}],"question":"What do you most enjoy about it?","html":"I most enjoy having a slower, quieter few days with my family. The celebrations are fun, but I especially like the feeling of <strong class=\"key-phrase\">starting again</strong> with fresh energy."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-025-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-025-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-025-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-025-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Film stars' pay, violence and censorship","prompt":"Are film stars paid too much money, in your opinion?\nDo you think there is too much violence in modern movies?\nWhat do you think about film censorship, and is it necessary?\nWhat was the last film you saw? Did you enjoy it?","answer":"Q: Are film stars paid too much money, in your opinion?\nA: A few global stars are paid extraordinary sums, but their names can determine whether a film attracts investment and audiences. I think the salaries seem excessive, although that&#x27;s more about <strong class=\"key-phrase\">commercial value rather than social value</strong>.\n\nQ: Do you think there is too much violence in modern movies?\nA: Some films rely too heavily on violence because it creates immediate excitement. I don&#x27;t think violence is a problem in itself, but repeated graphic scenes can become <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a substitute for good writing</strong>.\n\nQ: What do you think about film censorship, and is it necessary?\nA: I think some classification is necessary to protect children and warn viewers, but blanket censorship is risky. Adults should generally be free to choose what they watch, provided there&#x27;s <strong class=\"key-phrase\">clear age guidance</strong>.\n\nQ: What was the last film you saw? Did you enjoy it?\nA: The last film I watched was a thoughtful drama about a family dealing with change. I enjoyed it because the characters felt believable and the story avoided <strong class=\"key-phrase\">an overly predictable ending</strong>.","topic":"Films","phrases":[{"en":"commercial value rather than social value","context":"Q: Are film stars paid too much money, in your opinion?\nA: A few global stars are paid extraordinary sums, but their names can determine whether a film attracts investment and audiences. I think the salaries seem excessive, although that's more about commercial value rather than social value."},{"en":"a substitute for good writing","context":"Q: Do you think there is too much violence in modern movies?\nA: Some films rely too heavily on violence because it creates immediate excitement. I don't think violence is a problem in itself, but repeated graphic scenes can become a substitute for good writing."},{"en":"clear age guidance","context":"Q: What do you think about film censorship, and is it necessary?\nA: I think some classification is necessary to protect children and warn viewers, but blanket censorship is risky. Adults should generally be free to choose what they watch, provided there's clear age guidance."},{"en":"an overly predictable ending","context":"Q: What was the last film you saw? Did you enjoy it?\nA: The last film I watched was a thoughtful drama about a family dealing with change. I enjoyed it because the characters felt believable and the story avoided an overly predictable ending."}],"subtype":"Part 1","summary":"Films","visual":null,"id":"speaking-part-1-026","_displayNo":"#025","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-026-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-026-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-026-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-026-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"Some famous actors earn far more than seems reasonable to me. However, their names help attract money and audiences to films. Their pay reflects their business value more than their wider contribution to society.","phrases":[{"en":"attract","meaning":"Make people interested in coming or taking part."}],"question":"Are film stars paid too much money, in your opinion?","html":"Some famous actors earn far more than seems reasonable to me. However, their names help <strong class=\"key-phrase\">attract</strong> money and audiences to films. Their pay reflects their business value more than their wider contribution to society."},{"text":"Yes, some films use violence too often to make things exciting. Violence can be part of a story, but too many detailed, violent scenes cannot make up for a weak story.","phrases":[{"en":"make up for","meaning":"Balance or improve a bad situation by adding something else."}],"question":"Do you think there is too much violence in modern movies?","html":"Yes, some films use violence too often to make things exciting. Violence can be part of a story, but too many detailed, violent scenes cannot <strong class=\"key-phrase\">make up for</strong> a weak story."},{"text":"I think films need age ratings so parents can protect children and viewers know what to expect. However, adults should usually choose for themselves rather than have whole films banned.","phrases":[{"en":"age ratings","meaning":"Labels showing which age groups a film is suitable for."}],"question":"What do you think about film censorship, and is it necessary?","html":"I think films need <strong class=\"key-phrase\">age ratings</strong> so parents can protect children and viewers know what to expect. However, adults should usually choose for themselves rather than have whole films banned."},{"text":"The last film I saw was a drama about a family going through changes. I enjoyed it because the people seemed real and I could not easily guess how it would end.","phrases":[{"en":"going through","meaning":"Experiencing a situation or period of change."}],"question":"What was the last film you saw? Did you enjoy it?","html":"The last film I saw was a drama about a family <strong class=\"key-phrase\">going through</strong> changes. I enjoyed it because the people seemed real and I could not easily guess how it would end."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-026-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-026-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-026-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-026-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Watching films alone, with friends or at the cinema","prompt":"Do you enjoy watching movies?\nDo you prefer to see a movie alone or with your friends?\nDo you prefer watching films at the cinema or at home?\nWhat is your most/least favourite type of movie?","answer":"Q: Do you enjoy watching movies?\nA: Yes, especially well-written dramas and documentaries. A good film allows me to relax while seeing a situation from <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a different point of view</strong>.\n\nQ: Do you prefer to see a movie alone or with your friends?\nA: I usually watch films with friends because discussing them afterwards adds to the experience. For serious or complex films, however, I sometimes prefer watching alone so I can <strong class=\"key-phrase\">pay close attention to</strong> the details.\n\nQ: Do you prefer watching films at the cinema or at home?\nA: I prefer the cinema for <strong class=\"key-phrase\">visually impressive</strong> films, but home&#x27;s more convenient for ordinary viewing. The cinema offers immersion, while home allows me to pause and watch <strong class=\"key-phrase\">at my own pace</strong>.\n\nQ: What is your most/least favourite type of movie?\nA: My favourite genre is realistic drama, and I&#x27;m least interested in formulaic horror films. I prefer stories with convincing characters and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">emotional depth</strong>.","topic":"Films","phrases":[{"en":"a different point of view","context":"Q: Do you enjoy watching movies?\nA: Yes, especially well-written dramas and documentaries. A good film allows me to relax while seeing a situation from a different point of view."},{"en":"pay close attention to","context":"Q: Do you prefer to see a movie alone or with your friends?\nA: I usually watch films with friends because discussing them afterwards adds to the experience. For serious or complex films, however, I sometimes prefer watching alone so I can pay close attention to the details."},{"en":"visually impressive","context":"Q: Do you prefer watching films at the cinema or at home?\nA: I prefer the cinema for visually impressive films, but home's more convenient for ordinary viewing. The cinema offers immersion, while home allows me to pause and watch at my own pace."},{"en":"at my own pace","context":"Q: Do you prefer watching films at the cinema or at home?\nA: I prefer the cinema for visually impressive films, but home's more convenient for ordinary viewing. The cinema offers immersion, while home allows me to pause and watch at my own pace."},{"en":"emotional depth","context":"Q: What is your most/least favourite type of movie?\nA: My favourite genre is realistic drama, and I'm least interested in formulaic horror films. I prefer stories with convincing characters and emotional depth."}],"subtype":"Part 1","summary":"Films","visual":null,"id":"speaking-part-1-027","_displayNo":"#026","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-027-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-027-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-027-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-027-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"Yes, especially dramas with good stories and documentaries. Watching a film helps me relax, and it can also help me understand a situation from someone else's point of view.","phrases":[{"en":"point of view","meaning":"The way a person thinks about or understands something."}],"question":"Do you enjoy watching movies?","html":"Yes, especially dramas with good stories and documentaries. Watching a film helps me relax, and it can also help me understand a situation from someone else&#x27;s <strong class=\"key-phrase\">point of view</strong>."},{"text":"I usually watch with friends because I enjoy talking about the film afterwards. However, I sometimes watch complicated or serious films alone so I can concentrate on the details.","phrases":[{"en":"concentrate on","meaning":"Give your full attention to something."}],"question":"Do you prefer to see a movie alone or with your friends?","html":"I usually watch with friends because I enjoy talking about the film afterwards. However, I sometimes watch complicated or serious films alone so I can <strong class=\"key-phrase\">concentrate on</strong> the details."},{"text":"For films with impressive pictures, I prefer the cinema. For other films, home is easier because I can pause or choose my own speed. Both have advantages, depending on the film.","phrases":[{"en":"pause","meaning":"Stop something for a short time before continuing."}],"question":"Do you prefer watching films at the cinema or at home?","html":"For films with impressive pictures, I prefer the cinema. For other films, home is easier because I can <strong class=\"key-phrase\">pause</strong> or choose my own speed. Both have advantages, depending on the film."},{"text":"I like realistic dramas most because I enjoy believable people and meaningful feelings. I am least interested in horror films that repeat the same ideas and have predictable stories.","phrases":[{"en":"predictable","meaning":"Easy to guess before it happens."}],"question":"What is your most/least favourite type of movie?","html":"I like realistic dramas most because I enjoy believable people and meaningful feelings. I am least interested in horror films that repeat the same ideas and have <strong class=\"key-phrase\">predictable</strong> stories."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-027-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-027-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-027-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-027-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Cooking at home and family meals","prompt":"Do you like cooking?\nWho does the cooking in your home?\nDo you think family meals are important?\nWhat kind of food do you like?","answer":"Q: Do you like cooking?\nA: Yes, although I cook simple meals rather than elaborate dishes. I enjoy being able to control the ingredients and adjust flavours <strong class=\"key-phrase\">to my own taste</strong>.\n\nQ: Who does the cooking in your home?\nA: Cooking is shared in my home, depending on who&#x27;s got time. That arrangement is practical and prevents one person from carrying <strong class=\"key-phrase\">the entire responsibility</strong>.\n\nQ: Do you think family meals are important?\nA: Yes, because they create a regular opportunity for people to talk without distractions. Even a short meal can help family members <strong class=\"key-phrase\">stay connected</strong>.\n\nQ: What kind of food do you like?\nA: I like fresh Vietnamese food, particularly dishes with vegetables, herbs and light broths. I&#x27;m less keen on food that&#x27;s excessively oily because it leaves me feeling <strong class=\"key-phrase\">heavy and tired</strong>.","topic":"Food","phrases":[{"en":"to my own taste","context":"Q: Do you like cooking?\nA: Yes, although I cook simple meals rather than elaborate dishes. I enjoy being able to control the ingredients and adjust flavours to my own taste."},{"en":"the entire responsibility","context":"Q: Who does the cooking in your home?\nA: Cooking is shared in my home, depending on who's got time. That arrangement is practical and prevents one person from carrying the entire responsibility."},{"en":"stay connected","context":"Q: Do you think family meals are important?\nA: Yes, because they create a regular opportunity for people to talk without distractions. Even a short meal can help family members stay connected."},{"en":"heavy and tired","context":"Q: What kind of food do you like?\nA: I like fresh Vietnamese food, particularly dishes with vegetables, herbs and light broths. I'm less keen on food that's excessively oily because it leaves me feeling heavy and tired."}],"subtype":"Part 1","summary":"Food","visual":null,"id":"speaking-part-1-028","_displayNo":"#027","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-028-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-028-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-028-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-028-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"Yes, but I mainly make simple meals. I enjoy choosing the ingredients myself and changing the flavour until the food tastes the way I like it.","phrases":[{"en":"ingredients","meaning":"The foods used to make a dish."}],"question":"Do you like cooking?","html":"Yes, but I mainly make simple meals. I enjoy choosing the <strong class=\"key-phrase\">ingredients</strong> myself and changing the flavour until the food tastes the way I like it."},{"text":"We share the cooking, depending on who has time. This works well because one person does not have to prepare all the meals on their own.","phrases":[{"en":"share the cooking","meaning":"Divide the work of preparing meals between people."}],"question":"Who does the cooking in your home?","html":"We <strong class=\"key-phrase\">share the cooking</strong>, depending on who has time. This works well because one person does not have to prepare all the meals on their own."},{"text":"Yes, family meals are important because they give us a regular chance to talk. Even a quick meal together can help us stay close if we give each other our attention.","phrases":[{"en":"a regular chance","meaning":"An opportunity that happens often or repeatedly."}],"question":"Do you think family meals are important?","html":"Yes, family meals are important because they give us <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a regular chance</strong> to talk. Even a quick meal together can help us stay close if we give each other our attention."},{"text":"I enjoy fresh Vietnamese dishes, especially vegetables, herbs and light soups. I don't like food with too much oil because it can make me feel full in an uncomfortable way and tired.","phrases":[{"en":"herbs","meaning":"Plants or leaves used to add flavour to food."}],"question":"What kind of food do you like?","html":"I enjoy fresh Vietnamese dishes, especially vegetables, <strong class=\"key-phrase\">herbs</strong> and light soups. I don&#x27;t like food with too much oil because it can make me feel full in an uncomfortable way and tired."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-028-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-028-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-028-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-028-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Favourite foods and eating out","prompt":"What are your most/ least favourite foods?\nIf you invited a friend over for a meal, what would you serve?\nDo you prefer eating at home or in a restaurant and why?\nWhat special dish from your country would you recommend to a visitor?","answer":"Q: What are your most/ least favourite foods?\nA: I <strong class=\"key-phrase\">particularly enjoy</strong> fresh Vietnamese dishes with herbs, vegetables and light broths. I&#x27;m least fond of food that&#x27;s extremely greasy or sweet because it leaves me feeling <strong class=\"key-phrase\">heavy and tired</strong>.\n\nQ: If you invited a friend over for a meal, what would you serve?\nA: I&#x27;d probably serve grilled chicken, rice, vegetables and a light soup. It&#x27;s easy to prepare for several people and can be adapted to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">different dietary preferences</strong>.\n\nQ: Do you prefer eating at home or in a restaurant and why?\nA: I prefer eating at home on ordinary days because it&#x27;s healthier and less expensive. Restaurants are enjoyable for special occasions, but home cooking gives me <strong class=\"key-phrase\">more control over ingredients</strong>.\n\nQ: What special dish from your country would you recommend to a visitor?\nA: I&#x27;d recommend Vietnamese noodle soup because it&#x27;s <strong class=\"key-phrase\">widely available</strong> yet <strong class=\"key-phrase\">closely associated with</strong> Vietnamese cuisine. Its clear broth, herbs and rice noodles create <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a balanced combination of flavours</strong>.","topic":"Food","phrases":[{"en":"particularly enjoy","context":"Q: What are your most/ least favourite foods?\nA: I particularly enjoy fresh Vietnamese dishes with herbs, vegetables and light broths. I'm least fond of food that's extremely greasy or sweet because it leaves me feeling heavy and tired."},{"en":"heavy and tired","context":"Q: What are your most/ least favourite foods?\nA: I particularly enjoy fresh Vietnamese dishes with herbs, vegetables and light broths. I'm least fond of food that's extremely greasy or sweet because it leaves me feeling heavy and tired."},{"en":"different dietary preferences","context":"Q: If you invited a friend over for a meal, what would you serve?\nA: I'd probably serve grilled chicken, rice, vegetables and a light soup. It's easy to prepare for several people and can be adapted to different dietary preferences."},{"en":"more control over ingredients","context":"Q: Do you prefer eating at home or in a restaurant and why?\nA: I prefer eating at home on ordinary days because it's healthier and less expensive. Restaurants are enjoyable for special occasions, but home cooking gives me more control over ingredients."},{"en":"widely available","context":"Q: What special dish from your country would you recommend to a visitor?\nA: I'd recommend Vietnamese noodle soup because it's widely available yet closely associated with Vietnamese cuisine. Its clear broth, herbs and rice noodles create a balanced combination of flavours."},{"en":"closely associated with","context":"Q: What special dish from your country would you recommend to a visitor?\nA: I'd recommend Vietnamese noodle soup because it's widely available yet closely associated with Vietnamese cuisine. Its clear broth, herbs and rice noodles create a balanced combination of flavours."},{"en":"a balanced combination of flavours","context":"Q: What special dish from your country would you recommend to a visitor?\nA: I'd recommend Vietnamese noodle soup because it's widely available yet closely associated with Vietnamese cuisine. Its clear broth, herbs and rice noodles create a balanced combination of flavours."}],"subtype":"Part 1","summary":"Food","visual":null,"id":"speaking-part-1-029","_displayNo":"#028","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-029-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-029-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-029-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-029-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"I like fresh Vietnamese food with vegetables, herbs and light soup. I dislike very oily or very sweet food because it makes me feel uncomfortable and tired afterwards.","phrases":[{"en":"oily","meaning":"Containing a lot of oil or fat."}],"question":"What are your most/ least favourite foods?","html":"I like fresh Vietnamese food with vegetables, herbs and light soup. I dislike very <strong class=\"key-phrase\">oily</strong> or very sweet food because it makes me feel uncomfortable and tired afterwards."},{"text":"I'd make grilled chicken with rice, vegetables and a light soup. It is easy to prepare for a group, and I can change parts of the meal to suit what people eat.","phrases":[{"en":"suit","meaning":"Be right for someone's needs or preferences."}],"question":"If you invited a friend over for a meal, what would you serve?","html":"I&#x27;d make grilled chicken with rice, vegetables and a light soup. It is easy to prepare for a group, and I can change parts of the meal to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">suit</strong> what people eat."},{"text":"I prefer eating at home most days because it costs less and I can choose healthier ingredients. I still enjoy restaurants for special events, but I like having control over my everyday meals.","phrases":[{"en":"having control over","meaning":"Being able to decide how something is done."}],"question":"Do you prefer eating at home or in a restaurant and why?","html":"I prefer eating at home most days because it costs less and I can choose healthier ingredients. I still enjoy restaurants for special events, but I like <strong class=\"key-phrase\">having control over</strong> my everyday meals."},{"text":"I'd suggest Vietnamese noodle soup. Visitors can find it easily, and it is an important part of our food culture. The clear soup, herbs and rice noodles taste good together.","phrases":[{"en":"food culture","meaning":"The foods and eating traditions connected with a group of people."}],"question":"What special dish from your country would you recommend to a visitor?","html":"I&#x27;d suggest Vietnamese noodle soup. Visitors can find it easily, and it is an important part of our <strong class=\"key-phrase\">food culture</strong>. The clear soup, herbs and rice noodles taste good together."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-029-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-029-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-029-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-029-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Time at home and what you do with free time","prompt":"How much time do you spend at home?\nDo you prefer to spend your free time at home or outside the house?\nWhat do you do when you have some free time and you're at home?\nWould you like to have more spare time to spend at home in the future?","answer":"Q: How much time do you spend at home?\nA: Obviously I sleep at home, but I don&#x27;t <strong class=\"key-phrase\">spend very much time at home</strong> during the day, because I&#x27;m usually busy with work.\n\nQ: Do you prefer to spend your free time at home or outside the house?\nA: During the day I prefer to be out of the house, so I like visiting family or <strong class=\"key-phrase\">meeting up with friends</strong>. But I do like relaxing at home in the evenings.\n\nQ: What do you do when you have some free time and you&#x27;re at home?\nA: I usually sit and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">watch some TV</strong> or a film, or I <strong class=\"key-phrase\">listen to some music</strong>. I also like sitting outside if the weather is nice.\n\nQ: Would you like to have more spare time to spend at home in the future?\nA: No, not really. I get bored if I&#x27;m at home for too long. In the future, I imagine I&#x27;ll still <strong class=\"key-phrase\">prefer to go out</strong> and do things rather than stay indoors.","topic":"Free Time","phrases":[{"en":"spend very much time at home","context":"Q: How much time do you spend at home?\nA: Obviously I sleep at home, but I don't spend very much time at home during the day, because I'm usually busy with work."},{"en":"meeting up with friends","context":"Q: Do you prefer to spend your free time at home or outside the house?\nA: During the day I prefer to be out of the house, so I like visiting family or meeting up with friends. But I do like relaxing at home in the evenings."},{"en":"watch some TV","context":"Q: What do you do when you have some free time and you're at home?\nA: I usually sit and watch some TV or a film, or I listen to some music. I also like sitting outside if the weather is nice."},{"en":"listen to some music","context":"Q: What do you do when you have some free time and you're at home?\nA: I usually sit and watch some TV or a film, or I listen to some music. I also like sitting outside if the weather is nice."},{"en":"prefer to go out","context":"Q: Would you like to have more spare time to spend at home in the future?\nA: No, not really. I get bored if I'm at home for too long. In the future, I imagine I'll still prefer to go out and do things rather than stay indoors."}],"subtype":"","summary":"Free Time","id":"speaking-part-1-030","_displayNo":"#029","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-030-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-030-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-030-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-030-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"I sleep at home, of course, but I'm usually out working during the day. Because of that, I don't spend very much of my daytime at home.","phrases":[{"en":"during the day","meaning":"In the hours between morning and evening."}],"question":"How much time do you spend at home?","html":"I sleep at home, of course, but I&#x27;m usually out working <strong class=\"key-phrase\">during the day</strong>. Because of that, I don&#x27;t spend very much of my daytime at home."},{"text":"I like going out during the day to visit family or meet friends. In the evening, though, I enjoy staying at home and relaxing after a busy day.","phrases":[{"en":"meet friends","meaning":"Spend time with people you know and like."}],"question":"Do you prefer to spend your free time at home or outside the house?","html":"I like going out during the day to visit family or <strong class=\"key-phrase\">meet friends</strong>. In the evening, though, I enjoy staying at home and relaxing after a busy day."},{"text":"I usually watch television or a film, or listen to music. If the weather is pleasant, I also enjoy sitting outside and taking a break.","phrases":[{"en":"taking a break","meaning":"Stopping an activity for a short rest."}],"question":"What do you do when you have some free time and you're at home?","html":"I usually watch television or a film, or listen to music. If the weather is pleasant, I also enjoy sitting outside and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">taking a break</strong>."},{"text":"Not really. I become bored if I stay home too long. I think I will still enjoy going out and doing things rather than spending more time indoors.","phrases":[{"en":"indoors","meaning":"Inside a building."}],"question":"Would you like to have more spare time to spend at home in the future?","html":"Not really. I become bored if I stay home too long. I think I will still enjoy going out and doing things rather than spending more time <strong class=\"key-phrase\">indoors</strong>."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-030-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-030-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-030-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-030-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"The age of your friends and when you see them","prompt":"Are your friends mostly your age or different ages?\nDo you usually see your friends during the week or at weekends?\nThe last time you saw your friends, what did you do together?\nIn what ways are your friends important to you?","answer":"Q: Are your friends mostly your age or different ages?\nA: Most of my friends are <strong class=\"key-phrase\">about the same age</strong> as me because we met at school or university. I&#x27;ve got one or two friends who are older or younger that I <strong class=\"key-phrase\">met through work</strong>.\n\nQ: Do you usually see your friends during the week or at weekends?\nA: I tend to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">meet up with my friends</strong> at weekends because everyone&#x27;s too busy during the week.\n\nQ: The last time you saw your friends, what did you do together?\nA: It was one of my friends&#x27; birthday last weekend. Six of us went <strong class=\"key-phrase\">out for a meal</strong> to celebrate.\n\nQ: In what ways are your friends important to you?\nA: I think it&#x27;s important to have friends that you can talk to and share experiences with. My friends <strong class=\"key-phrase\">make me laugh</strong>, but I know I can also rely on them whenever I need help or support.","topic":"Friends","phrases":[{"en":"about the same age","context":"Q: Are your friends mostly your age or different ages?\nA: Most of my friends are about the same age as me because we met at school or university. I've got one or two friends who are older or younger that I met through work."},{"en":"met through work","context":"Q: Are your friends mostly your age or different ages?\nA: Most of my friends are about the same age as me because we met at school or university. I've got one or two friends who are older or younger that I met through work."},{"en":"meet up with my friends","context":"Q: Do you usually see your friends during the week or at weekends?\nA: I tend to meet up with my friends at weekends because everyone's too busy during the week."},{"en":"out for a meal","context":"Q: The last time you saw your friends, what did you do together?\nA: It was one of my friends' birthday last weekend. Six of us went out for a meal to celebrate."},{"en":"make me laugh","context":"Q: In what ways are your friends important to you?\nA: I think it's important to have friends that you can talk to and share experiences with. My friends make me laugh, but I know I can also rely on them whenever I need help or support."}],"subtype":"","summary":"Friends","id":"speaking-part-1-031","_displayNo":"#030","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-031-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-031-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-031-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-031-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"Most are around my age because we met at school or university. I also have one or two older or younger friends whom I met through work.","phrases":[{"en":"around my age","meaning":"About as old as I am."}],"question":"Are your friends mostly your age or different ages?","html":"Most are <strong class=\"key-phrase\">around my age</strong> because we met at school or university. I also have one or two older or younger friends whom I met through work."},{"text":"I usually see my friends at weekends. We are all busy with work or other things during the week, so it is easier to find time then.","phrases":[{"en":"at weekends","meaning":"On Saturdays and Sundays."}],"question":"Do you usually see your friends during the week or at weekends?","html":"I usually see my friends <strong class=\"key-phrase\">at weekends</strong>. We are all busy with work or other things during the week, so it is easier to find time then."},{"text":"We went out for dinner last weekend because it was a friend's birthday. There were six of us, and we had a meal together to celebrate.","phrases":[{"en":"celebrate","meaning":"Do something enjoyable to mark a special occasion."}],"question":"The last time you saw your friends, what did you do together?","html":"We went out for dinner last weekend because it was a friend&#x27;s birthday. There were six of us, and we had a meal together to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">celebrate</strong>."},{"text":"My friends give me people to talk to and share experiences with. They make me laugh, and I know they will help me when I need support.","phrases":[{"en":"support","meaning":"Help or encouragement when you need it."}],"question":"In what ways are your friends important to you?","html":"My friends give me people to talk to and share experiences with. They make me laugh, and I know they will help me when I need <strong class=\"key-phrase\">support</strong>."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-031-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-031-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-031-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-031-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"One close friend or a group of friends","prompt":"Do you prefer to have one particular friend or a group of friends?\nWhat do you like doing most with your friends?\nDo you think it's important to keep in touch with childhood friends?\nWhat makes a good friend?","answer":"Q: Do you prefer to have one particular friend or a group of friends?\nA: I prefer a small group of close friends rather than one exclusive friendship. Different friends bring different perspectives, while the group still gives me <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a reliable support network</strong>.\n\nQ: What do you like doing most with your friends?\nA: We usually have coffee, exercise or take short trips. The activity itself isn&#x27;t the main point; I mainly enjoy having time to talk openly and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">share everyday experiences</strong>.\n\nQ: Do you think it&#x27;s important to keep in touch with childhood friends?\nA: It&#x27;s valuable when the friendship remains healthy, because childhood friends understand your background. But people change, so staying in touch should feel natural rather than <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a social obligation</strong>.\n\nQ: What makes a good friend?\nA: A good friend is trustworthy, honest and able to listen without immediately judging. Mutual respect matters more than constant agreement because it creates <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a genuine connection</strong>.","topic":"Friends","phrases":[{"en":"a reliable support network","context":"Q: Do you prefer to have one particular friend or a group of friends?\nA: I prefer a small group of close friends rather than one exclusive friendship. Different friends bring different perspectives, while the group still gives me a reliable support network."},{"en":"share everyday experiences","context":"Q: What do you like doing most with your friends?\nA: We usually have coffee, exercise or take short trips. The activity itself isn't the main point; I mainly enjoy having time to talk openly and share everyday experiences."},{"en":"a social obligation","context":"Q: Do you think it's important to keep in touch with childhood friends?\nA: It's valuable when the friendship remains healthy, because childhood friends understand your background. But people change, so staying in touch should feel natural rather than a social obligation."},{"en":"a genuine connection","context":"Q: What makes a good friend?\nA: A good friend is trustworthy, honest and able to listen without immediately judging. Mutual respect matters more than constant agreement because it creates a genuine connection."}],"subtype":"Part 1","summary":"Friends","visual":null,"id":"speaking-part-1-032","_displayNo":"#031","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-032-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-032-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-032-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-032-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"I prefer a small group of close friends. Each person has different ideas, and I can learn from them. At the same time, I have several people I can depend on.","phrases":[{"en":"depend on","meaning":"Trust someone to help or do what you need."}],"question":"Do you prefer to have one particular friend or a group of friends?","html":"I prefer a small group of close friends. Each person has different ideas, and I can learn from them. At the same time, I have several people I can <strong class=\"key-phrase\">depend on</strong>."},{"text":"We usually have coffee, exercise or go on short trips. I mainly enjoy having time to talk honestly and share things from our daily lives, whatever activity we choose.","phrases":[{"en":"talk honestly","meaning":"Say what you really think or feel."}],"question":"What do you like doing most with your friends?","html":"We usually have coffee, exercise or go on short trips. I mainly enjoy having time to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">talk honestly</strong> and share things from our daily lives, whatever activity we choose."},{"text":"Yes, if the friendship is still good for both people. Childhood friends know a lot about your past. However, people change, so staying friends should be a choice rather than a duty.","phrases":[{"en":"a duty","meaning":"Something you are expected or required to do."}],"question":"Do you think it's important to keep in touch with childhood friends?","html":"Yes, if the friendship is still good for both people. Childhood friends know a lot about your past. However, people change, so staying friends should be a choice rather than <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a duty</strong>."},{"text":"A good friend is honest, reliable and willing to listen. You don't have to agree on everything, but you should respect one another and feel comfortable talking openly.","phrases":[{"en":"reliable","meaning":"Someone you can trust to do what they say."}],"question":"What makes a good friend?","html":"A good friend is honest, <strong class=\"key-phrase\">reliable</strong> and willing to listen. You don&#x27;t have to agree on everything, but you should respect one another and feel comfortable talking openly."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-032-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-032-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-032-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-032-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Popular games and how people learn them","prompt":"What games are popular in your country?\nDo you play any games?\nHow do people learn to play games in your country?\nDo you think it's important for people to play games?","answer":"Q: What games are popular in your country?\nA: Well, if we count sports as games, then football&#x27;s <strong class=\"key-phrase\">by far the most popular game</strong> in my country, but we also love board games like chess.\n\nQ: Do you play any games?\nA: Not regularly these days. I <strong class=\"key-phrase\">play the occasional game of</strong> tennis with my brother-in-law, and I recently played a bowling game on the Nintendo Wii with my nephew. I wasn&#x27;t very good at it.\n\nQ: How do people learn to play games in your country?\nA: I think children mostly teach each other how to play games, and that&#x27;s how I learned chess too. A friend at primary school <strong class=\"key-phrase\">taught me the rules</strong> when we were young.\n\nQ: Do you think it&#x27;s important for people to play games?\nA: Yes, it&#x27;s really important, especially for children. I think research has shown that play can improve <strong class=\"key-phrase\">brain development</strong>, intelligence, creativity, and the ability to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">cooperate with others</strong>.","topic":"Games","phrases":[{"en":"by far the most popular game","context":"Q: What games are popular in your country?\nA: Well, if we count sports as games, then football's by far the most popular game in my country, but we also love board games like chess."},{"en":"play the occasional game of","context":"Q: Do you play any games?\nA: Not regularly these days. I play the occasional game of tennis with my brother-in-law, and I recently played a bowling game on the Nintendo Wii with my nephew. I wasn't very good at it."},{"en":"taught me the rules","context":"Q: How do people learn to play games in your country?\nA: I think children mostly teach each other how to play games, and that's how I learned chess too. A friend at primary school taught me the rules when we were young."},{"en":"brain development","context":"Q: Do you think it's important for people to play games?\nA: Yes, it's really important, especially for children. I think research has shown that play can improve brain development, intelligence, creativity, and the ability to cooperate with others."},{"en":"cooperate with others","context":"Q: Do you think it's important for people to play games?\nA: Yes, it's really important, especially for children. I think research has shown that play can improve brain development, intelligence, creativity, and the ability to cooperate with others."}],"subtype":"","summary":"Games","id":"speaking-part-1-033","_displayNo":"#032","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-033-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-033-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-033-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-033-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"Football is the most popular if we include sports. People also enjoy board games such as chess, so there are both active games and quieter ones to choose from.","phrases":[{"en":"board games","meaning":"Games played on a board, often using small pieces."}],"question":"What games are popular in your country?","html":"Football is the most popular if we include sports. People also enjoy <strong class=\"key-phrase\">board games</strong> such as chess, so there are both active games and quieter ones to choose from."},{"text":"Not very often now. I sometimes play tennis with my brother-in-law. Recently, I also tried a bowling game on the Nintendo Wii with my nephew, but I wasn't very good.","phrases":[{"en":"Not very often","meaning":"Only sometimes, rather than regularly."}],"question":"Do you play any games?","html":"<strong class=\"key-phrase\">Not very often</strong> now. I sometimes play tennis with my brother-in-law. Recently, I also tried a bowling game on the Nintendo Wii with my nephew, but I wasn&#x27;t very good."},{"text":"Children often learn games from other children. That is how I learned chess: a friend at primary school explained the rules and showed me how to play.","phrases":[{"en":"the rules","meaning":"The instructions that tell you how a game works."}],"question":"How do people learn to play games in your country?","html":"Children often learn games from other children. That is how I learned chess: a friend at primary school explained <strong class=\"key-phrase\">the rules</strong> and showed me how to play."},{"text":"Yes, especially for children. Playing games can help them think, use their imagination and learn to work with other people. So games can be useful as well as enjoyable.","phrases":[{"en":"imagination","meaning":"The ability to form new ideas or pictures in your mind."}],"question":"Do you think it's important for people to play games?","html":"Yes, especially for children. Playing games can help them think, use their <strong class=\"key-phrase\">imagination</strong> and learn to work with other people. So games can be useful as well as enjoyable."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-033-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-033-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-033-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-033-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Games children and adults play","prompt":"Do you enjoy playing games?\nWhat kind of games do children play in your country?\nDo you think adults should play games?\nWhat kinds of games were popular when you were younger?","answer":"Q: Do you enjoy playing games?\nA: Yes, particularly strategy and word games. They&#x27;re entertaining but also require concentration, so they provide <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a healthy mental challenge</strong>.\n\nQ: What kind of games do children play in your country?\nA: Children play mobile games, football, hide-and-seek and a variety of classroom games. Digital games are more visible now, but physical games remain important for <strong class=\"key-phrase\">social and motor skills</strong>.\n\nQ: Do you think adults should play games?\nA: Certainly, provided gaming doesn&#x27;t replace work, exercise or relationships. Games can reduce stress and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">keep the mind active</strong>, so they&#x27;re not <strong class=\"key-phrase\">only for children</strong>.\n\nQ: What kinds of games were popular when you were younger?\nA: When I was younger, outdoor games and simple board games were common. Children had fewer devices, so entertainment depended more on imagination and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">face-to-face interaction</strong>.","topic":"Games","phrases":[{"en":"a healthy mental challenge","context":"Q: Do you enjoy playing games?\nA: Yes, particularly strategy and word games. They're entertaining but also require concentration, so they provide a healthy mental challenge."},{"en":"social and motor skills","context":"Q: What kind of games do children play in your country?\nA: Children play mobile games, football, hide-and-seek and a variety of classroom games. Digital games are more visible now, but physical games remain important for social and motor skills."},{"en":"keep the mind active","context":"Q: Do you think adults should play games?\nA: Certainly, provided gaming doesn't replace work, exercise or relationships. Games can reduce stress and keep the mind active, so they're not only for children."},{"en":"only for children","context":"Q: Do you think adults should play games?\nA: Certainly, provided gaming doesn't replace work, exercise or relationships. Games can reduce stress and keep the mind active, so they're not only for children."},{"en":"face-to-face interaction","context":"Q: What kinds of games were popular when you were younger?\nA: When I was younger, outdoor games and simple board games were common. Children had fewer devices, so entertainment depended more on imagination and face-to-face interaction."}],"subtype":"Part 1","summary":"Games","visual":null,"id":"speaking-part-1-034","_displayNo":"#033","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-034-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-034-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-034-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-034-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"Yes, I especially enjoy strategy games and word games. They are fun, but I also have to think carefully and pay attention, which gives my mind some exercise.","phrases":[{"en":"pay attention","meaning":"Listen, watch or think carefully about something."}],"question":"Do you enjoy playing games?","html":"Yes, I especially enjoy strategy games and word games. They are fun, but I also have to think carefully and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">pay attention</strong>, which gives my mind some exercise."},{"text":"Children play phone games, football, hide-and-seek and games at school. Phone games are common now, but active games still help children learn to move well and play with others.","phrases":[{"en":"active games","meaning":"Games that involve moving your body."}],"question":"What kind of games do children play in your country?","html":"Children play phone games, football, hide-and-seek and games at school. Phone games are common now, but <strong class=\"key-phrase\">active games</strong> still help children learn to move well and play with others."},{"text":"Yes, as long as games leave enough time for work, exercise and relationships. They can help adults relax and keep their minds busy, so they are not just for children.","phrases":[{"en":"as long as","meaning":"On the condition that something is true."}],"question":"Do you think adults should play games?","html":"Yes, <strong class=\"key-phrase\">as long as</strong> games leave enough time for work, exercise and relationships. They can help adults relax and keep their minds busy, so they are not just for children."},{"text":"Outdoor games and simple board games were popular when I was younger. We had fewer electronic devices, so we used our imagination more and played with other children in person.","phrases":[{"en":"electronic devices","meaning":"Equipment such as phones, tablets and computers."}],"question":"What kinds of games were popular when you were younger?","html":"Outdoor games and simple board games were popular when I was younger. We had fewer <strong class=\"key-phrase\">electronic devices</strong>, so we used our imagination more and played with other children in person."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-034-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-034-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-034-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-034-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Your health and health concerns in your country","prompt":"Is your health important to you?\nWhat do you do to improve your health?\nWhat is a major health concern in your country?\nWhat can be done about it?","answer":"Q: Is your health important to you?\nA: Yes, because health affects energy, concentration and independence. It&#x27;s easy to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">take it for granted</strong> until a problem appears, so prevention is <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a worthwhile investment</strong>.\n\nQ: What do you do to improve your health?\nA: I exercise several times a week, sleep consistently and try to eat mostly unprocessed food. None of these habits is dramatic, but together they <strong class=\"key-phrase\">make a noticeable difference</strong>.\n\nQ: What is a major health concern in your country?\nA: I&#x27;d say lifestyle-related conditions such as obesity, diabetes and stress are growing concerns. They develop gradually, which means public education and early screening should <strong class=\"key-phrase\">play a central role</strong>.\n\nQ: What can be done about it?\nA: Governments can improve preventive care, safe public spaces and nutrition education, while individuals need realistic habits they can maintain. In the end, I think it&#x27;s <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a shared responsibility</strong>.","topic":"Health & Fitness","phrases":[{"en":"take it for granted","context":"Q: Is your health important to you?\nA: Yes, because health affects energy, concentration and independence. It's easy to take it for granted until a problem appears, so prevention is a worthwhile investment."},{"en":"a worthwhile investment","context":"Q: Is your health important to you?\nA: Yes, because health affects energy, concentration and independence. It's easy to take it for granted until a problem appears, so prevention is a worthwhile investment."},{"en":"make a noticeable difference","context":"Q: What do you do to improve your health?\nA: I exercise several times a week, sleep consistently and try to eat mostly unprocessed food. None of these habits is dramatic, but together they make a noticeable difference."},{"en":"play a central role","context":"Q: What is a major health concern in your country?\nA: I'd say lifestyle-related conditions such as obesity, diabetes and stress are growing concerns. They develop gradually, which means public education and early screening should play a central role."},{"en":"a shared responsibility","context":"Q: What can be done about it?\nA: Governments can improve preventive care, safe public spaces and nutrition education, while individuals need realistic habits they can maintain. In the end, I think it's a shared responsibility."}],"subtype":"Part 1","summary":"Health & Fitness","visual":null,"id":"speaking-part-1-035","_displayNo":"#034","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-035-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-035-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-035-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-035-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"Yes, very important. Good health helps me feel energetic, focus and do things without help. I think it is better to look after it before problems appear.","phrases":[{"en":"energetic","meaning":"Having plenty of energy to do things."}],"question":"Is your health important to you?","html":"Yes, very important. Good health helps me feel <strong class=\"key-phrase\">energetic</strong>, focus and do things without help. I think it is better to look after it before problems appear."},{"text":"I exercise several times a week, keep regular sleeping habits and try to eat mostly fresh, simple food. These small habits work together to help me feel healthier.","phrases":[{"en":"sleeping habits","meaning":"Your usual patterns of going to sleep and resting."}],"question":"What do you do to improve your health?","html":"I exercise several times a week, keep regular <strong class=\"key-phrase\">sleeping habits</strong> and try to eat mostly fresh, simple food. These small habits work together to help me feel healthier."},{"text":"I think obesity, diabetes and stress are important concerns linked to people's lifestyles. These problems can develop slowly, so people need clear information and health checks before things get worse.","phrases":[{"en":"health checks","meaning":"Examinations to find out whether someone has a health problem."}],"question":"What is a major health concern in your country?","html":"I think obesity, diabetes and stress are important concerns linked to people&#x27;s lifestyles. These problems can develop slowly, so people need clear information and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">health checks</strong> before things get worse."},{"text":"Governments can provide better health services, safe places to exercise and advice about food. People also need healthy habits they can keep. I think both sides have a part to play.","phrases":[{"en":"a part to play","meaning":"A role or responsibility in something."}],"question":"What can be done about it?","html":"Governments can provide better health services, safe places to exercise and advice about food. People also need healthy habits they can keep. I think both sides have <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a part to play</strong>."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-035-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-035-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-035-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-035-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"The exercise you do and why it matters","prompt":"What kind of exercise do you do regularly?\nWhat kind of exercise do you enjoy least?\nWhy is exercise good for health?\nWhat kind of exercise would you suggest to someone who is very unfit?","answer":"Q: What kind of exercise do you do regularly?\nA: I do strength training and brisk walking several times a week. The combination improves fitness without requiring specialised facilities and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">fits naturally into my routine</strong>.\n\nQ: What kind of exercise do you enjoy least?\nA: I enjoy long-distance running least because repetitive impact can be uncomfortable. I prefer exercise that combines strength, mobility and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">steady progress</strong>.\n\nQ: Why is exercise good for health?\nA: Exercise strengthens the heart and muscles, improves sleep and helps regulate stress. It&#x27;s also good for long-term independence, which is often <strong class=\"key-phrase\">more important than appearance</strong>.\n\nQ: What kind of exercise would you suggest to someone who is very unfit?\nA: I&#x27;d suggest daily walking and simple body-weight exercises. They&#x27;re low-cost, easy to adjust and allow an unfit person to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">build confidence gradually</strong>.","topic":"Health & Fitness","phrases":[{"en":"fits naturally into my routine","context":"Q: What kind of exercise do you do regularly?\nA: I do strength training and brisk walking several times a week. The combination improves fitness without requiring specialised facilities and fits naturally into my routine."},{"en":"steady progress","context":"Q: What kind of exercise do you enjoy least?\nA: I enjoy long-distance running least because repetitive impact can be uncomfortable. I prefer exercise that combines strength, mobility and steady progress."},{"en":"more important than appearance","context":"Q: Why is exercise good for health?\nA: Exercise strengthens the heart and muscles, improves sleep and helps regulate stress. It's also good for long-term independence, which is often more important than appearance."},{"en":"build confidence gradually","context":"Q: What kind of exercise would you suggest to someone who is very unfit?\nA: I'd suggest daily walking and simple body-weight exercises. They're low-cost, easy to adjust and allow an unfit person to build confidence gradually."}],"subtype":"Part 1","summary":"Health & Fitness","visual":null,"id":"speaking-part-1-036","_displayNo":"#035","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-036-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-036-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-036-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-036-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"I lift weights and walk quickly several times a week. Together, these activities help me stay fit, and I can fit them into my normal schedule without needing special facilities for every session.","phrases":[{"en":"fit them into","meaning":"Find time for them in a schedule."}],"question":"What kind of exercise do you do regularly?","html":"I lift weights and walk quickly several times a week. Together, these activities help me stay fit, and I can <strong class=\"key-phrase\">fit them into</strong> my normal schedule without needing special facilities for every session."},{"text":"I like long-distance running least because the repeated movement can feel uncomfortable. I prefer activities that build strength, help me move better and let me improve gradually.","phrases":[{"en":"gradually","meaning":"Slowly, through small changes over time."}],"question":"What kind of exercise do you enjoy least?","html":"I like long-distance running least because the repeated movement can feel uncomfortable. I prefer activities that build strength, help me move better and let me improve <strong class=\"key-phrase\">gradually</strong>."},{"text":"Exercise helps the heart and muscles, improves sleep and makes stress easier to manage. It can also help us keep doing everyday things as we get older, which matters more than appearance.","phrases":[{"en":"appearance","meaning":"The way someone or something looks."}],"question":"Why is exercise good for health?","html":"Exercise helps the heart and muscles, improves sleep and makes stress easier to manage. It can also help us keep doing everyday things as we get older, which matters more than <strong class=\"key-phrase\">appearance</strong>."},{"text":"I'd suggest walking every day and doing simple exercises using their own body weight. These are cheap and can be made easier or harder, helping the person improve and feel more confident.","phrases":[{"en":"body weight","meaning":"The weight of your own body used as resistance in exercise."}],"question":"What kind of exercise would you suggest to someone who is very unfit?","html":"I&#x27;d suggest walking every day and doing simple exercises using their own <strong class=\"key-phrase\">body weight</strong>. These are cheap and can be made easier or harder, helping the person improve and feel more confident."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-036-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-036-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-036-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-036-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Your hobbies and how you spend spare time","prompt":"Do you have any hobbies?\nWhat are some of your hobbies?\nWhat do you usually do in your spare time?\nDo you prefer to stay alone or with your friends?","answer":"Q: Do you have any hobbies?\nA: Yes, I&#x27;ve got a few. I enjoy reading, I do some strength training at the gym, and I&#x27;m learning Spanish at the moment too. Having a few different interests gives me <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a healthy outlet</strong> outside work.\n\nQ: What are some of your hobbies?\nA: Reading&#x27;s probably my favourite — I try to read a little most evenings. Strength training gives me something to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">work towards</strong>, and learning a language keeps my brain active in a completely different way.\n\nQ: What do you usually do in your spare time?\nA: I usually read, exercise or meet up with a friend for coffee. I try to spend my free time doing something worthwhile rather than just <strong class=\"key-phrase\">scrolling without purpose</strong>.\n\nQ: Do you prefer to stay alone or with your friends?\nA: A bit of both, really. Reading and training on my own help me focus, but I also make time for friends so I don&#x27;t end up too isolated — I suppose I just try to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">strike a balance</strong>.","topic":"Hobbies","phrases":[{"en":"a healthy outlet","context":"Q: Do you have any hobbies?\nA: Yes, I've got a few. I enjoy reading, I do some strength training at the gym, and I'm learning Spanish at the moment too. Having a few different interests gives me a healthy outlet outside work."},{"en":"work towards","context":"Q: What are some of your hobbies?\nA: Reading's probably my favourite — I try to read a little most evenings. Strength training gives me something to work towards, and learning a language keeps my brain active in a completely different way."},{"en":"scrolling without purpose","context":"Q: What do you usually do in your spare time?\nA: I usually read, exercise or meet up with a friend for coffee. I try to spend my free time doing something worthwhile rather than just scrolling without purpose."},{"en":"strike a balance","context":"Q: Do you prefer to stay alone or with your friends?\nA: A bit of both, really. Reading and training on my own help me focus, but I also make time for friends so I don't end up too isolated — I suppose I just try to strike a balance."}],"subtype":"Part 1","summary":"Hobbies","visual":null,"id":"speaking-part-1-037","_displayNo":"#036","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-037-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-037-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-037-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-037-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"Yes, I enjoy reading, lifting weights at the gym and learning Spanish. Having different interests gives me enjoyable things to do and helps me relax when I'm not working.","phrases":[{"en":"interests","meaning":"Activities or subjects that you enjoy learning about or doing."}],"question":"Do you have any hobbies?","html":"Yes, I enjoy reading, lifting weights at the gym and learning Spanish. Having different <strong class=\"key-phrase\">interests</strong> gives me enjoyable things to do and helps me relax when I&#x27;m not working."},{"text":"Reading is probably my favourite, and I read most evenings. I also enjoy getting stronger at the gym, while learning a language gives my mind a different kind of activity.","phrases":[{"en":"getting stronger","meaning":"Becoming able to use more physical strength."}],"question":"What are some of your hobbies?","html":"Reading is probably my favourite, and I read most evenings. I also enjoy <strong class=\"key-phrase\">getting stronger</strong> at the gym, while learning a language gives my mind a different kind of activity."},{"text":"I usually read, exercise or have coffee with a friend. I like using my free time for something useful or enjoyable instead of looking through my phone without a reason.","phrases":[{"en":"free time","meaning":"Time when you do not have to work or study."}],"question":"What do you usually do in your spare time?","html":"I usually read, exercise or have coffee with a friend. I like using my <strong class=\"key-phrase\">free time</strong> for something useful or enjoyable instead of looking through my phone without a reason."},{"text":"I enjoy both. Reading and exercising alone help me focus, but I also spend time with friends. I try to have enough quiet time without becoming too separated from other people.","phrases":[{"en":"separated from","meaning":"Away from or not closely connected with someone."}],"question":"Do you prefer to stay alone or with your friends?","html":"I enjoy both. Reading and exercising alone help me focus, but I also spend time with friends. I try to have enough quiet time without becoming too <strong class=\"key-phrase\">separated from</strong> other people."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-037-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-037-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-037-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-037-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"A spare-time activity and how long you have done it","prompt":"What do you do in your spare time?\nHow long have you been interested in this activity?\nDo you do this alone or with other people?\nHow much time do you spend doing this activity?","answer":"Q: What do you do in your spare time?\nA: <strong class=\"key-phrase\">In my spare time</strong> I usually train at the gym, read or go for a quiet walk. I prefer activities that leave me feeling refreshed rather than just filling the time.\n\nQ: How long have you been interested in this activity?\nA: I&#x27;ve been strength training for several years now. I started just to get fit, but tracking small improvements is what&#x27;s made it <strong class=\"key-phrase\">personally rewarding</strong>.\n\nQ: Do you do this alone or with other people?\nA: I do some hobbies alone because being on my own helps me concentrate, but I also exercise or go out with friends. That combination lets me <strong class=\"key-phrase\">strike a healthy balance</strong> between independence and social contact.\n\nQ: How much time do you spend doing this activity?\nA: I spend roughly four or five hours a week on it. That&#x27;s enough to make progress without letting the hobby <strong class=\"key-phrase\">take over my schedule</strong>.","topic":"Hobbies","phrases":[{"en":"In my spare time","context":"Q: What do you do in your spare time?\nA: In my spare time I usually train at the gym, read or go for a quiet walk. I prefer activities that leave me feeling refreshed rather than just filling the time."},{"en":"personally rewarding","context":"Q: How long have you been interested in this activity?\nA: I've been strength training for several years now. I started just to get fit, but tracking small improvements is what's made it personally rewarding."},{"en":"strike a healthy balance","context":"Q: Do you do this alone or with other people?\nA: I do some hobbies alone because being on my own helps me concentrate, but I also exercise or go out with friends. That combination lets me strike a healthy balance between independence and social contact."},{"en":"take over my schedule","context":"Q: How much time do you spend doing this activity?\nA: I spend roughly four or five hours a week on it. That's enough to make progress without letting the hobby take over my schedule."}],"subtype":"Part 1","summary":"Hobbies","visual":null,"id":"speaking-part-1-038","_displayNo":"#037","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-038-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-038-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-038-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-038-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"I usually go to the gym, read or take a quiet walk. I choose things that help me feel rested and ready for the next part of my day.","phrases":[{"en":"rested","meaning":"Feeling less tired after relaxing or sleeping."}],"question":"What do you do in your spare time?","html":"I usually go to the gym, read or take a quiet walk. I choose things that help me feel <strong class=\"key-phrase\">rested</strong> and ready for the next part of my day."},{"text":"I've been lifting weights for several years. At first, I just wanted to get fit. Now I enjoy seeing small improvements, which makes the activity feel worthwhile.","phrases":[{"en":"worthwhile","meaning":"Useful or enjoyable enough to deserve your time."}],"question":"How long have you been interested in this activity?","html":"I&#x27;ve been lifting weights for several years. At first, I just wanted to get fit. Now I enjoy seeing small improvements, which makes the activity feel <strong class=\"key-phrase\">worthwhile</strong>."},{"text":"I do some hobbies alone because I can concentrate better. I also exercise or go out with friends, so I get both time to myself and time with other people.","phrases":[{"en":"time to myself","meaning":"Time spent alone doing what I choose."}],"question":"Do you do this alone or with other people?","html":"I do some hobbies alone because I can concentrate better. I also exercise or go out with friends, so I get both <strong class=\"key-phrase\">time to myself</strong> and time with other people."},{"text":"I spend about four or five hours a week on it. That gives me enough practice to improve while still leaving time for my other responsibilities.","phrases":[{"en":"responsibilities","meaning":"Things you need to do or take care of."}],"question":"How much time do you spend doing this activity?","html":"I spend about four or five hours a week on it. That gives me enough practice to improve while still leaving time for my other <strong class=\"key-phrase\">responsibilities</strong>."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-038-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-038-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-038-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-038-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Where you live and what you like about it","prompt":"How long have you lived there?\nWhat do you like about living there?\nWhat sort of accommodation would you most like to live in?","answer":"Q: How long have you lived there?\nA: I&#x27;ve lived there for about five years. It&#x27;s the first house that I&#x27;ve owned; before that I was <strong class=\"key-phrase\">renting an apartment</strong>.\n\nQ: What do you like about living there?\nA: I like living there because I think the house <strong class=\"key-phrase\">reflects my personality</strong>: I decorated it myself, I chose all the furniture, and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">everything is where I want it to be</strong>.\n\nQ: What sort of accommodation would you most like to live in?\nA: <strong class=\"key-phrase\">If I could</strong>, I&#x27;d buy a bigger house near a beach or in the mountains, preferably somewhere <strong class=\"key-phrase\">with a warm climate</strong>.","topic":"Home & Accommodation","phrases":[{"en":"renting an apartment","context":"Q: How long have you lived there?\nA: I've lived there for about five years. It's the first house that I've owned; before that I was renting an apartment."},{"en":"reflects my personality","context":"Q: What do you like about living there?\nA: I like living there because I think the house reflects my personality: I decorated it myself, I chose all the furniture, and everything is where I want it to be."},{"en":"everything is where I want it to be","context":"Q: What do you like about living there?\nA: I like living there because I think the house reflects my personality: I decorated it myself, I chose all the furniture, and everything is where I want it to be."},{"en":"If I could","context":"Q: What sort of accommodation would you most like to live in?\nA: If I could, I'd buy a bigger house near a beach or in the mountains, preferably somewhere with a warm climate."},{"en":"with a warm climate","context":"Q: What sort of accommodation would you most like to live in?\nA: If I could, I'd buy a bigger house near a beach or in the mountains, preferably somewhere with a warm climate."}],"subtype":"","summary":"Home & Accommodation","id":"speaking-part-1-039","_displayNo":"#038","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-039-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-039-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-039-q03.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"I've lived there for about five years. It is the first house I have owned. Before moving there, I lived in a flat that I rented.","phrases":[{"en":"rented","meaning":"Paid to use a home owned by someone else."}],"question":"How long have you lived there?","html":"I&#x27;ve lived there for about five years. It is the first house I have owned. Before moving there, I lived in a flat that I <strong class=\"key-phrase\">rented</strong>."},{"text":"I like it because it feels like my own place. I decorated it and chose the furniture myself, so everything looks the way I want it to.","phrases":[{"en":"decorated","meaning":"Chose colours and other things to make a room look attractive."}],"question":"What do you like about living there?","html":"I like it because it feels like my own place. I <strong class=\"key-phrase\">decorated</strong> it and chose the furniture myself, so everything looks the way I want it to."},{"text":"I'd love a bigger house near the beach or in the mountains if I could buy one. Ideally, it would be somewhere warm because I prefer that kind of weather.","phrases":[{"en":"Ideally","meaning":"In the best situation you can imagine."}],"question":"What sort of accommodation would you most like to live in?","html":"I&#x27;d love a bigger house near the beach or in the mountains if I could buy one. <strong class=\"key-phrase\">Ideally</strong>, it would be somewhere warm because I prefer that kind of weather."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-039-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-039-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-039-q03.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Your favourite room and what you would change","prompt":"Do you live in a house or an apartment?\nWhich is your favourite room in your home?\nWould you change anything about your home?\nWould you like to move to a different home in the future?","answer":"Q: Do you live in a house or an apartment?\nA: I live in a semi-detached house with three bedrooms in a suburb of Manchester. I&#x27;ve lived there for <strong class=\"key-phrase\">just over a year</strong>.\n\nQ: Which is your favourite room in your home?\nA: I don&#x27;t really have a favourite room. But <strong class=\"key-phrase\">if I had to choose</strong>, I&#x27;d say the living room because that&#x27;s where I go to sit and relax.\n\nQ: Would you change anything about your home?\nA: Yes, I&#x27;ve <strong class=\"key-phrase\">been meaning to</strong> redecorate it since I moved in last year. It needs a new kitchen, so that&#x27;s what I&#x27;d change first.\n\nQ: Would you like to move to a different home in the future?\nA: Yes, I&#x27;d definitely move again <strong class=\"key-phrase\">at some point</strong> if I could afford to. I&#x27;d like to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">live in the countryside</strong>, or maybe in a different city or country.","topic":"Home & Accommodation","phrases":[{"en":"just over a year","context":"Q: Do you live in a house or an apartment?\nA: I live in a semi-detached house with three bedrooms in a suburb of Manchester. I've lived there for just over a year."},{"en":"if I had to choose","context":"Q: Which is your favourite room in your home?\nA: I don't really have a favourite room. But if I had to choose, I'd say the living room because that's where I go to sit and relax."},{"en":"been meaning to","context":"Q: Would you change anything about your home?\nA: Yes, I've been meaning to redecorate it since I moved in last year. It needs a new kitchen, so that's what I'd change first."},{"en":"at some point","context":"Q: Would you like to move to a different home in the future?\nA: Yes, I'd definitely move again at some point if I could afford to. I'd like to live in the countryside, or maybe in a different city or country."},{"en":"live in the countryside","context":"Q: Would you like to move to a different home in the future?\nA: Yes, I'd definitely move again at some point if I could afford to. I'd like to live in the countryside, or maybe in a different city or country."}],"subtype":"","summary":"Home & Accommodation","id":"speaking-part-1-040","_displayNo":"#039","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-040-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-040-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-040-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-040-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"I live in a three-bedroom house outside central Manchester. It is joined to one other house, and I have lived there for a little over a year.","phrases":[{"en":"a little over","meaning":"Slightly more than a particular amount."}],"question":"Do you live in a house or an apartment?","html":"I live in a three-bedroom house outside central Manchester. It is joined to one other house, and I have lived there for <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a little over</strong> a year."},{"text":"I don't have a strong favourite, but I would probably choose the living room. It is the place where I sit down and relax, so I enjoy spending time there.","phrases":[{"en":"living room","meaning":"The room at home used for sitting and relaxing."}],"question":"Which is your favourite room in your home?","html":"I don&#x27;t have a strong favourite, but I would probably choose the <strong class=\"key-phrase\">living room</strong>. It is the place where I sit down and relax, so I enjoy spending time there."},{"text":"Yes, I want to decorate the house again. I have planned to do that since moving in last year. The kitchen needs replacing, so I would start there.","phrases":[{"en":"replacing","meaning":"Removing something and putting a new one in its place."}],"question":"Would you change anything about your home?","html":"Yes, I want to decorate the house again. I have planned to do that since moving in last year. The kitchen needs <strong class=\"key-phrase\">replacing</strong>, so I would start there."},{"text":"Yes, if I had enough money. I'd like to try living in the countryside, or perhaps another city or country, at some time in the future.","phrases":[{"en":"countryside","meaning":"Areas outside towns and cities, with fields or natural land."}],"question":"Would you like to move to a different home in the future?","html":"Yes, if I had enough money. I&#x27;d like to try living in the <strong class=\"key-phrase\">countryside</strong>, or perhaps another city or country, at some time in the future."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-040-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-040-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-040-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-040-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"House or apartment, and changes you would make","prompt":"Do you live in a house or an apartment?\nWhich room do you like most in your house?\nIs there anything about your house that you would like to change?","answer":"Q: Do you live in a house or an apartment?\nA: I live in a semi-detached house with three bedrooms and a small garden, which <strong class=\"key-phrase\">comes in handy</strong> when the weather&#x27;s nice.\n\nQ: Which room do you like most in your house?\nA: My favourite room is the kitchen because it <strong class=\"key-phrase\">looks out onto</strong> the back garden, and it&#x27;s on the side of the house that <strong class=\"key-phrase\">catches the afternoon sun</strong>.\n\nQ: Is there anything about your house that you would like to change?\nA: Well, it would be nice if it were <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a detached house</strong> so that we could have windows on the wall that we currently share with our neighbours.","topic":"Home & Accommodation","phrases":[{"en":"comes in handy","context":"Q: Do you live in a house or an apartment?\nA: I live in a semi-detached house with three bedrooms and a small garden, which comes in handy when the weather's nice."},{"en":"looks out onto","context":"Q: Which room do you like most in your house?\nA: My favourite room is the kitchen because it looks out onto the back garden, and it's on the side of the house that catches the afternoon sun."},{"en":"catches the afternoon sun","context":"Q: Which room do you like most in your house?\nA: My favourite room is the kitchen because it looks out onto the back garden, and it's on the side of the house that catches the afternoon sun."},{"en":"a detached house","context":"Q: Is there anything about your house that you would like to change?\nA: Well, it would be nice if it were a detached house so that we could have windows on the wall that we currently share with our neighbours."}],"subtype":"","summary":"Home & Accommodation","id":"speaking-part-1-041","_displayNo":"#040","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-041-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-041-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-041-q03.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"I live in a house that shares one wall with another house. It has three bedrooms and a small garden, which is useful when the weather is pleasant.","phrases":[{"en":"shares one wall","meaning":"Has a wall that also forms part of a neighbouring building."}],"question":"Do you live in a house or an apartment?","html":"I live in a house that <strong class=\"key-phrase\">shares one wall</strong> with another house. It has three bedrooms and a small garden, which is useful when the weather is pleasant."},{"text":"My favourite room is the kitchen. I can see the back garden from there, and the room gets sunlight in the afternoon, which makes it a pleasant place.","phrases":[{"en":"sunlight","meaning":"Natural light from the sun."}],"question":"Which room do you like most in your house?","html":"My favourite room is the kitchen. I can see the back garden from there, and the room gets <strong class=\"key-phrase\">sunlight</strong> in the afternoon, which makes it a pleasant place."},{"text":"I'd like the house to be separate from our neighbours' home. Then we could put windows in the wall we currently share, which would let in more light.","phrases":[{"en":"separate from","meaning":"Not joined or attached to something else."}],"question":"Is there anything about your house that you would like to change?","html":"I&#x27;d like the house to be <strong class=\"key-phrase\">separate from</strong> our neighbours&#x27; home. Then we could put windows in the wall we currently share, which would let in more light."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-041-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-041-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-041-q03.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"The town you come from","prompt":"Which town or city do you come from?\nWhat's the best thing about living there?\nIs there anything you don't like?\nWhich places would you recommend to a tourist?","answer":"Q: Which town or city do you come from?\nA: I come from Hanoi, a large city in northern Vietnam. It combines historic neighbourhoods with rapidly developing business districts, so it feels both traditional and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">constantly in motion</strong>.\n\nQ: What&#x27;s the best thing about living there?\nA: I think the best thing is the variety — there are parks, cafes, cultural sites and excellent food, all within a <strong class=\"key-phrase\">relatively small</strong> area. I also like that daily services are <strong class=\"key-phrase\">within easy reach</strong>.\n\nQ: Is there anything you don&#x27;t like?\nA: <strong class=\"key-phrase\">Traffic congestion</strong> and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">air pollution</strong> are the main drawbacks. At peak times, even a short journey can be exhausting, so the city needs a more reliable <strong class=\"key-phrase\">public transport network</strong>.\n\nQ: Which places would you recommend to a tourist?\nA: I&#x27;d recommend the Old Quarter, Hoan Kiem Lake and the Temple of Literature. Together they give visitors <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a balanced picture</strong> of the city&#x27;s history and everyday life.","topic":"Hometown","phrases":[{"en":"constantly in motion","context":"Q: Which town or city do you come from?\nA: I come from Hanoi, a large city in northern Vietnam. It combines historic neighbourhoods with rapidly developing business districts, so it feels both traditional and constantly in motion."},{"en":"relatively small","context":"Q: What's the best thing about living there?\nA: I think the best thing is the variety — there are parks, cafes, cultural sites and excellent food, all within a relatively small area. I also like that daily services are within easy reach."},{"en":"within easy reach","context":"Q: What's the best thing about living there?\nA: I think the best thing is the variety — there are parks, cafes, cultural sites and excellent food, all within a relatively small area. I also like that daily services are within easy reach."},{"en":"Traffic congestion","context":"Q: Is there anything you don't like?\nA: Traffic congestion and air pollution are the main drawbacks. At peak times, even a short journey can be exhausting, so the city needs a more reliable public transport network."},{"en":"air pollution","context":"Q: Is there anything you don't like?\nA: Traffic congestion and air pollution are the main drawbacks. At peak times, even a short journey can be exhausting, so the city needs a more reliable public transport network."},{"en":"public transport network","context":"Q: Is there anything you don't like?\nA: Traffic congestion and air pollution are the main drawbacks. At peak times, even a short journey can be exhausting, so the city needs a more reliable public transport network."},{"en":"a balanced picture","context":"Q: Which places would you recommend to a tourist?\nA: I'd recommend the Old Quarter, Hoan Kiem Lake and the Temple of Literature. Together they give visitors a balanced picture of the city's history and everyday life."}],"subtype":"Part 1","summary":"City","visual":null,"id":"speaking-part-1-007","_displayNo":"#041","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-007-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-007-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-007-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-007-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"I'm from Hanoi, a large city in the north of Vietnam. It has old neighbourhoods as well as new business areas, so it feels traditional but is also changing quickly.","phrases":[{"en":"as well as","meaning":"In addition to something else."}],"question":"Which town or city do you come from?","html":"I&#x27;m from Hanoi, a large city in the north of Vietnam. It has old neighbourhoods <strong class=\"key-phrase\">as well as</strong> new business areas, so it feels traditional but is also changing quickly."},{"text":"The best thing is the choice of things to do. There are parks, cafes, interesting cultural places and great food close together. Shops and other daily services are also easy to reach.","phrases":[{"en":"easy to reach","meaning":"Not difficult to get to."}],"question":"What's the best thing about living there?","html":"The best thing is the choice of things to do. There are parks, cafes, interesting cultural places and great food close together. Shops and other daily services are also <strong class=\"key-phrase\">easy to reach</strong>."},{"text":"I dislike the heavy traffic and dirty air. Travelling can be tiring during busy hours, even for a short distance. I think the city needs more dependable public transport.","phrases":[{"en":"heavy traffic","meaning":"A large number of vehicles on the roads."}],"question":"Is there anything you don't like?","html":"I dislike the <strong class=\"key-phrase\">heavy traffic</strong> and dirty air. Travelling can be tiring during busy hours, even for a short distance. I think the city needs more dependable public transport."},{"text":"I'd suggest the Old Quarter, Hoan Kiem Lake and the Temple of Literature. These places help visitors learn about Hanoi's history and see what daily life in the city is like.","phrases":[{"en":"daily life","meaning":"The usual activities and experiences of each day."}],"question":"Which places would you recommend to a tourist?","html":"I&#x27;d suggest the Old Quarter, Hoan Kiem Lake and the Temple of Literature. These places help visitors learn about Hanoi&#x27;s history and see what <strong class=\"key-phrase\">daily life</strong> in the city is like."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-007-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-007-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-007-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-007-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Your hometown and whether you would move","prompt":"Where are you from?\nDo you like your hometown?\nWould you prefer to live somewhere else?\nDo you think your hometown is a good place for young people?","answer":"Q: Where are you from?\nA: I&#x27;m from Manchester, which is a city in the <strong class=\"key-phrase\">north west of England</strong>.\n\nQ: Do you like your hometown?\nA: Yes, I like living in Manchester because it&#x27;s where most of my friends live, and because there are <strong class=\"key-phrase\">plenty of things to do</strong> there. The only thing I don&#x27;t like is the weather.\n\nQ: Would you prefer to live somewhere else?\nA: For the moment I&#x27;m happy living here, but <strong class=\"key-phrase\">at some point</strong> I&#x27;d like to live in a country with a warmer climate, and I&#x27;d like to live near a beach!\n\nQ: Do you think your hometown is a good place for young people?\nA: Yes, Manchester has lots of things for young people, such as <strong class=\"key-phrase\">sports facilities</strong>, music and cinemas.","topic":"Hometown","phrases":[{"en":"north west of England","context":"Q: Where are you from?\nA: I'm from Manchester, which is a city in the north west of England."},{"en":"plenty of things to do","context":"Q: Do you like your hometown?\nA: Yes, I like living in Manchester because it's where most of my friends live, and because there are plenty of things to do there. The only thing I don't like is the weather."},{"en":"at some point","context":"Q: Would you prefer to live somewhere else?\nA: For the moment I'm happy living here, but at some point I'd like to live in a country with a warmer climate, and I'd like to live near a beach!"},{"en":"sports facilities","context":"Q: Do you think your hometown is a good place for young people?\nA: Yes, Manchester has lots of things for young people, such as sports facilities, music and cinemas."}],"subtype":"","summary":"Hometown","id":"speaking-part-1-042","_displayNo":"#042","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-042-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-042-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-042-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-042-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"I'm from Manchester, a city in the north-west of England. That is my hometown, and it is the place I think of when someone asks where I'm from.","phrases":[{"en":"hometown","meaning":"The town or city you come from."}],"question":"Where are you from?","html":"I&#x27;m from Manchester, a city in the north-west of England. That is my <strong class=\"key-phrase\">hometown</strong>, and it is the place I think of when someone asks where I&#x27;m from."},{"text":"Yes, I enjoy living there because most of my friends are nearby and there are many things to do. The weather is the only part I don't really like.","phrases":[{"en":"nearby","meaning":"Not far away."}],"question":"Do you like your hometown?","html":"Yes, I enjoy living there because most of my friends are <strong class=\"key-phrase\">nearby</strong> and there are many things to do. The weather is the only part I don&#x27;t really like."},{"text":"I'm happy here for now, but I'd like to live somewhere warmer in the future. A place near a beach would be especially nice because I like that idea.","phrases":[{"en":"for now","meaning":"At the present time, even if things may change later."}],"question":"Would you prefer to live somewhere else?","html":"I&#x27;m happy here <strong class=\"key-phrase\">for now</strong>, but I&#x27;d like to live somewhere warmer in the future. A place near a beach would be especially nice because I like that idea."},{"text":"Yes, I think it is. Manchester has places to play sport, enjoy music and watch films. Young people have plenty of different activities to choose from.","phrases":[{"en":"plenty of","meaning":"A large or more than enough amount of something."}],"question":"Do you think your hometown is a good place for young people?","html":"Yes, I think it is. Manchester has places to play sport, enjoy music and watch films. Young people have <strong class=\"key-phrase\">plenty of</strong> different activities to choose from."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-042-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-042-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-042-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-042-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Where you were born and how it has changed","prompt":"Describe a place where you were born?\nTell me about the main types of buildings there?\nHow have buildings in your hometown changed since you were a child?\nCan you describe your hometown?","answer":"Q: Describe a place where you were born?\nA: I was born in Hanoi, a historic city in northern Vietnam. It&#x27;s densely populated, but the lakes, old streets and mature trees give a lot of areas <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a distinctive atmosphere</strong>.\n\nQ: Tell me about the main types of buildings there?\nA: The city&#x27;s got a real mix — traditional houses, French colonial buildings, apartment blocks and modern offices. It&#x27;s more a case of different stages of development than <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a single architectural style</strong>.\n\nQ: How have buildings in your hometown changed since you were a child?\nA: There are a lot more high-rise apartments and commercial buildings now. The city&#x27;s gained some modern facilities, but some neighbourhoods have lost part of their <strong class=\"key-phrase\">original character</strong>.\n\nQ: Can you describe your hometown?\nA: Hanoi&#x27;s lively, culturally rich and sometimes a bit chaotic. It&#x27;s got great food and services, but the traffic and pollution <strong class=\"key-phrase\">place considerable pressure on</strong> daily life.","topic":"Hometown","phrases":[{"en":"a distinctive atmosphere","context":"Q: Describe a place where you were born?\nA: I was born in Hanoi, a historic city in northern Vietnam. It's densely populated, but the lakes, old streets and mature trees give a lot of areas a distinctive atmosphere."},{"en":"a single architectural style","context":"Q: Tell me about the main types of buildings there?\nA: The city's got a real mix — traditional houses, French colonial buildings, apartment blocks and modern offices. It's more a case of different stages of development than a single architectural style."},{"en":"original character","context":"Q: How have buildings in your hometown changed since you were a child?\nA: There are a lot more high-rise apartments and commercial buildings now. The city's gained some modern facilities, but some neighbourhoods have lost part of their original character."},{"en":"place considerable pressure on","context":"Q: Can you describe your hometown?\nA: Hanoi's lively, culturally rich and sometimes a bit chaotic. It's got great food and services, but the traffic and pollution place considerable pressure on daily life."}],"subtype":"Part 1","summary":"Hometown","visual":null,"id":"speaking-part-1-043","_displayNo":"#043","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-043-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-043-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-043-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-043-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"I was born in Hanoi, an old city in northern Vietnam. A lot of people live there, but its lakes, old streets and large trees make many areas feel special.","phrases":[{"en":"northern","meaning":"In the north of a country or region."}],"question":"Describe a place where you were born?","html":"I was born in Hanoi, an old city in <strong class=\"key-phrase\">northern</strong> Vietnam. A lot of people live there, but its lakes, old streets and large trees make many areas feel special."},{"text":"There are traditional houses, French-style old buildings, blocks of flats and modern offices. The city has developed at different times, so there is a mixture of building styles.","phrases":[{"en":"a mixture of","meaning":"Several different things together."}],"question":"Tell me about the main types of buildings there?","html":"There are traditional houses, French-style old buildings, blocks of flats and modern offices. The city has developed at different times, so there is <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a mixture of</strong> building styles."},{"text":"There are more tall flats and business buildings now. The city has better modern services, but some older neighbourhoods no longer have quite the same look and feeling.","phrases":[{"en":"neighbourhoods","meaning":"Areas of a town where people live."}],"question":"How have buildings in your hometown changed since you were a child?","html":"There are more tall flats and business buildings now. The city has better modern services, but some older <strong class=\"key-phrase\">neighbourhoods</strong> no longer have quite the same look and feeling."},{"text":"Hanoi is busy and full of culture, with good food and useful services. However, it can also feel crowded and confusing, and traffic and pollution make everyday life harder.","phrases":[{"en":"pollution","meaning":"Harmful substances or dirty air in the environment."}],"question":"Can you describe your hometown?","html":"Hanoi is busy and full of culture, with good food and useful services. However, it can also feel crowded and confusing, and traffic and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">pollution</strong> make everyday life harder."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-043-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-043-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-043-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-043-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Your hometown and its well-known places","prompt":"Where do you come from?\nWhere do you live?\nCan you tell me something about your hometown?\nCan you name some well-known scenic places in your city?","answer":"Q: Where do you come from?\nA: I come from Hanoi, Vietnam&#x27;s capital. It&#x27;s a really energetic city with a long history, a strong food culture, and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a pace of development</strong> that&#x27;s visible almost everywhere you look.\n\nQ: Where do you live?\nA: I live in Hanoi, in an urban district with easy access to shops and public services. It&#x27;s busy, but it&#x27;s convenient enough to make daily errands <strong class=\"key-phrase\">relatively straightforward</strong>.\n\nQ: Can you tell me something about your hometown?\nA: My hometown&#x27;s <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a city of contrasts</strong>: historic streets sit right next to modern districts, and quiet lakes are surrounded by really busy roads. That mixture is what gives Hanoi its character, I think.\n\nQ: Can you name some well-known scenic places in your city?\nA: Hoan Kiem Lake, the Old Quarter and West Lake are probably the best-known spots. They each show a different side of the city and they&#x27;re <strong class=\"key-phrase\">easy for visitors to explore</strong>.","topic":"Hometown","phrases":[{"en":"a pace of development","context":"Q: Where do you come from?\nA: I come from Hanoi, Vietnam's capital. It's a really energetic city with a long history, a strong food culture, and a pace of development that's visible almost everywhere you look."},{"en":"relatively straightforward","context":"Q: Where do you live?\nA: I live in Hanoi, in an urban district with easy access to shops and public services. It's busy, but it's convenient enough to make daily errands relatively straightforward."},{"en":"a city of contrasts","context":"Q: Can you tell me something about your hometown?\nA: My hometown's a city of contrasts: historic streets sit right next to modern districts, and quiet lakes are surrounded by really busy roads. That mixture is what gives Hanoi its character, I think."},{"en":"easy for visitors to explore","context":"Q: Can you name some well-known scenic places in your city?\nA: Hoan Kiem Lake, the Old Quarter and West Lake are probably the best-known spots. They each show a different side of the city and they're easy for visitors to explore."}],"subtype":"Part 1","summary":"Hometown","visual":null,"id":"speaking-part-1-044","_displayNo":"#044","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-044-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-044-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-044-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-044-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"I'm from Hanoi, the capital of Vietnam. It is a lively city with a long history and great food. Many parts of it are changing quickly as new buildings and businesses appear.","phrases":[{"en":"lively","meaning":"Full of energy and activity."}],"question":"Where do you come from?","html":"I&#x27;m from Hanoi, the capital of Vietnam. It is a <strong class=\"key-phrase\">lively</strong> city with a long history and great food. Many parts of it are changing quickly as new buildings and businesses appear."},{"text":"I live in a busy district of Hanoi. Shops and public services are close by, so although it can be crowded, doing everyday tasks is fairly easy.","phrases":[{"en":"close by","meaning":"Near where you are."}],"question":"Where do you live?","html":"I live in a busy district of Hanoi. Shops and public services are <strong class=\"key-phrase\">close by</strong>, so although it can be crowded, doing everyday tasks is fairly easy."},{"text":"Hanoi has both old streets and modern areas. There are peaceful lakes beside busy roads, too. I think these different sides of the city are what make it interesting.","phrases":[{"en":"peaceful","meaning":"Quiet and calm."}],"question":"Can you tell me something about your hometown?","html":"Hanoi has both old streets and modern areas. There are <strong class=\"key-phrase\">peaceful</strong> lakes beside busy roads, too. I think these different sides of the city are what make it interesting."},{"text":"Hoan Kiem Lake, the Old Quarter and West Lake are well-known places. They are easy for visitors to explore, and each gives a different impression of Hanoi.","phrases":[{"en":"explore","meaning":"Visit a place and learn about it by looking around."}],"question":"Can you name some well-known scenic places in your city?","html":"Hoan Kiem Lake, the Old Quarter and West Lake are well-known places. They are easy for visitors to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">explore</strong>, and each gives a different impression of Hanoi."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-044-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-044-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-044-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-044-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"How you use the internet and its advantages","prompt":"Do you use the internet much during the day?\nWhich website have you visited recently?\nWhat are some advantages of the internet?\nDo people in your country use the internet a lot?","answer":"Q: Do you use the internet much during the day?\nA: Yes, I&#x27;m on it throughout the day really — for work, communication and research. I try to use it deliberately though, because constant notifications can <strong class=\"key-phrase\">fragment my attention</strong>.\n\nQ: Which website have you visited recently?\nA: I recently visited an educational website to compare language-learning resources. I liked the clear structure, and the fact that the information was <strong class=\"key-phrase\">supported by practical examples</strong>.\n\nQ: What are some advantages of the internet?\nA: The internet gives people rapid <strong class=\"key-phrase\">access to information</strong>, services and communication. I&#x27;d say its greatest advantage is that it can <strong class=\"key-phrase\">lower the barrier to entry</strong> for education and business.\n\nQ: Do people in your country use the internet a lot?\nA: Yes, definitely, especially in the cities, where people rely on it for banking, shopping, entertainment and work. It&#x27;s pretty widespread now, although digital skills and good-quality access are still <strong class=\"key-phrase\">unevenly distributed</strong>.","topic":"Internet","phrases":[{"en":"fragment my attention","context":"Q: Do you use the internet much during the day?\nA: Yes, I'm on it throughout the day really — for work, communication and research. I try to use it deliberately though, because constant notifications can fragment my attention."},{"en":"supported by practical examples","context":"Q: Which website have you visited recently?\nA: I recently visited an educational website to compare language-learning resources. I liked the clear structure, and the fact that the information was supported by practical examples."},{"en":"access to information","context":"Q: What are some advantages of the internet?\nA: The internet gives people rapid access to information, services and communication. I'd say its greatest advantage is that it can lower the barrier to entry for education and business."},{"en":"lower the barrier to entry","context":"Q: What are some advantages of the internet?\nA: The internet gives people rapid access to information, services and communication. I'd say its greatest advantage is that it can lower the barrier to entry for education and business."},{"en":"unevenly distributed","context":"Q: Do people in your country use the internet a lot?\nA: Yes, definitely, especially in the cities, where people rely on it for banking, shopping, entertainment and work. It's pretty widespread now, although digital skills and good-quality access are still unevenly distributed."}],"subtype":"Part 1","summary":"Internet","visual":null,"id":"speaking-part-1-045","_displayNo":"#045","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-045-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-045-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-045-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-045-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"Yes, I use it throughout the day for work, messages and research. I try to have a clear purpose because too many alerts can make it difficult to focus.","phrases":[{"en":"a clear purpose","meaning":"A definite reason for doing something."}],"question":"Do you use the internet much during the day?","html":"Yes, I use it throughout the day for work, messages and research. I try to have <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a clear purpose</strong> because too many alerts can make it difficult to focus."},{"text":"I recently used an education website to compare materials for learning languages. It was easy to follow, and the examples helped me understand how I could use the information.","phrases":[{"en":"easy to follow","meaning":"Simple to understand or use."}],"question":"Which website have you visited recently?","html":"I recently used an education website to compare materials for learning languages. It was <strong class=\"key-phrase\">easy to follow</strong>, and the examples helped me understand how I could use the information."},{"text":"It helps people find information, use services and communicate quickly. One big benefit is that it makes education and starting a business more accessible to people who had fewer chances before.","phrases":[{"en":"accessible","meaning":"Easy for people to get or use."}],"question":"What are some advantages of the internet?","html":"It helps people find information, use services and communicate quickly. One big benefit is that it makes education and starting a business more <strong class=\"key-phrase\">accessible</strong> to people who had fewer chances before."},{"text":"Yes, especially in cities. People use it for shopping, banking, work and entertainment. However, not everyone has the same level of internet skills or a good connection.","phrases":[{"en":"connection","meaning":"The link that allows a device to use the internet."}],"question":"Do people in your country use the internet a lot?","html":"Yes, especially in cities. People use it for shopping, banking, work and entertainment. However, not everyone has the same level of internet skills or a good <strong class=\"key-phrase\">connection</strong>."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-045-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-045-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-045-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-045-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"What makes you laugh and why it matters","prompt":"What kinds of thing make you laugh?\nDo you like making other people laugh?\nDo you think it's important for people to laugh?\nIs laughing the same as feeling happy?","answer":"Q: What kinds of thing make you laugh?\nA: I laugh most when I&#x27;m with friends talking about funny things that have <strong class=\"key-phrase\">happened to</strong> us. I also like watching comedians and comedy films.\n\nQ: Do you like making other people laugh?\nA: Yes, it&#x27;s a nice feeling when you can <strong class=\"key-phrase\">make someone laugh</strong> because you can see that you&#x27;ve made them happy. It&#x27;s great to share a funny moment with someone.\n\nQ: Do you think it&#x27;s important for people to laugh?\nA: Yes, of course. It&#x27;s important to see the funny side of things; humour helps us not to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">take life too seriously</strong>. I think that laughter is good for our health.\n\nQ: Is laughing the same as feeling happy?\nA: It&#x27;s not exactly the same because you can be happy without laughing, and sometimes we laugh when something bad has happened; <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a sense of humour</strong> can help us to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">cope with difficult situations</strong>.","topic":"Laughing","phrases":[{"en":"happened to","context":"Q: What kinds of thing make you laugh?\nA: I laugh most when I'm with friends talking about funny things that have happened to us. I also like watching comedians and comedy films."},{"en":"make someone laugh","context":"Q: Do you like making other people laugh?\nA: Yes, it's a nice feeling when you can make someone laugh because you can see that you've made them happy. It's great to share a funny moment with someone."},{"en":"take life too seriously","context":"Q: Do you think it's important for people to laugh?\nA: Yes, of course. It's important to see the funny side of things; humour helps us not to take life too seriously. I think that laughter is good for our health."},{"en":"a sense of humour","context":"Q: Is laughing the same as feeling happy?\nA: It's not exactly the same because you can be happy without laughing, and sometimes we laugh when something bad has happened; a sense of humour can help us to cope with difficult situations."},{"en":"cope with difficult situations","context":"Q: Is laughing the same as feeling happy?\nA: It's not exactly the same because you can be happy without laughing, and sometimes we laugh when something bad has happened; a sense of humour can help us to cope with difficult situations."}],"subtype":"","summary":"Laughing","id":"speaking-part-1-047","_displayNo":"#046","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-047-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-047-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-047-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-047-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"Funny stories with friends make me laugh the most, especially when we talk about things that happened to us. I also enjoy watching comedians and funny films.","phrases":[{"en":"comedians","meaning":"People whose job is to make an audience laugh."}],"question":"What kinds of thing make you laugh?","html":"Funny stories with friends make me laugh the most, especially when we talk about things that happened to us. I also enjoy watching <strong class=\"key-phrase\">comedians</strong> and funny films."},{"text":"Yes, I enjoy it because it feels good to make someone happy. Sharing a joke or a funny moment can be a nice way to connect with another person.","phrases":[{"en":"connect with","meaning":"Build a friendly or understanding relationship with someone."}],"question":"Do you like making other people laugh?","html":"Yes, I enjoy it because it feels good to make someone happy. Sharing a joke or a funny moment can be a nice way to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">connect with</strong> another person."},{"text":"Yes, laughter helps us enjoy life and not worry about everything too much. Being able to find something funny can help us relax, and I think that is good for us.","phrases":[{"en":"relax","meaning":"Feel calmer and less worried."}],"question":"Do you think it's important for people to laugh?","html":"Yes, laughter helps us enjoy life and not worry about everything too much. Being able to find something funny can help us <strong class=\"key-phrase\">relax</strong>, and I think that is good for us."},{"text":"Not exactly. You can feel happy without laughing, and people sometimes laugh during difficult times. Humour can help us deal with problems even when we are not feeling very happy.","phrases":[{"en":"Humour","meaning":"The ability to find things funny or make people laugh."}],"question":"Is laughing the same as feeling happy?","html":"Not exactly. You can feel happy without laughing, and people sometimes laugh during difficult times. <strong class=\"key-phrase\">Humour</strong> can help us deal with problems even when we are not feeling very happy."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-047-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-047-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-047-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-047-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Using maps and asking for directions","prompt":"Do you ever use maps?\nWhen do people usually need to use a map?\nDo you prefer electronic or paper maps?\nDo you ever ask people for directions instead of using a map?","answer":"Q: Do you ever use maps?\nA: Yes. Whenever I go somewhere new, I <strong class=\"key-phrase\">plan my journey</strong> with the help of a map.\n\nQ: When do people usually need to use a map?\nA: I imagine that some people use a map every day if they travel to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">different places for work</strong>. Others might only use a map when they&#x27;re on holiday.\n\nQ: Do you prefer electronic or paper maps?\nA: I still prefer paper maps for a long journey; I like being able to open the map out on a table and see the <strong class=\"key-phrase\">full journey ahead</strong>.\n\nQ: Do you ever ask people for directions instead of using a map?\nA: Only if I&#x27;m really lost. Whenever I ask for directions, I <strong class=\"key-phrase\">find it difficult to</strong> remember what the person said. So I prefer to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">find my own way</strong>.","topic":"Maps","phrases":[{"en":"plan my journey","context":"Q: Do you ever use maps?\nA: Yes. Whenever I go somewhere new, I plan my journey with the help of a map."},{"en":"different places for work","context":"Q: When do people usually need to use a map?\nA: I imagine that some people use a map every day if they travel to different places for work. Others might only use a map when they're on holiday."},{"en":"full journey ahead","context":"Q: Do you prefer electronic or paper maps?\nA: I still prefer paper maps for a long journey; I like being able to open the map out on a table and see the full journey ahead."},{"en":"find it difficult to","context":"Q: Do you ever ask people for directions instead of using a map?\nA: Only if I'm really lost. Whenever I ask for directions, I find it difficult to remember what the person said. So I prefer to find my own way."},{"en":"find my own way","context":"Q: Do you ever ask people for directions instead of using a map?\nA: Only if I'm really lost. Whenever I ask for directions, I find it difficult to remember what the person said. So I prefer to find my own way."}],"subtype":"","summary":"Maps","id":"speaking-part-1-048","_displayNo":"#047","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-048-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-048-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-048-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-048-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"Yes, I use maps when I visit a place I don't know. Looking at a map before I leave helps me plan how to get there.","phrases":[{"en":"plan","meaning":"Decide in advance how to do something."}],"question":"Do you ever use maps?","html":"Yes, I use maps when I visit a place I don&#x27;t know. Looking at a map before I leave helps me <strong class=\"key-phrase\">plan</strong> how to get there."},{"text":"Some people need maps regularly because their work takes them to different places. Others mainly use them on holiday when they are somewhere new and need help finding the way.","phrases":[{"en":"finding the way","meaning":"Working out how to reach a place."}],"question":"When do people usually need to use a map?","html":"Some people need maps regularly because their work takes them to different places. Others mainly use them on holiday when they are somewhere new and need help <strong class=\"key-phrase\">finding the way</strong>."},{"text":"For a long trip, I prefer a paper map. I can spread it out on a table and look at the whole route at once, which I find useful.","phrases":[{"en":"route","meaning":"The way you follow to travel from one place to another."}],"question":"Do you prefer electronic or paper maps?","html":"For a long trip, I prefer a paper map. I can spread it out on a table and look at the whole <strong class=\"key-phrase\">route</strong> at once, which I find useful."},{"text":"Only when I'm really lost. I often forget spoken directions, so I usually prefer using a map and working out the route by myself.","phrases":[{"en":"lost","meaning":"Not knowing where you are or how to get somewhere."}],"question":"Do you ever ask people for directions instead of using a map?","html":"Only when I&#x27;m really <strong class=\"key-phrase\">lost</strong>. I often forget spoken directions, so I usually prefer using a map and working out the route by myself."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-048-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-048-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-048-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-048-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Studying mathematics and whether everyone needs it","prompt":"At what age did you start studying mathematics?\nDo you like mathematics?\nIs it necessary for everyone to learn mathematics?\nDo you prefer to use a calculator when doing mathematics?","answer":"Q: At what age did you start studying mathematics?\nA: I can&#x27;t exactly remember, but it was probably in my first year at primary school when I was 5 years old. I probably learned <strong class=\"key-phrase\">simple addition</strong> at that age.\n\nQ: Do you like mathematics?\nA: I don&#x27;t dislike maths, but I wouldn&#x27;t say that I&#x27;ve ever really liked the subject either. I&#x27;m happy to do <strong class=\"key-phrase\">simple calculations</strong>, but my brain can&#x27;t cope with the complex stuff!\n\nQ: Is it necessary for everyone to learn mathematics?\nA: Yes, I think it is. We all need <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a basic grounding in maths</strong> so that we can do daily tasks, like <strong class=\"key-phrase\">managing our money</strong>, working out bills, and so on.\n\nQ: Do you prefer to use a calculator when doing mathematics?\nA: It depends. I quite like <strong class=\"key-phrase\">exercising my brain</strong> with anything that&#x27;s easy enough, but I use the calculator on my phone for anything tricky.","topic":"Mathematics","phrases":[{"en":"simple addition","context":"Q: At what age did you start studying mathematics?\nA: I can't exactly remember, but it was probably in my first year at primary school when I was 5 years old. I probably learned simple addition at that age."},{"en":"simple calculations","context":"Q: Do you like mathematics?\nA: I don't dislike maths, but I wouldn't say that I've ever really liked the subject either. I'm happy to do simple calculations, but my brain can't cope with the complex stuff!"},{"en":"a basic grounding in maths","context":"Q: Is it necessary for everyone to learn mathematics?\nA: Yes, I think it is. We all need a basic grounding in maths so that we can do daily tasks, like managing our money, working out bills, and so on."},{"en":"managing our money","context":"Q: Is it necessary for everyone to learn mathematics?\nA: Yes, I think it is. We all need a basic grounding in maths so that we can do daily tasks, like managing our money, working out bills, and so on."},{"en":"exercising my brain","context":"Q: Do you prefer to use a calculator when doing mathematics?\nA: It depends. I quite like exercising my brain with anything that's easy enough, but I use the calculator on my phone for anything tricky."}],"subtype":"","summary":"Mathematics","id":"speaking-part-1-049","_displayNo":"#048","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-049-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-049-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-049-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-049-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"I don't remember exactly, but I probably started at primary school when I was five. At that age, I think we learned simple things such as adding numbers together.","phrases":[{"en":"adding","meaning":"Putting numbers together to find a total."}],"question":"At what age did you start studying mathematics?","html":"I don&#x27;t remember exactly, but I probably started at primary school when I was five. At that age, I think we learned simple things such as <strong class=\"key-phrase\">adding</strong> numbers together."},{"text":"I don't mind basic maths, but it has never been my favourite subject. I can do simple calculations, while more difficult maths is hard for me to understand.","phrases":[{"en":"calculations","meaning":"Ways of using numbers to find an answer."}],"question":"Do you like mathematics?","html":"I don&#x27;t mind basic maths, but it has never been my favourite subject. I can do simple <strong class=\"key-phrase\">calculations</strong>, while more difficult maths is hard for me to understand."},{"text":"Yes, everyone needs some basic maths. We use it in ordinary life, for example when we manage money, check a bill or work out how much something costs.","phrases":[{"en":"work out","meaning":"Find an answer by thinking or calculating."}],"question":"Is it necessary for everyone to learn mathematics?","html":"Yes, everyone needs some basic maths. We use it in ordinary life, for example when we manage money, check a bill or <strong class=\"key-phrase\">work out</strong> how much something costs."},{"text":"For easy sums, I like doing them in my head because it gives my brain some practice. If a calculation is more difficult, I use the calculator on my phone.","phrases":[{"en":"in my head","meaning":"By thinking, without writing or using a device."}],"question":"Do you prefer to use a calculator when doing mathematics?","html":"For easy sums, I like doing them <strong class=\"key-phrase\">in my head</strong> because it gives my brain some practice. If a calculation is more difficult, I use the calculator on my phone."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-049-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-049-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-049-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-049-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Museums you have visited and would like to visit","prompt":"Which museums have you visited recently?\nWhat did you enjoy seeing there?\nWhich famous museum would you like to visit?\nWhich collections would you particularly like to see there?","answer":"Q: Which museums have you visited recently?\nA: I recently visited the Vietnam Museum of Ethnology in Hanoi. It shows the cultures of different ethnic groups through objects, photos and reconstructed houses, so the whole visit&#x27;s <strong class=\"key-phrase\">highly informative</strong>.\n\nQ: What did you enjoy seeing there?\nA: I particularly enjoyed the traditional houses and everyday objects. They showed how climate, materials and local customs shape the way communities <strong class=\"key-phrase\">organise daily life</strong>.\n\nQ: Which famous museum would you like to visit?\nA: I&#x27;d love to visit the British Museum because its collection covers such an enormous span of history. Seeing the original objects would give me <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a more tangible connection</strong> with the past.\n\nQ: Which collections would you particularly like to see there?\nA: I&#x27;d be most interested in the ancient civilisations and the history of writing. Those collections show how ideas travelled and how societies <strong class=\"key-phrase\">influenced one another</strong>.","topic":"Museums","phrases":[{"en":"highly informative","context":"Q: Which museums have you visited recently?\nA: I recently visited the Vietnam Museum of Ethnology in Hanoi. It shows the cultures of different ethnic groups through objects, photos and reconstructed houses, so the whole visit's highly informative."},{"en":"organise daily life","context":"Q: What did you enjoy seeing there?\nA: I particularly enjoyed the traditional houses and everyday objects. They showed how climate, materials and local customs shape the way communities organise daily life."},{"en":"a more tangible connection","context":"Q: Which famous museum would you like to visit?\nA: I'd love to visit the British Museum because its collection covers such an enormous span of history. Seeing the original objects would give me a more tangible connection with the past."},{"en":"influenced one another","context":"Q: Which collections would you particularly like to see there?\nA: I'd be most interested in the ancient civilisations and the history of writing. Those collections show how ideas travelled and how societies influenced one another."}],"subtype":"Part 1","summary":"Museum","visual":null,"id":"speaking-part-1-050","_displayNo":"#049","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-050-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-050-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-050-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-050-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"I recently visited the Vietnam Museum of Ethnology in Hanoi. It has objects, photos and examples of traditional houses from different ethnic groups, so I learned a lot during the visit.","phrases":[{"en":"ethnic groups","meaning":"Groups of people who share a cultural background or traditions."}],"question":"Which museums have you visited recently?","html":"I recently visited the Vietnam Museum of Ethnology in Hanoi. It has objects, photos and examples of traditional houses from different <strong class=\"key-phrase\">ethnic groups</strong>, so I learned a lot during the visit."},{"text":"I liked the traditional houses and everyday objects most. They helped me see how weather, local materials and traditions affect the way different groups of people live.","phrases":[{"en":"local materials","meaning":"Things available in an area that people can use to make objects or buildings."}],"question":"What did you enjoy seeing there?","html":"I liked the traditional houses and everyday objects most. They helped me see how weather, <strong class=\"key-phrase\">local materials</strong> and traditions affect the way different groups of people live."},{"text":"I'd love to visit the British Museum because it has objects from so many periods of history. Seeing the real things would help me feel closer to the past.","phrases":[{"en":"periods of history","meaning":"Different times or ages in the past."}],"question":"Which famous museum would you like to visit?","html":"I&#x27;d love to visit the British Museum because it has objects from so many <strong class=\"key-phrase\">periods of history</strong>. Seeing the real things would help me feel closer to the past."},{"text":"I'd especially like to see objects from ancient societies and the history of writing. They can show how people shared ideas and learned from other societies.","phrases":[{"en":"ancient","meaning":"Belonging to a time very far in the past."}],"question":"Which collections would you particularly like to see there?","html":"I&#x27;d especially like to see objects from <strong class=\"key-phrase\">ancient</strong> societies and the history of writing. They can show how people shared ideas and learned from other societies."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-050-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-050-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-050-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-050-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"The music you listen to and going to concerts","prompt":"Do you like music?\nWhat kind of music did you listen to when you were young?\nWhen was the last time you went to a concert?\nWould you like to participate in a live music show?","answer":"Q: Do you like music?\nA: No, I don&#x27;t really like music, and I don&#x27;t listen to it. It&#x27;s <strong class=\"key-phrase\">not something that I&#x27;ve ever been interested in</strong>.\n\nQ: What kind of music did you listen to when you were young?\nA: I can&#x27;t remember listening to much music as a child either. I suppose I must have heard some traditional music at festivals or parties, but I didn&#x27;t <strong class=\"key-phrase\">take much notice of</strong> it.\n\nQ: When was the last time you went to a concert?\nA: I&#x27;ve never been to a music concert. Maybe I should try going to one; perhaps it would be interesting to see an orchestra playing <strong class=\"key-phrase\">classical music</strong>.\n\nQ: Would you like to participate in a live music show?\nA: No, definitely not. I don&#x27;t <strong class=\"key-phrase\">play a musical instrument</strong> and I don&#x27;t sing, so I can&#x27;t imagine that I&#x27;d ever find myself performing to an audience.","topic":"Music","phrases":[{"en":"not something that I've ever been interested in","context":"Q: Do you like music?\nA: No, I don't really like music, and I don't listen to it. It's not something that I've ever been interested in."},{"en":"take much notice of","context":"Q: What kind of music did you listen to when you were young?\nA: I can't remember listening to much music as a child either. I suppose I must have heard some traditional music at festivals or parties, but I didn't take much notice of it."},{"en":"classical music","context":"Q: When was the last time you went to a concert?\nA: I've never been to a music concert. Maybe I should try going to one; perhaps it would be interesting to see an orchestra playing classical music."},{"en":"play a musical instrument","context":"Q: Would you like to participate in a live music show?\nA: No, definitely not. I don't play a musical instrument and I don't sing, so I can't imagine that I'd ever find myself performing to an audience."}],"subtype":"","summary":"Music","id":"speaking-part-1-051","_displayNo":"#050","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-051-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-051-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-051-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-051-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"No, I'm not really interested in music. I don't usually listen to it, and it has never been an important hobby or part of my life.","phrases":[{"en":"interested in","meaning":"Wanting to know about or spend time doing something."}],"question":"Do you like music?","html":"No, I&#x27;m not really <strong class=\"key-phrase\">interested in</strong> music. I don&#x27;t usually listen to it, and it has never been an important hobby or part of my life."},{"text":"I don't remember listening to much music as a child. I probably heard traditional music at celebrations and parties, but I didn't pay much attention to it.","phrases":[{"en":"pay much attention","meaning":"Notice or think about something carefully."}],"question":"What kind of music did you listen to when you were young?","html":"I don&#x27;t remember listening to much music as a child. I probably heard traditional music at celebrations and parties, but I didn&#x27;t <strong class=\"key-phrase\">pay much attention</strong> to it."},{"text":"I've never been to a music concert. I might try one in the future, though. Watching an orchestra play classical music could be an interesting experience.","phrases":[{"en":"orchestra","meaning":"A large group of musicians who play instruments together."}],"question":"When was the last time you went to a concert?","html":"I&#x27;ve never been to a music concert. I might try one in the future, though. Watching an <strong class=\"key-phrase\">orchestra</strong> play classical music could be an interesting experience."},{"text":"No, I wouldn't want to perform. I don't sing or play an instrument, so I would not feel comfortable getting on a stage in front of other people.","phrases":[{"en":"perform","meaning":"Sing, act or play music for an audience."}],"question":"Would you like to participate in a live music show?","html":"No, I wouldn&#x27;t want to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">perform</strong>. I don&#x27;t sing or play an instrument, so I would not feel comfortable getting on a stage in front of other people."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-051-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-051-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-051-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-051-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Listening habits and how your taste has changed","prompt":"How often do you listen to music?\nHas the music you like changed since you were younger?\nDo you prefer listening to music alone or with other people?\nDo you listen to music while you are working or studying?","answer":"Q: How often do you listen to music?\nA: Pretty much daily, though it is usually <strong class=\"key-phrase\">on in the background</strong> rather than something I sit down for. The commute is when I actually pay attention to it.\n\nQ: Has the music you like changed since you were younger?\nA: Quite a lot, yes. As a teenager I mostly listened to whatever my friends were into, and I have <strong class=\"key-phrase\">drifted towards</strong> quieter things since then — acoustic stuff, a bit of jazz. I think my taste got narrower but deeper.\n\nQ: Do you prefer listening to music alone or with other people?\nA: Alone, definitely. Music is quite a private thing for me, and when other people are around I end up <strong class=\"key-phrase\">worrying about whether they like it</strong> instead of listening properly.\n\nQ: Do you listen to music while you are working or studying?\nA: Only if the work is routine. Anything that needs concentration and lyrics <strong class=\"key-phrase\">get in the way</strong>, so I either put on something instrumental or work in silence.","topic":"Music","phrases":[{"en":"on in the background","context":"Q: How often do you listen to music?\nA: Pretty much daily, though it is usually on in the background rather than something I sit down for. The commute is when I actually pay attention to it."},{"en":"drifted towards","context":"Q: Has the music you like changed since you were younger?\nA: Quite a lot, yes. As a teenager I mostly listened to whatever my friends were into, and I have drifted towards quieter things since then — acoustic stuff, a bit of jazz. I think my taste got narrower but deeper."},{"en":"worrying about whether they like it","context":"Q: Do you prefer listening to music alone or with other people?\nA: Alone, definitely. Music is quite a private thing for me, and when other people are around I end up worrying about whether they like it instead of listening properly."},{"en":"get in the way","context":"Q: Do you listen to music while you are working or studying?\nA: Only if the work is routine. Anything that needs concentration and lyrics get in the way, so I either put on something instrumental or work in silence."}],"subtype":"","summary":"Music","id":"speaking-part-1-052","_displayNo":"#051","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-052-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-052-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-052-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-052-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"I listen almost every day, usually while doing something else. I pay more attention to the music when I travel to and from work, because that is time I can really listen.","phrases":[{"en":"to and from work","meaning":"Going to your workplace and returning home."}],"question":"How often do you listen to music?","html":"I listen almost every day, usually while doing something else. I pay more attention to the music when I travel <strong class=\"key-phrase\">to and from work</strong>, because that is time I can really listen."},{"text":"Yes, quite a lot. As a teenager, I listened to the music my friends liked. Now I prefer quieter music, such as acoustic songs and some jazz, and know those styles better.","phrases":[{"en":"acoustic","meaning":"Using instruments whose sound is not produced electronically."}],"question":"Has the music you like changed since you were younger?","html":"Yes, quite a lot. As a teenager, I listened to the music my friends liked. Now I prefer quieter music, such as <strong class=\"key-phrase\">acoustic</strong> songs and some jazz, and know those styles better."},{"text":"I prefer listening alone. Music feels quite personal to me, and with other people I worry about whether they enjoy my choice instead of simply enjoying it myself.","phrases":[{"en":"personal","meaning":"Connected with your own feelings, taste or private life."}],"question":"Do you prefer listening to music alone or with other people?","html":"I prefer listening alone. Music feels quite <strong class=\"key-phrase\">personal</strong> to me, and with other people I worry about whether they enjoy my choice instead of simply enjoying it myself."},{"text":"Only when the task is simple and familiar. Words in songs can distract me when I need to think, so I choose music without singing or work with no music at all.","phrases":[{"en":"distract me","meaning":"Take my attention away from what I am doing."}],"question":"Do you listen to music while you are working or studying?","html":"Only when the task is simple and familiar. Words in songs can <strong class=\"key-phrase\">distract me</strong> when I need to think, so I choose music without singing or work with no music at all."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-052-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-052-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-052-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-052-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Instruments you enjoy and learning at school","prompt":"Which instruments do you like listening to most and why?\nHave you ever learned to play a musical instrument at school and why?\nDo you think children should learn to play a musical instrument at school?\nHow easy would it be to learn to play an instrument without a teacher?","answer":"Q: Which instruments do you like listening to most and why?\nA: I enjoy the piano and acoustic guitar most. Both can sound intimate or powerful, and they work across loads of musical styles without <strong class=\"key-phrase\">overwhelming the melody</strong>.\n\nQ: Have you ever learned to play a musical instrument at school and why?\nA: I had a few basic music lessons at school but never really got good at it. Even so, they taught me rhythm and showed me how much <strong class=\"key-phrase\">consistent practice</strong> a musician needs.\n\nQ: Do you think children should learn to play a musical instrument at school?\nA: Yes, at least at a basic level. It&#x27;s great for their listening, coordination and discipline, and it gives them <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a creative form of expression</strong> too.\n\nQ: How easy would it be to learn to play an instrument without a teacher?\nA: It&#x27;s possible with videos and apps, but a teacher can correct your technique before bad habits set in. Self-study works best when you&#x27;ve already got <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a clear practice plan</strong>.","topic":"Music","phrases":[{"en":"overwhelming the melody","context":"Q: Which instruments do you like listening to most and why?\nA: I enjoy the piano and acoustic guitar most. Both can sound intimate or powerful, and they work across loads of musical styles without overwhelming the melody."},{"en":"consistent practice","context":"Q: Have you ever learned to play a musical instrument at school and why?\nA: I had a few basic music lessons at school but never really got good at it. Even so, they taught me rhythm and showed me how much consistent practice a musician needs."},{"en":"a creative form of expression","context":"Q: Do you think children should learn to play a musical instrument at school?\nA: Yes, at least at a basic level. It's great for their listening, coordination and discipline, and it gives them a creative form of expression too."},{"en":"a clear practice plan","context":"Q: How easy would it be to learn to play an instrument without a teacher?\nA: It's possible with videos and apps, but a teacher can correct your technique before bad habits set in. Self-study works best when you've already got a clear practice plan."}],"subtype":"Part 1","summary":"Music","visual":null,"id":"speaking-part-1-053","_displayNo":"#052","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-053-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-053-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-053-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-053-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"I most enjoy piano and acoustic guitar. They can sound gentle or strong and fit many styles of music, while still allowing me to hear the tune clearly.","phrases":[{"en":"tune","meaning":"The main series of notes in a piece of music."}],"question":"Which instruments do you like listening to most and why?","html":"I most enjoy piano and acoustic guitar. They can sound gentle or strong and fit many styles of music, while still allowing me to hear the <strong class=\"key-phrase\">tune</strong> clearly."},{"text":"I had a few simple music lessons at school, but I never became very good. Still, I learned about rhythm and realised that musicians need to practise regularly.","phrases":[{"en":"rhythm","meaning":"The pattern of beats in music."}],"question":"Have you ever learned to play a musical instrument at school and why?","html":"I had a few simple music lessons at school, but I never became very good. Still, I learned about <strong class=\"key-phrase\">rhythm</strong> and realised that musicians need to practise regularly."},{"text":"Yes, I think they should learn the basics. Playing an instrument helps children listen carefully, control their movements and practise regularly. It also gives them a way to be creative.","phrases":[{"en":"creative","meaning":"Able to use imagination to make or express something."}],"question":"Do you think children should learn to play a musical instrument at school?","html":"Yes, I think they should learn the basics. Playing an instrument helps children listen carefully, control their movements and practise regularly. It also gives them a way to be <strong class=\"key-phrase\">creative</strong>."},{"text":"You can learn from videos and apps, but it may be harder without a teacher to correct mistakes. Learning alone works better if you have a clear plan for practice.","phrases":[{"en":"correct mistakes","meaning":"Show what is wrong and help make it right."}],"question":"How easy would it be to learn to play an instrument without a teacher?","html":"You can learn from videos and apps, but it may be harder without a teacher to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">correct mistakes</strong>. Learning alone works better if you have a clear plan for practice."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-053-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-053-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-053-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-053-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"How you were named and what names mean","prompt":"How did your parents choose your name?\nDoes your name have any special meaning?\nIs your name common or unusual in your country?\nIf you could change your name, would you?","answer":"Q: How did your parents choose your name?\nA: <strong class=\"key-phrase\">To be honest</strong>, I&#x27;m not sure how they chose it; I&#x27;ve never asked them. I suppose it was just a name that they both liked, and maybe they thought it suited me.\n\nQ: Does your name have any special meaning?\nA: It might do, but I don&#x27;t know what that meaning is; I&#x27;ve never <strong class=\"key-phrase\">looked it up</strong>. Maybe I&#x27;ll google it later today; you&#x27;ve <strong class=\"key-phrase\">made me curious to find out</strong>!\n\nQ: Is your name common or unusual in your country?\nA: Yes, it&#x27;s quite a common name. I remember that there were two other people with the <strong class=\"key-phrase\">same name as me</strong> in my class at school.\n\nQ: If you could change your name, would you?\nA: No, I definitely wouldn&#x27;t. My name is <strong class=\"key-phrase\">part of my identity</strong> now, and it would feel strange to suddenly change it. I don&#x27;t think my friends and family would like that either.","topic":"Names","phrases":[{"en":"To be honest","context":"Q: How did your parents choose your name?\nA: To be honest, I'm not sure how they chose it; I've never asked them. I suppose it was just a name that they both liked, and maybe they thought it suited me."},{"en":"looked it up","context":"Q: Does your name have any special meaning?\nA: It might do, but I don't know what that meaning is; I've never looked it up. Maybe I'll google it later today; you've made me curious to find out!"},{"en":"made me curious to find out","context":"Q: Does your name have any special meaning?\nA: It might do, but I don't know what that meaning is; I've never looked it up. Maybe I'll google it later today; you've made me curious to find out!"},{"en":"same name as me","context":"Q: Is your name common or unusual in your country?\nA: Yes, it's quite a common name. I remember that there were two other people with the same name as me in my class at school."},{"en":"part of my identity","context":"Q: If you could change your name, would you?\nA: No, I definitely wouldn't. My name is part of my identity now, and it would feel strange to suddenly change it. I don't think my friends and family would like that either."}],"subtype":"","summary":"Names","id":"speaking-part-1-054","_displayNo":"#053","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-054-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-054-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-054-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-054-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"I'm not sure because I've never asked my parents. I imagine they chose a name that they both liked and thought would be right for me.","phrases":[{"en":"imagine","meaning":"Think something is probably true without knowing for certain."}],"question":"How did your parents choose your name?","html":"I&#x27;m not sure because I&#x27;ve never asked my parents. I <strong class=\"key-phrase\">imagine</strong> they chose a name that they both liked and thought would be right for me."},{"text":"It might have a special meaning, but I haven't checked. I may search for it online later because this question has made me want to find out.","phrases":[{"en":"find out","meaning":"Discover or learn some information."}],"question":"Does your name have any special meaning?","html":"It might have a special meaning, but I haven&#x27;t checked. I may search for it online later because this question has made me want to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">find out</strong>."},{"text":"It is quite common. When I was at school, there were two other people in my class with the same name, so it wasn't unusual there.","phrases":[{"en":"common","meaning":"Happening often or found in many people or places."}],"question":"Is your name common or unusual in your country?","html":"It is quite <strong class=\"key-phrase\">common</strong>. When I was at school, there were two other people in my class with the same name, so it wasn&#x27;t unusual there."},{"text":"No, I wouldn't change it. My name feels like part of who I am, so a different one would seem strange. I don't think my family or friends would like it either.","phrases":[{"en":"part of who I am","meaning":"Something closely connected with my identity."}],"question":"If you could change your name, would you?","html":"No, I wouldn&#x27;t change it. My name feels like <strong class=\"key-phrase\">part of who I am</strong>, so a different one would seem strange. I don&#x27;t think my family or friends would like it either."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-054-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-054-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-054-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-054-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Knowing your neighbours, and problems with them","prompt":"How well do you know the people who live next door to you?\nHow often do you see them?\nWhat kinds of problem do people sometimes have with their neighbours?\nHow do you think neighbours can help each other?","answer":"Q: How well do you know the people who live next door to you?\nA: I <strong class=\"key-phrase\">know my neighbours quite well</strong>. They&#x27;re really nice people, and I always stop to talk whenever I see them.\n\nQ: How often do you see them?\nA: I see my neighbours at least <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a few times a week</strong>. We usually see each other when we&#x27;re leaving for work in the morning or coming home in the evening.\n\nQ: What kinds of problem do people sometimes have with their neighbours?\nA: I think the most common problem is probably noise. It&#x27;s difficult to live next to people who have a dog that barks at night, or who <strong class=\"key-phrase\">play loud music</strong>.\n\nQ: How do you think neighbours can help each other?\nA: Neighbours can do little things like watching your house if you go on holiday or <strong class=\"key-phrase\">taking a delivery</strong> if something arrives by post when you&#x27;re not at home. I think <strong class=\"key-phrase\">these little favours</strong> are a good way for neighbours to help each other.","topic":"Neighbours","phrases":[{"en":"know my neighbours quite well","context":"Q: How well do you know the people who live next door to you?\nA: I know my neighbours quite well. They're really nice people, and I always stop to talk whenever I see them."},{"en":"a few times a week","context":"Q: How often do you see them?\nA: I see my neighbours at least a few times a week. We usually see each other when we're leaving for work in the morning or coming home in the evening."},{"en":"play loud music","context":"Q: What kinds of problem do people sometimes have with their neighbours?\nA: I think the most common problem is probably noise. It's difficult to live next to people who have a dog that barks at night, or who play loud music."},{"en":"taking a delivery","context":"Q: How do you think neighbours can help each other?\nA: Neighbours can do little things like watching your house if you go on holiday or taking a delivery if something arrives by post when you're not at home. I think these little favours are a good way for neighbours to help each other."},{"en":"these little favours","context":"Q: How do you think neighbours can help each other?\nA: Neighbours can do little things like watching your house if you go on holiday or taking a delivery if something arrives by post when you're not at home. I think these little favours are a good way for neighbours to help each other."}],"subtype":"","summary":"Neighbours","id":"speaking-part-1-055","_displayNo":"#054","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-055-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-055-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-055-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-055-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"I know them quite well. They are friendly, and when I see them, I usually stop for a short conversation. We have a good relationship.","phrases":[{"en":"a good relationship","meaning":"A friendly connection in which people get along well."}],"question":"How well do you know the people who live next door to you?","html":"I know them quite well. They are friendly, and when I see them, I usually stop for a short conversation. We have <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a good relationship</strong>."},{"text":"I see them a few times a week, often when we leave for work in the morning or return in the evening. Those are the times we tend to meet outside.","phrases":[{"en":"tend to","meaning":"Usually or often do something."}],"question":"How often do you see them?","html":"I see them a few times a week, often when we leave for work in the morning or return in the evening. Those are the times we <strong class=\"key-phrase\">tend to</strong> meet outside."},{"text":"Noise is probably the most common problem. A dog barking at night or someone playing loud music can make it hard for the people next door to rest.","phrases":[{"en":"next door","meaning":"In the home immediately beside yours."}],"question":"What kinds of problem do people sometimes have with their neighbours?","html":"Noise is probably the most common problem. A dog barking at night or someone playing loud music can make it hard for the people <strong class=\"key-phrase\">next door</strong> to rest."},{"text":"They can check your home while you are away or accept a parcel when you are out. Small helpful actions like these make living near each other easier.","phrases":[{"en":"a parcel","meaning":"A package sent or delivered to someone."}],"question":"How do you think neighbours can help each other?","html":"They can check your home while you are away or accept <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a parcel</strong> when you are out. Small helpful actions like these make living near each other easier."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-055-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-055-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-055-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-055-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Where you get news and how reporting differs","prompt":"Where do you normally get news from?\nHow does news reporting in your country differ from reporting abroad?\nTell me about an interesting news item you have read or heard recently.\nAre you interested in the news, and what kind of news do you follow?","answer":"Q: Where do you normally get news from?\nA: I mainly get my news from a few reputable websites, and I&#x27;ve also signed up to some specialist newsletters. If a story&#x27;s really important, I&#x27;ll compare more than one source, because headlines alone don&#x27;t always give you <strong class=\"key-phrase\">the full picture</strong>.\n\nQ: How does news reporting in your country differ from reporting abroad?\nA: I&#x27;d say our media focuses more on local politics and social issues, whereas foreign news often looks at the same story from <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a completely different angle</strong>. Comparing the two actually helps me <strong class=\"key-phrase\">spot any bias</strong>.\n\nQ: Tell me about an interesting news item you have read or heard recently.\nA: I recently read about a new piece of medical technology that lets doctors detect diseases much earlier. What interested me most was how it showed research can have <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a direct practical benefit</strong> for everyday people.\n\nQ: Are you interested in the news, and what kind of news do you follow?\nA: Yes, I am, especially anything to do with science, education or major world events. I don&#x27;t try to follow every single update though, because constant exposure just creates noise rather than <strong class=\"key-phrase\">reliable understanding</strong>.","topic":"News","phrases":[{"en":"the full picture","context":"Q: Where do you normally get news from?\nA: I mainly get my news from a few reputable websites, and I've also signed up to some specialist newsletters. If a story's really important, I'll compare more than one source, because headlines alone don't always give you the full picture."},{"en":"a completely different angle","context":"Q: How does news reporting in your country differ from reporting abroad?\nA: I'd say our media focuses more on local politics and social issues, whereas foreign news often looks at the same story from a completely different angle. Comparing the two actually helps me spot any bias."},{"en":"spot any bias","context":"Q: How does news reporting in your country differ from reporting abroad?\nA: I'd say our media focuses more on local politics and social issues, whereas foreign news often looks at the same story from a completely different angle. Comparing the two actually helps me spot any bias."},{"en":"a direct practical benefit","context":"Q: Tell me about an interesting news item you have read or heard recently.\nA: I recently read about a new piece of medical technology that lets doctors detect diseases much earlier. What interested me most was how it showed research can have a direct practical benefit for everyday people."},{"en":"reliable understanding","context":"Q: Are you interested in the news, and what kind of news do you follow?\nA: Yes, I am, especially anything to do with science, education or major world events. I don't try to follow every single update though, because constant exposure just creates noise rather than reliable understanding."}],"subtype":"Part 1","summary":"News","visual":null,"id":"speaking-part-1-056","_displayNo":"#055","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-056-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-056-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-056-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-056-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"I use a few news websites I trust and receive some newsletters about subjects I follow. For an important story, I check several sources because a headline does not explain everything.","phrases":[{"en":"sources","meaning":"Places or people that provide information."}],"question":"Where do you normally get news from?","html":"I use a few news websites I trust and receive some newsletters about subjects I follow. For an important story, I check several <strong class=\"key-phrase\">sources</strong> because a headline does not explain everything."},{"text":"News here often pays more attention to local politics and social problems. Reports from other countries may explain the same event differently. Reading both helps me notice when a report favours one side.","phrases":[{"en":"favours one side","meaning":"Supports one view more strongly than another."}],"question":"How does news reporting in your country differ from reporting abroad?","html":"News here often pays more attention to local politics and social problems. Reports from other countries may explain the same event differently. Reading both helps me notice when a report <strong class=\"key-phrase\">favours one side</strong>."},{"text":"I recently read about medical technology that helps doctors find diseases earlier. I found it interesting because it showed how research can lead to something useful in ordinary people's lives.","phrases":[{"en":"lead to","meaning":"Cause or make something possible."}],"question":"Tell me about an interesting news item you have read or heard recently.","html":"I recently read about medical technology that helps doctors find diseases earlier. I found it interesting because it showed how research can <strong class=\"key-phrase\">lead to</strong> something useful in ordinary people&#x27;s lives."},{"text":"Yes, I follow science, education and important world events. I don't read every update, though, because too much news can make it harder to understand what is really important.","phrases":[{"en":"update","meaning":"New information about something that is changing."}],"question":"Are you interested in the news, and what kind of news do you follow?","html":"Yes, I follow science, education and important world events. I don&#x27;t read every <strong class=\"key-phrase\">update</strong>, though, because too much news can make it harder to understand what is really important."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-056-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-056-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-056-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-056-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Special numbers and remembering them","prompt":"Do you have a favourite number or a number that is special to you?\nDo any numbers have special importance in your country?\nAre you good at remembering numbers?\nWhat numbers do people often have to memorise?","answer":"Q: Do you have a favourite number or a number that is special to you?\nA: My favourite number is seven because it&#x27;s the date of my birthday, and I&#x27;ve always had <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a soft spot for it</strong>. I wouldn&#x27;t call it genuinely lucky, but I do feel a strong attachment to it.\n\nQ: Do any numbers have special importance in your country?\nA: Yes. The number 7, for example, is <strong class=\"key-phrase\">supposed to be a special number</strong> in my country. It appears in so many places, like the seven days of the week, the seven main notes in music, and the seven ages of man that Shakespeare described.\n\nQ: Are you good at remembering numbers?\nA: No, I&#x27;m not very good at remembering numbers. I don&#x27;t think it&#x27;s necessary to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">learn them by heart</strong>; I just save them on my phone.\n\nQ: What numbers do people often have to memorise?\nA: The most important number to remember <strong class=\"key-phrase\">on a daily basis</strong> is the PIN number for your bank card. Without this you can&#x27;t pay for anything or <strong class=\"key-phrase\">get cash out</strong>.","topic":"Numbers","phrases":[{"en":"a soft spot for it","context":"Q: Do you have a favourite number or a number that is special to you?\nA: My favourite number is seven because it's the date of my birthday, and I've always had a soft spot for it. I wouldn't call it genuinely lucky, but I do feel a strong attachment to it."},{"en":"supposed to be a special number","context":"Q: Do any numbers have special importance in your country?\nA: Yes. The number 7, for example, is supposed to be a special number in my country. It appears in so many places, like the seven days of the week, the seven main notes in music, and the seven ages of man that Shakespeare described."},{"en":"learn them by heart","context":"Q: Are you good at remembering numbers?\nA: No, I'm not very good at remembering numbers. I don't think it's necessary to learn them by heart; I just save them on my phone."},{"en":"on a daily basis","context":"Q: What numbers do people often have to memorise?\nA: The most important number to remember on a daily basis is the PIN number for your bank card. Without this you can't pay for anything or get cash out."},{"en":"get cash out","context":"Q: What numbers do people often have to memorise?\nA: The most important number to remember on a daily basis is the PIN number for your bank card. Without this you can't pay for anything or get cash out."}],"subtype":"","summary":"Numbers","id":"speaking-part-1-057","_displayNo":"#056","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-057-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-057-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-057-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-057-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"Seven is special to me because my birthday is on the seventh. I don't really believe it brings good luck, but I like it because of that personal connection.","phrases":[{"en":"personal connection","meaning":"A link with your own life or experiences."}],"question":"Do you have a favourite number or a number that is special to you?","html":"Seven is special to me because my birthday is on the seventh. I don&#x27;t really believe it brings good luck, but I like it because of that <strong class=\"key-phrase\">personal connection</strong>."},{"text":"Yes, seven is seen as special, for example. There are seven days in a week and seven main musical notes. Shakespeare also described human life as having seven stages.","phrases":[{"en":"stages","meaning":"Different parts of a process or period of development."}],"question":"Do any numbers have special importance in your country?","html":"Yes, seven is seen as special, for example. There are seven days in a week and seven main musical notes. Shakespeare also described human life as having seven <strong class=\"key-phrase\">stages</strong>."},{"text":"No, I find numbers difficult to remember. I usually save them on my phone rather than try to remember every one, which is more practical for me.","phrases":[{"en":"practical","meaning":"Useful and suitable for everyday needs."}],"question":"Are you good at remembering numbers?","html":"No, I find numbers difficult to remember. I usually save them on my phone rather than try to remember every one, which is more <strong class=\"key-phrase\">practical</strong> for me."},{"text":"A bank card PIN is an important number to remember. People often need it to pay by card or take money from a cash machine, so forgetting it can cause problems.","phrases":[{"en":"PIN","meaning":"A secret number used to confirm that you can use a card or account."}],"question":"What numbers do people often have to memorise?","html":"A bank card <strong class=\"key-phrase\">PIN</strong> is an important number to remember. People often need it to pay by card or take money from a cash machine, so forgetting it can cause problems."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-057-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-057-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-057-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-057-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Visiting parks and why towns need them","prompt":"Do you like parks?\nHow often do you visit parks?\nWhy are parks an important part of many towns and cities?\nWhat do you think could be done to make parks better?","answer":"Q: Do you like parks?\nA: Yes, I like parks because they&#x27;re great places to relax or go for a walk. I think every city needs some green space where people can <strong class=\"key-phrase\">escape from the crowds</strong>.\n\nQ: How often do you visit parks?\nA: There&#x27;s a park very close to where I live, so I probably go there <strong class=\"key-phrase\">once or twice a week</strong> if the weather&#x27;s nice.\n\nQ: Why are parks an important part of many towns and cities?\nA: Parks are like an oasis where people get away from <strong class=\"key-phrase\">the hustle and bustle</strong> of city life. They are where people go to have lunch, to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">take some exercise</strong>, or to forget about work for a while.\n\nQ: What do you think could be done to make parks better?\nA: Even well-designed parks have <strong class=\"key-phrase\">room for improvement</strong>. Cities could add safer paths, accessible toilets, shaded seating and better maintenance, while protecting quiet areas from excessive commercial activity.","topic":"Parks","phrases":[{"en":"escape from the crowds","context":"Q: Do you like parks?\nA: Yes, I like parks because they're great places to relax or go for a walk. I think every city needs some green space where people can escape from the crowds."},{"en":"once or twice a week","context":"Q: How often do you visit parks?\nA: There's a park very close to where I live, so I probably go there once or twice a week if the weather's nice."},{"en":"the hustle and bustle","context":"Q: Why are parks an important part of many towns and cities?\nA: Parks are like an oasis where people get away from the hustle and bustle of city life. They are where people go to have lunch, to take some exercise, or to forget about work for a while."},{"en":"take some exercise","context":"Q: Why are parks an important part of many towns and cities?\nA: Parks are like an oasis where people get away from the hustle and bustle of city life. They are where people go to have lunch, to take some exercise, or to forget about work for a while."},{"en":"room for improvement","context":"Q: What do you think could be done to make parks better?\nA: Even well-designed parks have room for improvement. Cities could add safer paths, accessible toilets, shaded seating and better maintenance, while protecting quiet areas from excessive commercial activity."}],"subtype":"","summary":"Parks","id":"speaking-part-1-058","_displayNo":"#057","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-058-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-058-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-058-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-058-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"Yes, I like them because I can relax or walk there. Busy cities need green places where people can take a break from crowds and noise.","phrases":[{"en":"green places","meaning":"Areas with grass, trees or other plants."}],"question":"Do you like parks?","html":"Yes, I like them because I can relax or walk there. Busy cities need <strong class=\"key-phrase\">green places</strong> where people can take a break from crowds and noise."},{"text":"There is a park near my home, so I usually visit once or twice a week when the weather is good. Being close makes it easy to go regularly.","phrases":[{"en":"once or twice a week","meaning":"One or two times during a week."}],"question":"How often do you visit parks?","html":"There is a park near my home, so I usually visit <strong class=\"key-phrase\">once or twice a week</strong> when the weather is good. Being close makes it easy to go regularly."},{"text":"Parks give people a quieter place away from busy streets. People can eat lunch, exercise or stop thinking about work for a while, so they make city life more pleasant.","phrases":[{"en":"for a while","meaning":"For a short period of time."}],"question":"Why are parks an important part of many towns and cities?","html":"Parks give people a quieter place away from busy streets. People can eat lunch, exercise or stop thinking about work <strong class=\"key-phrase\">for a while</strong>, so they make city life more pleasant."},{"text":"Cities could improve paths, add shaded seats and toilets that everyone can use, and look after parks better. Quiet areas should also be protected from too many shops or other business activities.","phrases":[{"en":"shaded","meaning":"Protected from direct sunlight."}],"question":"What do you think could be done to make parks better?","html":"Cities could improve paths, add <strong class=\"key-phrase\">shaded</strong> seats and toilets that everyone can use, and look after parks better. Quiet areas should also be protected from too many shops or other business activities."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-058-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-058-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-058-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-058-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Patience, politeness and rude behaviour","prompt":"Are you a patient person?\nIs it important to be polite?\nWhat do you do when others are rude?","answer":"Q: Are you a patient person?\nA: I&#x27;d say I&#x27;m fairly patient, especially when something&#x27;s <strong class=\"key-phrase\">out of someone&#x27;s control</strong>. But I do get a bit frustrated when the same avoidable mistake keeps happening. I try to pause for a second before reacting, so I don&#x27;t let frustration <strong class=\"key-phrase\">control my response</strong>.\n\nQ: Is it important to be polite?\nA: Yes, definitely, because it stops unnecessary arguments and shows respect. Being polite doesn&#x27;t mean you have to agree with everyone, though; it just means you can disagree without <strong class=\"key-phrase\">attacking the person</strong>.\n\nQ: What do you do when others are rude?\nA: I try to stay calm and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">set a clear boundary</strong>, without matching their tone. If it carries on, I&#x27;ll just end the conversation rather than letting things <strong class=\"key-phrase\">escalate further</strong>.","topic":"Patience & Politeness","phrases":[{"en":"out of someone's control","context":"Q: Are you a patient person?\nA: I'd say I'm fairly patient, especially when something's out of someone's control. But I do get a bit frustrated when the same avoidable mistake keeps happening. I try to pause for a second before reacting, so I don't let frustration control my response."},{"en":"control my response","context":"Q: Are you a patient person?\nA: I'd say I'm fairly patient, especially when something's out of someone's control. But I do get a bit frustrated when the same avoidable mistake keeps happening. I try to pause for a second before reacting, so I don't let frustration control my response."},{"en":"attacking the person","context":"Q: Is it important to be polite?\nA: Yes, definitely, because it stops unnecessary arguments and shows respect. Being polite doesn't mean you have to agree with everyone, though; it just means you can disagree without attacking the person."},{"en":"set a clear boundary","context":"Q: What do you do when others are rude?\nA: I try to stay calm and set a clear boundary, without matching their tone. If it carries on, I'll just end the conversation rather than letting things escalate further."},{"en":"escalate further","context":"Q: What do you do when others are rude?\nA: I try to stay calm and set a clear boundary, without matching their tone. If it carries on, I'll just end the conversation rather than letting things escalate further."}],"subtype":"","summary":"Patience & Politeness","id":"speaking-part-1-059","_displayNo":"#058","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-059-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-059-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-059-q03.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"I'm usually patient when someone cannot control the situation. Repeated mistakes can annoy me, though. I try to stop and think before responding so I don't speak only out of frustration.","phrases":[{"en":"frustration","meaning":"The annoyed feeling of being unable to do or change something."}],"question":"Are you a patient person?","html":"I&#x27;m usually patient when someone cannot control the situation. Repeated mistakes can annoy me, though. I try to stop and think before responding so I don&#x27;t speak only out of <strong class=\"key-phrase\">frustration</strong>."},{"text":"Yes, being polite shows respect and helps prevent arguments. You can still disagree with someone, but you should explain your opinion without being hurtful or insulting them.","phrases":[{"en":"insulting","meaning":"Speaking to someone in a rude or offensive way."}],"question":"Is it important to be polite?","html":"Yes, being polite shows respect and helps prevent arguments. You can still disagree with someone, but you should explain your opinion without being hurtful or <strong class=\"key-phrase\">insulting</strong> them."},{"text":"I try to stay calm and explain what behaviour I will not accept. If the person continues being rude, I end the conversation before it becomes a bigger argument.","phrases":[{"en":"stay calm","meaning":"Keep your feelings under control and avoid becoming angry."}],"question":"What do you do when others are rude?","html":"I try to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">stay calm</strong> and explain what behaviour I will not accept. If the person continues being rude, I end the conversation before it becomes a bigger argument."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-059-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-059-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-059-q03.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"The photos you take and what you do with them","prompt":"What type of photos do you like taking?\nWhat do you do with photos you take?\nWhen you visit other places, do you take photos or buy postcards?\nDo you like people taking photos of you?","answer":"Q: What type of photos do you like taking?\nA: I rarely take photographs because I prefer to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">stay present in the moment</strong>. I <strong class=\"key-phrase\">make an exception for</strong> family occasions or unusual places that I genuinely want to remember.\n\nQ: What do you do with photos you take?\nA: Most photos remain on my phone or in cloud storage. I occasionally create an album after a trip, but I admit that I don&#x27;t <strong class=\"key-phrase\">organise them systematically</strong>.\n\nQ: When you visit other places, do you take photos or buy postcards?\nA: I don&#x27;t really do either. I <strong class=\"key-phrase\">leave it to my friends</strong> or other family members to take photographs; I&#x27;m usually with someone who likes taking photos and can share them with me later.\n\nQ: Do you like people taking photos of you?\nA: No, I prefer not to be in photos. I always feel awkward when someone asks me to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">smile for the camera</strong>, and I don&#x27;t think I&#x27;m very photogenic.","topic":"Photography","phrases":[{"en":"stay present in the moment","context":"Q: What type of photos do you like taking?\nA: I rarely take photographs because I prefer to stay present in the moment. I make an exception for family occasions or unusual places that I genuinely want to remember."},{"en":"make an exception for","context":"Q: What type of photos do you like taking?\nA: I rarely take photographs because I prefer to stay present in the moment. I make an exception for family occasions or unusual places that I genuinely want to remember."},{"en":"organise them systematically","context":"Q: What do you do with photos you take?\nA: Most photos remain on my phone or in cloud storage. I occasionally create an album after a trip, but I admit that I don't organise them systematically."},{"en":"leave it to my friends","context":"Q: When you visit other places, do you take photos or buy postcards?\nA: I don't really do either. I leave it to my friends or other family members to take photographs; I'm usually with someone who likes taking photos and can share them with me later."},{"en":"smile for the camera","context":"Q: Do you like people taking photos of you?\nA: No, I prefer not to be in photos. I always feel awkward when someone asks me to smile for the camera, and I don't think I'm very photogenic."}],"subtype":"","summary":"Photography","id":"speaking-part-1-060","_displayNo":"#059","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-060-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-060-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-060-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-060-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"I don't take many photos because I prefer enjoying what is happening. I mainly take them at family events or unusual places that I especially want to remember.","phrases":[{"en":"family events","meaning":"Occasions when family members meet or celebrate together."}],"question":"What type of photos do you like taking?","html":"I don&#x27;t take many photos because I prefer enjoying what is happening. I mainly take them at <strong class=\"key-phrase\">family events</strong> or unusual places that I especially want to remember."},{"text":"Most stay on my phone or in online storage. Sometimes I make an album after a trip, but I don't have a very organised system for keeping all my photos.","phrases":[{"en":"an album","meaning":"A collection of photographs arranged together."}],"question":"What do you do with photos you take?","html":"Most stay on my phone or in online storage. Sometimes I make <strong class=\"key-phrase\">an album</strong> after a trip, but I don&#x27;t have a very organised system for keeping all my photos."},{"text":"I usually do neither. I often travel with friends or family who enjoy taking pictures, so I let them take the photos and share them with me later.","phrases":[{"en":"share them with me","meaning":"Let me see or have copies of them."}],"question":"When you visit other places, do you take photos or buy postcards?","html":"I usually do neither. I often travel with friends or family who enjoy taking pictures, so I let them take the photos and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">share them with me</strong> later."},{"text":"No, I don't really enjoy it. I feel uncomfortable when someone asks me to smile for a photo, and I don't think I usually look good in pictures.","phrases":[{"en":"uncomfortable","meaning":"Not relaxed or at ease."}],"question":"Do you like people taking photos of you?","html":"No, I don&#x27;t really enjoy it. I feel <strong class=\"key-phrase\">uncomfortable</strong> when someone asks me to smile for a photo, and I don&#x27;t think I usually look good in pictures."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-060-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-060-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-060-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-060-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Whether photography is growing, and whether cameras lie","prompt":"Is photography becoming more popular these days, in your experience?\nDo you agree with the saying “The camera never lies”?\nWould you say photography is an art?","answer":"Q: Is photography becoming more popular these days, in your experience?\nA: Yes, I&#x27;d say it definitely is. Smartphones have made photography available to almost everyone, so people now document everyday moments as well as special occasions. But with so many images around, an individual photo can easily <strong class=\"key-phrase\">feel less significant</strong>.\n\nQ: Do you agree with the saying “The camera never lies”?\nA: No, I don&#x27;t, really. A photo does capture something real, but the framing, timing, editing and captions can completely change the message it sends. So photos are <strong class=\"key-phrase\">powerful evidence</strong>, but they&#x27;re still <strong class=\"key-phrase\">open to interpretation</strong>.\n\nQ: Would you say photography is an art?\nA: Yes, I think it can be, when the photographer&#x27;s using light, composition and timing to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">get across an idea</strong> or a feeling. It&#x27;s not just about technical accuracy; artistic photography needs <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a deliberate point of view</strong>.","topic":"Photography","phrases":[{"en":"feel less significant","context":"Q: Is photography becoming more popular these days, in your experience?\nA: Yes, I'd say it definitely is. Smartphones have made photography available to almost everyone, so people now document everyday moments as well as special occasions. But with so many images around, an individual photo can easily feel less significant."},{"en":"powerful evidence","context":"Q: Do you agree with the saying “The camera never lies”?\nA: No, I don't, really. A photo does capture something real, but the framing, timing, editing and captions can completely change the message it sends. So photos are powerful evidence, but they're still open to interpretation."},{"en":"open to interpretation","context":"Q: Do you agree with the saying “The camera never lies”?\nA: No, I don't, really. A photo does capture something real, but the framing, timing, editing and captions can completely change the message it sends. So photos are powerful evidence, but they're still open to interpretation."},{"en":"get across an idea","context":"Q: Would you say photography is an art?\nA: Yes, I think it can be, when the photographer's using light, composition and timing to get across an idea or a feeling. It's not just about technical accuracy; artistic photography needs a deliberate point of view."},{"en":"a deliberate point of view","context":"Q: Would you say photography is an art?\nA: Yes, I think it can be, when the photographer's using light, composition and timing to get across an idea or a feeling. It's not just about technical accuracy; artistic photography needs a deliberate point of view."}],"subtype":"Part 1","summary":"Photography","visual":null,"id":"speaking-part-1-061","_displayNo":"#060","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-061-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-061-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-061-q03.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"Yes, smartphones make it easy for almost everyone to take photos. People now photograph ordinary moments as well as special events. However, because there are so many pictures, each one may feel less important.","phrases":[{"en":"ordinary moments","meaning":"Normal everyday experiences, rather than special events."}],"question":"Is photography becoming more popular these days, in your experience?","html":"Yes, smartphones make it easy for almost everyone to take photos. People now photograph <strong class=\"key-phrase\">ordinary moments</strong> as well as special events. However, because there are so many pictures, each one may feel less important."},{"text":"No, not completely. A photograph shows something real, but the choice of what to include, editing and the words added to it can change its meaning. We still need to think about the context.","phrases":[{"en":"context","meaning":"The background or situation that helps explain something."}],"question":"Do you agree with the saying “The camera never lies”?","html":"No, not completely. A photograph shows something real, but the choice of what to include, editing and the words added to it can change its meaning. We still need to think about the <strong class=\"key-phrase\">context</strong>."},{"text":"Yes, photography can be art. A photographer can use light, timing and the way things are arranged to express an idea or feeling. It involves more than just taking a clear picture.","phrases":[{"en":"express","meaning":"Show or communicate a feeling or idea."}],"question":"Would you say photography is an art?","html":"Yes, photography can be art. A photographer can use light, timing and the way things are arranged to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">express</strong> an idea or feeling. It involves more than just taking a clear picture."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-061-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-061-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-061-q03.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Rain and how it affects people","prompt":"Do you like rain?\nDo you think that rain affects people's mood?\nDoes it often rain where you live?\nHave you ever been caught in the rain without a coat or umbrella?","answer":"Q: Do you like rain?\nA: No, not at all. It rains far too often in Manchester, where I live, and I&#x27;m <strong class=\"key-phrase\">fed up of it</strong>; I wish we had more sun!\n\nQ: Do you think that rain affects people&#x27;s mood?\nA: Yes, definitely. I think <strong class=\"key-phrase\">rainy days and grey skies</strong> can be a bit sad and depressing. Where I live, people are much more cheerful when the sun comes out.\n\nQ: Does it often rain where you live?\nA: Yes, unfortunately it does. As I said, Manchester is <strong class=\"key-phrase\">known for being a rainy place</strong>; you can&#x27;t trust the weather here, because it can <strong class=\"key-phrase\">cloud over</strong> and start raining at any moment.\n\nQ: Have you ever been caught in the rain without a coat or umbrella?\nA: Yes, many times. Just last week I went out without an umbrella and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">got soaked</strong>; I did have a coat on, but it didn&#x27;t really help.","topic":"Rain","phrases":[{"en":"fed up of it","context":"Q: Do you like rain?\nA: No, not at all. It rains far too often in Manchester, where I live, and I'm fed up of it; I wish we had more sun!"},{"en":"rainy days and grey skies","context":"Q: Do you think that rain affects people's mood?\nA: Yes, definitely. I think rainy days and grey skies can be a bit sad and depressing. Where I live, people are much more cheerful when the sun comes out."},{"en":"known for being a rainy place","context":"Q: Does it often rain where you live?\nA: Yes, unfortunately it does. As I said, Manchester is known for being a rainy place; you can't trust the weather here, because it can cloud over and start raining at any moment."},{"en":"cloud over","context":"Q: Does it often rain where you live?\nA: Yes, unfortunately it does. As I said, Manchester is known for being a rainy place; you can't trust the weather here, because it can cloud over and start raining at any moment."},{"en":"got soaked","context":"Q: Have you ever been caught in the rain without a coat or umbrella?\nA: Yes, many times. Just last week I went out without an umbrella and got soaked; I did have a coat on, but it didn't really help."}],"subtype":"","summary":"Rain","id":"speaking-part-1-062","_displayNo":"#061","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-062-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-062-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-062-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-062-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"No, I don't like it much. It rains very often in Manchester, where I live, and I'm tired of the wet weather. I'd really like more sunshine.","phrases":[{"en":"tired of","meaning":"Annoyed because something has happened too often."}],"question":"Do you like rain?","html":"No, I don&#x27;t like it much. It rains very often in Manchester, where I live, and I&#x27;m <strong class=\"key-phrase\">tired of</strong> the wet weather. I&#x27;d really like more sunshine."},{"text":"Yes, rainy days and grey skies can make people feel a little sad. People where I live seem much happier when the sun appears, so I think weather can affect mood.","phrases":[{"en":"mood","meaning":"The way someone feels at a particular time."}],"question":"Do you think that rain affects people's mood?","html":"Yes, rainy days and grey skies can make people feel a little sad. People where I live seem much happier when the sun appears, so I think weather can affect <strong class=\"key-phrase\">mood</strong>."},{"text":"Yes, it rains a lot in Manchester. The weather changes quickly, so even if it looks fine at first, clouds and rain can arrive quite suddenly.","phrases":[{"en":"suddenly","meaning":"Quickly and without much warning."}],"question":"Does it often rain where you live?","html":"Yes, it rains a lot in Manchester. The weather changes quickly, so even if it looks fine at first, clouds and rain can arrive quite <strong class=\"key-phrase\">suddenly</strong>."},{"text":"Yes, many times. Last week, I went out without an umbrella and became completely wet. I was wearing a coat, but it did not keep the rain out very well.","phrases":[{"en":"keep the rain out","meaning":"Stop rain from getting inside or reaching you."}],"question":"Have you ever been caught in the rain without a coat or umbrella?","html":"Yes, many times. Last week, I went out without an umbrella and became completely wet. I was wearing a coat, but it did not <strong class=\"key-phrase\">keep the rain out</strong> very well."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-062-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-062-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-062-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-062-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Reading for leisure and childhood books","prompt":"Do you like reading?\nDo you usually read for leisure or for work purposes?\nWhat was your favourite book or story when you were a child?\nDo you think it's important that children read regularly?","answer":"Q: Do you like reading?\nA: Yes, I like reading a lot. I read <strong class=\"key-phrase\">all sorts of things</strong>, including novels, newspapers, magazines, and online articles.\n\nQ: Do you usually read for leisure or for work purposes?\nA: Well, I&#x27;ve got to do a certain amount of reading <strong class=\"key-phrase\">as part of my job</strong>, but I probably read more for enjoyment. I pick up a newspaper most days, and I usually <strong class=\"key-phrase\">have a book on the go</strong>.\n\nQ: What was your favourite book or story when you were a child?\nA: The first book I remember loving was Harry Potter and the Philosopher&#x27;s Stone. The magical setting immediately captured my imagination, and I read it so quickly that I <strong class=\"key-phrase\">could hardly put it down</strong>.\n\nQ: Do you think it&#x27;s important that children read regularly?\nA: Definitely. I think reading&#x27;s possibly the most important skill that children learn. The ability to read <strong class=\"key-phrase\">opens the door to</strong> all aspects of education.","topic":"Reading","phrases":[{"en":"all sorts of things","context":"Q: Do you like reading?\nA: Yes, I like reading a lot. I read all sorts of things, including novels, newspapers, magazines, and online articles."},{"en":"as part of my job","context":"Q: Do you usually read for leisure or for work purposes?\nA: Well, I've got to do a certain amount of reading as part of my job, but I probably read more for enjoyment. I pick up a newspaper most days, and I usually have a book on the go."},{"en":"have a book on the go","context":"Q: Do you usually read for leisure or for work purposes?\nA: Well, I've got to do a certain amount of reading as part of my job, but I probably read more for enjoyment. I pick up a newspaper most days, and I usually have a book on the go."},{"en":"could hardly put it down","context":"Q: What was your favourite book or story when you were a child?\nA: The first book I remember loving was Harry Potter and the Philosopher's Stone. The magical setting immediately captured my imagination, and I read it so quickly that I could hardly put it down."},{"en":"opens the door to","context":"Q: Do you think it's important that children read regularly?\nA: Definitely. I think reading's possibly the most important skill that children learn. The ability to read opens the door to all aspects of education."}],"subtype":"","summary":"Reading","id":"speaking-part-1-063","_displayNo":"#062","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-063-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-063-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-063-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-063-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"Yes, I enjoy reading many different things. I read novels, newspapers, magazines and articles online, so it is a hobby that gives me plenty of choice.","phrases":[{"en":"novels","meaning":"Books that tell made-up stories."}],"question":"Do you like reading?","html":"Yes, I enjoy reading many different things. I read <strong class=\"key-phrase\">novels</strong>, newspapers, magazines and articles online, so it is a hobby that gives me plenty of choice."},{"text":"I read for both, but probably more for pleasure. I need to read for my job, but I also read a newspaper most days and usually have a book that I'm reading.","phrases":[{"en":"for pleasure","meaning":"Because you enjoy it, rather than because you have to."}],"question":"Do you usually read for leisure or for work purposes?","html":"I read for both, but probably more <strong class=\"key-phrase\">for pleasure</strong>. I need to read for my job, but I also read a newspaper most days and usually have a book that I&#x27;m reading."},{"text":"My favourite was Harry Potter and the Philosopher's Stone. I loved the magical world and wanted to know what happened next, so I read it very quickly.","phrases":[{"en":"magical","meaning":"Involving powers or events that cannot happen in the normal world."}],"question":"What was your favourite book or story when you were a child?","html":"My favourite was Harry Potter and the Philosopher&#x27;s Stone. I loved the <strong class=\"key-phrase\">magical</strong> world and wanted to know what happened next, so I read it very quickly."},{"text":"Yes, regular reading is very important. When children can read well, they can learn about many subjects more easily. It helps them with almost every part of their education.","phrases":[{"en":"education","meaning":"The process of learning, especially at school or college."}],"question":"Do you think it's important that children read regularly?","html":"Yes, regular reading is very important. When children can read well, they can learn about many subjects more easily. It helps them with almost every part of their <strong class=\"key-phrase\">education</strong>."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-063-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-063-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-063-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-063-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Robots at home and in childhood cartoons","prompt":"What do you think of robots?\nDid you watch any cartoons related to robots in your childhood?\nDo you like the idea of robots helping you at home or driving your car?","answer":"Q: What do you think of robots?\nA: I think robots are <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a clever idea</strong>. I&#x27;d love to have a robot that could speak to me and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">do things for me</strong>!\n\nQ: Did you watch any cartoons related to robots in your childhood?\nA: I can&#x27;t remember <strong class=\"key-phrase\">watching cartoons with robots</strong>, but I remember that I liked the robots in films like Star Wars.\n\nQ: Do you like the idea of robots helping you at home or driving your car?\nA: Yes, definitely. It would be great to have <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a robot helper</strong> at home, and I like the idea of <strong class=\"key-phrase\">driverless cars</strong> - I think driving would be safer if cars were controlled by robots.","topic":"Robots","phrases":[{"en":"a clever idea","context":"Q: What do you think of robots?\nA: I think robots are a clever idea. I'd love to have a robot that could speak to me and do things for me!"},{"en":"do things for me","context":"Q: What do you think of robots?\nA: I think robots are a clever idea. I'd love to have a robot that could speak to me and do things for me!"},{"en":"watching cartoons with robots","context":"Q: Did you watch any cartoons related to robots in your childhood?\nA: I can't remember watching cartoons with robots, but I remember that I liked the robots in films like Star Wars."},{"en":"a robot helper","context":"Q: Do you like the idea of robots helping you at home or driving your car?\nA: Yes, definitely. It would be great to have a robot helper at home, and I like the idea of driverless cars - I think driving would be safer if cars were controlled by robots."},{"en":"driverless cars","context":"Q: Do you like the idea of robots helping you at home or driving your car?\nA: Yes, definitely. It would be great to have a robot helper at home, and I like the idea of driverless cars - I think driving would be safer if cars were controlled by robots."}],"subtype":"","summary":"Robots","id":"speaking-part-1-064","_displayNo":"#063","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-064-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-064-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-064-q03.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"I think robots are a very clever invention. I'd enjoy having one that could talk to me and help with tasks, because it would make daily life easier.","phrases":[{"en":"invention","meaning":"Something new that someone has designed or made."}],"question":"What do you think of robots?","html":"I think robots are a very clever <strong class=\"key-phrase\">invention</strong>. I&#x27;d enjoy having one that could talk to me and help with tasks, because it would make daily life easier."},{"text":"I don't remember any cartoons about robots, but I liked the robots in films such as Star Wars. Those are the ones I remember from childhood.","phrases":[{"en":"childhood","meaning":"The period of life when you were a child."}],"question":"Did you watch any cartoons related to robots in your childhood?","html":"I don&#x27;t remember any cartoons about robots, but I liked the robots in films such as Star Wars. Those are the ones I remember from <strong class=\"key-phrase\">childhood</strong>."},{"text":"Yes, I'd like a robot to help around the house. I also like the idea of cars that drive themselves, and I think they could make driving safer if the technology works well.","phrases":[{"en":"drive themselves","meaning":"Move and control the journey without a person driving."}],"question":"Do you like the idea of robots helping you at home or driving your car?","html":"Yes, I&#x27;d like a robot to help around the house. I also like the idea of cars that <strong class=\"key-phrase\">drive themselves</strong>, and I think they could make driving safer if the technology works well."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-064-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-064-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-064-q03.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Living near the sea and how it makes you feel","prompt":"Do you live near the sea?\nHow do you feel when you are near the sea?\nWhat do you like and dislike about the sea?\nWould you like to live on an island and why?","answer":"Q: Do you live near the sea?\nA: I don&#x27;t live right by the sea, so going to the coast still feels like a bit of a treat. It takes a while to get there, but that&#x27;s what makes each trip <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a refreshing change</strong>.\n\nQ: How do you feel when you are near the sea?\nA: I usually feel a lot calmer near the sea, because the open horizon and the sound of the waves just clear my head. It&#x27;s one of the few places where I can <strong class=\"key-phrase\">switch off completely</strong>.\n\nQ: What do you like and dislike about the sea?\nA: I like the fresh air and the views, but I&#x27;m not so keen on crowded beaches or plastic waste. The coast&#x27;s always nicer when tourism doesn&#x27;t end up <strong class=\"key-phrase\">damaging the environment</strong>.\n\nQ: Would you like to live on an island and why?\nA: I&#x27;d enjoy living on an island for a short while, but probably not permanently. Isolation might be peaceful, but limited healthcare, transport and job options would make everyday life <strong class=\"key-phrase\">less convenient</strong>.","topic":"Sea","phrases":[{"en":"a refreshing change","context":"Q: Do you live near the sea?\nA: I don't live right by the sea, so going to the coast still feels like a bit of a treat. It takes a while to get there, but that's what makes each trip a refreshing change."},{"en":"switch off completely","context":"Q: How do you feel when you are near the sea?\nA: I usually feel a lot calmer near the sea, because the open horizon and the sound of the waves just clear my head. It's one of the few places where I can switch off completely."},{"en":"damaging the environment","context":"Q: What do you like and dislike about the sea?\nA: I like the fresh air and the views, but I'm not so keen on crowded beaches or plastic waste. The coast's always nicer when tourism doesn't end up damaging the environment."},{"en":"less convenient","context":"Q: Would you like to live on an island and why?\nA: I'd enjoy living on an island for a short while, but probably not permanently. Isolation might be peaceful, but limited healthcare, transport and job options would make everyday life less convenient."}],"subtype":"Part 1","summary":"Sea","visual":null,"id":"speaking-part-1-065","_displayNo":"#064","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-065-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-065-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-065-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-065-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"No, I don't live close to the sea. It takes some time to get there, so visiting the coast feels special and gives me a pleasant change from normal life.","phrases":[{"en":"the coast","meaning":"The land beside the sea."}],"question":"Do you live near the sea?","html":"No, I don&#x27;t live close to the sea. It takes some time to get there, so visiting <strong class=\"key-phrase\">the coast</strong> feels special and gives me a pleasant change from normal life."},{"text":"I feel much calmer there. Seeing the open sea and hearing the waves help me stop worrying and relax. It is a place where I can really take a mental break.","phrases":[{"en":"waves","meaning":"The moving lines of water that rise and fall on the sea."}],"question":"How do you feel when you are near the sea?","html":"I feel much calmer there. Seeing the open sea and hearing the <strong class=\"key-phrase\">waves</strong> help me stop worrying and relax. It is a place where I can really take a mental break."},{"text":"I enjoy the fresh air and beautiful views. However, I don't like busy beaches or plastic rubbish. The sea is more enjoyable when visitors look after the environment.","phrases":[{"en":"environment","meaning":"The natural world around us, including land, water and air."}],"question":"What do you like and dislike about the sea?","html":"I enjoy the fresh air and beautiful views. However, I don&#x27;t like busy beaches or plastic rubbish. The sea is more enjoyable when visitors look after the <strong class=\"key-phrase\">environment</strong>."},{"text":"I'd like to try it for a short time, but not forever. An island might be peaceful, but fewer hospitals, jobs and transport options could make normal life difficult.","phrases":[{"en":"options","meaning":"Different choices that are available."}],"question":"Would you like to live on an island and why?","html":"I&#x27;d like to try it for a short time, but not forever. An island might be peaceful, but fewer hospitals, jobs and transport <strong class=\"key-phrase\">options</strong> could make normal life difficult."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-065-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-065-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-065-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-065-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Buying shoes: comfort or style","prompt":"Do you like to buy expensive shoes?\nWhen you buy shoes, do you prefer convenience or style?\nWhy do you think some people buy many pairs of shoes?\nHave you ever bought shoes online?","answer":"Q: Do you like to buy expensive shoes?\nA: No. I tend to buy <strong class=\"key-phrase\">average-priced shoes</strong> because I&#x27;m more interested in comfort than expensive brands.\n\nQ: When you buy shoes, do you prefer convenience or style?\nA: I mainly look for <strong class=\"key-phrase\">comfort and convenience</strong>. But obviously I consider the style too, because I do choose shoes that <strong class=\"key-phrase\">match the clothes I wear</strong>.\n\nQ: Why do you think some people buy many pairs of shoes?\nA: I suppose they either like <strong class=\"key-phrase\">following the latest fashions</strong>, or they just enjoy having a different pair for every occasion.\n\nQ: Have you ever bought shoes online?\nA: No, I haven&#x27;t. I always like to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">try shoes on</strong> before I buy them, to make sure that they fit properly and feel comfortable.","topic":"Shoes","phrases":[{"en":"average-priced shoes","context":"Q: Do you like to buy expensive shoes?\nA: No. I tend to buy average-priced shoes because I'm more interested in comfort than expensive brands."},{"en":"comfort and convenience","context":"Q: When you buy shoes, do you prefer convenience or style?\nA: I mainly look for comfort and convenience. But obviously I consider the style too, because I do choose shoes that match the clothes I wear."},{"en":"match the clothes I wear","context":"Q: When you buy shoes, do you prefer convenience or style?\nA: I mainly look for comfort and convenience. But obviously I consider the style too, because I do choose shoes that match the clothes I wear."},{"en":"following the latest fashions","context":"Q: Why do you think some people buy many pairs of shoes?\nA: I suppose they either like following the latest fashions, or they just enjoy having a different pair for every occasion."},{"en":"try shoes on","context":"Q: Have you ever bought shoes online?\nA: No, I haven't. I always like to try shoes on before I buy them, to make sure that they fit properly and feel comfortable."}],"subtype":"","summary":"Shoes","id":"speaking-part-1-066","_displayNo":"#065","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-066-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-066-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-066-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-066-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"No, I usually buy shoes at a reasonable price. I care more about how comfortable they feel than whether they come from an expensive or famous brand.","phrases":[{"en":"reasonable price","meaning":"A cost that seems fair and not too high."}],"question":"Do you like to buy expensive shoes?","html":"No, I usually buy shoes at a <strong class=\"key-phrase\">reasonable price</strong>. I care more about how comfortable they feel than whether they come from an expensive or famous brand."},{"text":"Comfort and ease of use matter most to me. I still think about appearance, though, because I want the shoes to look good with the clothes I usually wear.","phrases":[{"en":"appearance","meaning":"The way something looks."}],"question":"When you buy shoes, do you prefer convenience or style?","html":"Comfort and ease of use matter most to me. I still think about <strong class=\"key-phrase\">appearance</strong>, though, because I want the shoes to look good with the clothes I usually wear."},{"text":"Some people enjoy following new fashions. Others like having different shoes for work, parties and other situations, so they buy several pairs to suit different occasions.","phrases":[{"en":"occasions","meaning":"Particular events or situations."}],"question":"Why do you think some people buy many pairs of shoes?","html":"Some people enjoy following new fashions. Others like having different shoes for work, parties and other situations, so they buy several pairs to suit different <strong class=\"key-phrase\">occasions</strong>."},{"text":"No, I haven't. I prefer to put shoes on in a shop before buying them. That way, I can check that they are the right size and feel comfortable.","phrases":[{"en":"the right size","meaning":"A size that fits properly."}],"question":"Have you ever bought shoes online?","html":"No, I haven&#x27;t. I prefer to put shoes on in a shop before buying them. That way, I can check that they are <strong class=\"key-phrase\">the right size</strong> and feel comfortable."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-066-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-066-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-066-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-066-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Who shops in your household and what you enjoy buying","prompt":"Who does most of the shopping in your household?\nWhat kind of shopping do you like doing?\nIs shopping a popular activity in your country?\nWhat types of shops do teenagers like best in your country?","answer":"Q: Who does most of the shopping in your household?\nA: There isn&#x27;t one person who does most of the shopping. I&#x27;d say it&#x27;s <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a shared responsibility</strong> because we tend to go shopping together as a family.\n\nQ: What kind of shopping do you like doing?\nA: I quite like <strong class=\"key-phrase\">shopping for presents</strong> for people&#x27;s birthdays or for Christmas. My favourite type of shop would have to be a bookshop.\n\nQ: Is shopping a popular activity in your country?\nA: Yes, it&#x27;s very popular. Saturday is the busiest shopping day, and lots of people treat shopping as a kind of <strong class=\"key-phrase\">leisure activity</strong>, rather than something practical.\n\nQ: What types of shops do teenagers like best in your country?\nA: I&#x27;m <strong class=\"key-phrase\">not an expert on</strong> teenage behaviour, but I guess they like buying clothes, music, gadgets, that kind of thing.","topic":"Shopping","phrases":[{"en":"a shared responsibility","context":"Q: Who does most of the shopping in your household?\nA: There isn't one person who does most of the shopping. I'd say it's a shared responsibility because we tend to go shopping together as a family."},{"en":"shopping for presents","context":"Q: What kind of shopping do you like doing?\nA: I quite like shopping for presents for people's birthdays or for Christmas. My favourite type of shop would have to be a bookshop."},{"en":"leisure activity","context":"Q: Is shopping a popular activity in your country?\nA: Yes, it's very popular. Saturday is the busiest shopping day, and lots of people treat shopping as a kind of leisure activity, rather than something practical."},{"en":"not an expert on","context":"Q: What types of shops do teenagers like best in your country?\nA: I'm not an expert on teenage behaviour, but I guess they like buying clothes, music, gadgets, that kind of thing."}],"subtype":"","summary":"Shopping","id":"speaking-part-1-067","_displayNo":"#066","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-067-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-067-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-067-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-067-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"We share the shopping rather than leaving it to one person. We often go together as a family, so everyone takes part and no one does most of it alone.","phrases":[{"en":"takes part","meaning":"Joins in an activity."}],"question":"Who does most of the shopping in your household?","html":"We share the shopping rather than leaving it to one person. We often go together as a family, so everyone <strong class=\"key-phrase\">takes part</strong> and no one does most of it alone."},{"text":"I enjoy buying presents for birthdays or Christmas. My favourite shops are bookshops because I like looking at books, so that is the shopping I enjoy most.","phrases":[{"en":"presents","meaning":"Things given to someone as gifts."}],"question":"What kind of shopping do you like doing?","html":"I enjoy buying <strong class=\"key-phrase\">presents</strong> for birthdays or Christmas. My favourite shops are bookshops because I like looking at books, so that is the shopping I enjoy most."},{"text":"Yes, shopping is very popular. Saturdays are especially busy, and many people go shopping for enjoyment rather than just to buy things they need.","phrases":[{"en":"for enjoyment","meaning":"To have fun or feel pleased."}],"question":"Is shopping a popular activity in your country?","html":"Yes, shopping is very popular. Saturdays are especially busy, and many people go shopping <strong class=\"key-phrase\">for enjoyment</strong> rather than just to buy things they need."},{"text":"I'm not completely sure, but I think teenagers enjoy shops selling clothes, music and electronic gadgets. Those seem like things many young people are interested in buying.","phrases":[{"en":"gadgets","meaning":"Small useful electronic devices."}],"question":"What types of shops do teenagers like best in your country?","html":"I&#x27;m not completely sure, but I think teenagers enjoy shops selling clothes, music and electronic <strong class=\"key-phrase\">gadgets</strong>. Those seem like things many young people are interested in buying."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-067-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-067-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-067-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-067-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Brands, and whether they matter","prompt":"Are you loyal to any brands?\nDo you want other people to know you buy a particular brand?\nDo you buy any products without considering the brand name?\nHow do you feel about going shopping?","answer":"Q: Are you loyal to any brands?\nA: I&#x27;m only loyal to a brand once it&#x27;s proved <strong class=\"key-phrase\">consistently reliable</strong>. I usually compare quality, after-sales service and price first, because I care more about how well something works than the brand name.\n\nQ: Do you want other people to know you buy a particular brand?\nA: Not really. I just want products that work well, and I don&#x27;t really see brand names as a way to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">show off</strong>. That kind of shopping can easily become <strong class=\"key-phrase\">more about image than value</strong>.\n\nQ: Do you buy any products without considering the brand name?\nA: Yes, definitely, especially with things like basic food, stationery and household goods. For simple stuff like that, I&#x27;ll compare ingredients, durability or price rather than <strong class=\"key-phrase\">relying on brand recognition</strong>.\n\nQ: How do you feel about going shopping?\nA: I don&#x27;t really see shopping as entertainment, more of <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a practical task</strong>. I enjoy it when I know exactly what I need, but crowded shops and too many choices can make it needlessly time-consuming.","topic":"Shopping","phrases":[{"en":"consistently reliable","context":"Q: Are you loyal to any brands?\nA: I'm only loyal to a brand once it's proved consistently reliable. I usually compare quality, after-sales service and price first, because I care more about how well something works than the brand name."},{"en":"show off","context":"Q: Do you want other people to know you buy a particular brand?\nA: Not really. I just want products that work well, and I don't really see brand names as a way to show off. That kind of shopping can easily become more about image than value."},{"en":"more about image than value","context":"Q: Do you want other people to know you buy a particular brand?\nA: Not really. I just want products that work well, and I don't really see brand names as a way to show off. That kind of shopping can easily become more about image than value."},{"en":"relying on brand recognition","context":"Q: Do you buy any products without considering the brand name?\nA: Yes, definitely, especially with things like basic food, stationery and household goods. For simple stuff like that, I'll compare ingredients, durability or price rather than relying on brand recognition."},{"en":"a practical task","context":"Q: How do you feel about going shopping?\nA: I don't really see shopping as entertainment, more of a practical task. I enjoy it when I know exactly what I need, but crowded shops and too many choices can make it needlessly time-consuming."}],"subtype":"Part 1","summary":"Shopping","visual":null,"id":"speaking-part-1-068","_displayNo":"#067","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-068-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-068-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-068-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-068-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"I keep buying a brand only after its products have worked well for me. I compare quality, price and help after purchase, because those matter more than the name.","phrases":[{"en":"after purchase","meaning":"After you have bought something."}],"question":"Are you loyal to any brands?","html":"I keep buying a brand only after its products have worked well for me. I compare quality, price and help <strong class=\"key-phrase\">after purchase</strong>, because those matter more than the name."},{"text":"No, I don't need people to notice the brands I buy. I mainly want products that work properly. Buying something just to impress others matters less to me than getting good value.","phrases":[{"en":"good value","meaning":"Worth the money you pay for it."}],"question":"Do you want other people to know you buy a particular brand?","html":"No, I don&#x27;t need people to notice the brands I buy. I mainly want products that work properly. Buying something just to impress others matters less to me than getting <strong class=\"key-phrase\">good value</strong>."},{"text":"Yes, with basic food, pens, paper and things for the home. I usually check what they contain, how long they last and their price rather than choosing a familiar name.","phrases":[{"en":"familiar","meaning":"Well known to you or easy to recognise."}],"question":"Do you buy any products without considering the brand name?","html":"Yes, with basic food, pens, paper and things for the home. I usually check what they contain, how long they last and their price rather than choosing a <strong class=\"key-phrase\">familiar</strong> name."},{"text":"I see shopping mainly as a task, not entertainment. I enjoy it when I know what I need, but crowds and too much choice can make it take longer than necessary.","phrases":[{"en":"necessary","meaning":"Needed for a particular purpose."}],"question":"How do you feel about going shopping?","html":"I see shopping mainly as a task, not entertainment. I enjoy it when I know what I need, but crowds and too much choice can make it take longer than <strong class=\"key-phrase\">necessary</strong>."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-068-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-068-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-068-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-068-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Shopping online and what you dislike about shopping","prompt":"Do you like shopping and why?\nDo you like shopping on the internet?\nWhat don't you like about shopping?\nWhat time do you do the shopping and why?","answer":"Q: Do you like shopping and why?\nA: I don&#x27;t really see shopping as a hobby, but I enjoy it when I&#x27;ve got <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a clear purpose</strong> and enough time to compare things properly. I find <strong class=\"key-phrase\">aimless shopping</strong> tiring rather than relaxing.\n\nQ: Do you like shopping on the internet?\nA: Yes, for everyday products that are easy to compare online. It saves time and gives me more choice, although I still go to actual shops for clothes or anything that needs <strong class=\"key-phrase\">careful inspection</strong>.\n\nQ: What don&#x27;t you like about shopping?\nA: I&#x27;m not keen on misleading discounts, pushy sales staff or long queues. I think a good shop should let you compare things properly and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">make an informed decision</strong>, without all the pressure.\n\nQ: What time do you do the shopping and why?\nA: I usually go shopping early in the morning or on weekday evenings, when it&#x27;s quieter. Avoiding the busy times just makes the whole thing <strong class=\"key-phrase\">far more efficient</strong>.","topic":"Shopping","phrases":[{"en":"a clear purpose","context":"Q: Do you like shopping and why?\nA: I don't really see shopping as a hobby, but I enjoy it when I've got a clear purpose and enough time to compare things properly. I find aimless shopping tiring rather than relaxing."},{"en":"aimless shopping","context":"Q: Do you like shopping and why?\nA: I don't really see shopping as a hobby, but I enjoy it when I've got a clear purpose and enough time to compare things properly. I find aimless shopping tiring rather than relaxing."},{"en":"careful inspection","context":"Q: Do you like shopping on the internet?\nA: Yes, for everyday products that are easy to compare online. It saves time and gives me more choice, although I still go to actual shops for clothes or anything that needs careful inspection."},{"en":"make an informed decision","context":"Q: What don't you like about shopping?\nA: I'm not keen on misleading discounts, pushy sales staff or long queues. I think a good shop should let you compare things properly and make an informed decision, without all the pressure."},{"en":"far more efficient","context":"Q: What time do you do the shopping and why?\nA: I usually go shopping early in the morning or on weekday evenings, when it's quieter. Avoiding the busy times just makes the whole thing far more efficient."}],"subtype":"Part 1","summary":"Shopping","visual":null,"id":"speaking-part-1-069","_displayNo":"#068","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-069-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-069-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-069-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-069-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"I don't treat it as a hobby. It is more enjoyable when I know what I need and have time to compare products. Walking around shops without a purpose makes me tired.","phrases":[{"en":"compare products","meaning":"Look at different items to see how they are similar or different."}],"question":"Do you like shopping and why?","html":"I don&#x27;t treat it as a hobby. It is more enjoyable when I know what I need and have time to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">compare products</strong>. Walking around shops without a purpose makes me tired."},{"text":"Yes, I buy everyday products online when they are easy to compare. It saves time and offers more choice. For clothes or things I need to examine closely, I still visit shops.","phrases":[{"en":"examine closely","meaning":"Look at something carefully to check its details."}],"question":"Do you like shopping on the internet?","html":"Yes, I buy everyday products online when they are easy to compare. It saves time and offers more choice. For clothes or things I need to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">examine closely</strong>, I still visit shops."},{"text":"I dislike discounts that are not really good deals, salespeople who pressure me and long lines. I want time and clear information to choose what is right for me.","phrases":[{"en":"pressure me","meaning":"Try strongly to make me do something."}],"question":"What don't you like about shopping?","html":"I dislike discounts that are not really good deals, salespeople who <strong class=\"key-phrase\">pressure me</strong> and long lines. I want time and clear information to choose what is right for me."},{"text":"I usually shop early in the morning or on weekday evenings because the shops are quieter. It is easier to find what I need and finish quickly then.","phrases":[{"en":"weekday evenings","meaning":"The evenings from Monday to Friday."}],"question":"What time do you do the shopping and why?","html":"I usually shop early in the morning or on <strong class=\"key-phrase\">weekday evenings</strong> because the shops are quieter. It is easier to find what I need and finish quickly then."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-069-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-069-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-069-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-069-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"The sports you do and whether you prefer watching","prompt":"What sports or physical activities do you regularly do?\nWhich sport or game would you like to be good at?\nDo you prefer watching or playing sports?\nDo you think children should be encouraged to do more sport?","answer":"Q: What sports or physical activities do you regularly do?\nA: Unfortunately I don&#x27;t have time to do any sports or physical activities because of my <strong class=\"key-phrase\">work commitments</strong>. I&#x27;d like to find more time for regular exercise.\n\nQ: Which sport or game would you like to be good at?\nA: I would like to be good at tennis because it combines stamina, timing and precise control. Being able to place the ball accurately <strong class=\"key-phrase\">under pressure</strong> would be extremely satisfying.\n\nQ: Do you prefer watching or playing sports?\nA: I don&#x27;t watch much sport on TV and I&#x27;m <strong class=\"key-phrase\">not a big sports fan</strong>, so I think I would probably enjoy doing sports more than watching them.\n\nQ: Do you think children should be encouraged to do more sport?\nA: Yes. Sport helps children develop <strong class=\"key-phrase\">teamwork and resilience</strong>, and it gives them <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a constructive way to use their energy</strong>. The emphasis should be on participation and improvement rather than winning at all costs.","topic":"Sports","phrases":[{"en":"work commitments","context":"Q: What sports or physical activities do you regularly do?\nA: Unfortunately I don't have time to do any sports or physical activities because of my work commitments. I'd like to find more time for regular exercise."},{"en":"under pressure","context":"Q: Which sport or game would you like to be good at?\nA: I would like to be good at tennis because it combines stamina, timing and precise control. Being able to place the ball accurately under pressure would be extremely satisfying."},{"en":"not a big sports fan","context":"Q: Do you prefer watching or playing sports?\nA: I don't watch much sport on TV and I'm not a big sports fan, so I think I would probably enjoy doing sports more than watching them."},{"en":"teamwork and resilience","context":"Q: Do you think children should be encouraged to do more sport?\nA: Yes. Sport helps children develop teamwork and resilience, and it gives them a constructive way to use their energy. The emphasis should be on participation and improvement rather than winning at all costs."},{"en":"a constructive way to use their energy","context":"Q: Do you think children should be encouraged to do more sport?\nA: Yes. Sport helps children develop teamwork and resilience, and it gives them a constructive way to use their energy. The emphasis should be on participation and improvement rather than winning at all costs."}],"subtype":"","summary":"Sports","id":"speaking-part-1-070","_displayNo":"#069","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-070-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-070-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-070-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-070-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"I don't currently do regular sport because work takes up so much time. I'd like to change that and find more time for exercise in my weekly routine.","phrases":[{"en":"takes up","meaning":"Uses an amount of time or space."}],"question":"What sports or physical activities do you regularly do?","html":"I don&#x27;t currently do regular sport because work <strong class=\"key-phrase\">takes up</strong> so much time. I&#x27;d like to change that and find more time for exercise in my weekly routine."},{"text":"I'd like to be good at tennis. You need energy, good timing and control of the ball. I think being able to hit accurately during a difficult game would feel very satisfying.","phrases":[{"en":"accurately","meaning":"Correctly and in the exact place intended."}],"question":"Which sport or game would you like to be good at?","html":"I&#x27;d like to be good at tennis. You need energy, good timing and control of the ball. I think being able to hit <strong class=\"key-phrase\">accurately</strong> during a difficult game would feel very satisfying."},{"text":"I would probably prefer playing. I don't watch much sport on television and I'm not a big fan, but taking part seems more enjoyable than watching other people.","phrases":[{"en":"taking part","meaning":"Joining in and doing an activity yourself."}],"question":"Do you prefer watching or playing sports?","html":"I would probably prefer playing. I don&#x27;t watch much sport on television and I&#x27;m not a big fan, but <strong class=\"key-phrase\">taking part</strong> seems more enjoyable than watching other people."},{"text":"Yes, sport helps children learn to work together and keep trying when things are difficult. It also uses their energy well. Enjoying it and improving should matter more than always winning.","phrases":[{"en":"keep trying","meaning":"Continue making an effort, even when something is difficult."}],"question":"Do you think children should be encouraged to do more sport?","html":"Yes, sport helps children learn to work together and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">keep trying</strong> when things are difficult. It also uses their energy well. Enjoying it and improving should matter more than always winning."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-070-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-070-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-070-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-070-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Watching and taking part in sport","prompt":"Do you like sports?\nDo you enjoy watching sports?\nDo you enjoy participating in any sports?\nWhat is your favourite sports activity?","answer":"Q: Do you like sports?\nA: Yes. I enjoy strength training, swimming and occasionally badminton. I prefer activities where progress can be measured and technique improves through <strong class=\"key-phrase\">consistent practice</strong>.\n\nQ: Do you enjoy watching sports?\nA: I watch major events occasionally, but I&#x27;d rather participate than sit through an entire season. Watching is most enjoyable when I understand the strategy and have <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a reason to care about the result</strong>.\n\nQ: Do you enjoy participating in any sports?\nA: Yes, particularly in individual exercise and casual games with friends. Participation improves my mood and gives me <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a clear physical challenge</strong>.\n\nQ: What is your favourite sports activity?\nA: Strength training&#x27;s my favourite because it supports health, posture and long-term mobility. I also like the fact that progress is gradual and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">easy to track</strong>.","topic":"Sports","phrases":[{"en":"consistent practice","context":"Q: Do you like sports?\nA: Yes. I enjoy strength training, swimming and occasionally badminton. I prefer activities where progress can be measured and technique improves through consistent practice."},{"en":"a reason to care about the result","context":"Q: Do you enjoy watching sports?\nA: I watch major events occasionally, but I'd rather participate than sit through an entire season. Watching is most enjoyable when I understand the strategy and have a reason to care about the result."},{"en":"a clear physical challenge","context":"Q: Do you enjoy participating in any sports?\nA: Yes, particularly in individual exercise and casual games with friends. Participation improves my mood and gives me a clear physical challenge."},{"en":"easy to track","context":"Q: What is your favourite sports activity?\nA: Strength training's my favourite because it supports health, posture and long-term mobility. I also like the fact that progress is gradual and easy to track."}],"subtype":"Part 1","summary":"Sports","visual":null,"id":"speaking-part-1-071","_displayNo":"#070","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-071-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-071-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-071-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-071-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"Yes, I enjoy lifting weights, swimming and sometimes playing badminton. I like activities where regular practice helps me improve and where I can see the progress I make.","phrases":[{"en":"progress","meaning":"Improvement or movement towards a goal."}],"question":"Do you like sports?","html":"Yes, I enjoy lifting weights, swimming and sometimes playing badminton. I like activities where regular practice helps me improve and where I can see the <strong class=\"key-phrase\">progress</strong> I make."},{"text":"I sometimes watch important events, but I prefer doing sport myself. Watching is more interesting when I understand how the game works and care about who wins.","phrases":[{"en":"care about","meaning":"Feel interested in or concerned about something."}],"question":"Do you enjoy watching sports?","html":"I sometimes watch important events, but I prefer doing sport myself. Watching is more interesting when I understand how the game works and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">care about</strong> who wins."},{"text":"Yes, especially exercise I can do by myself and relaxed games with friends. Being active makes me feel happier and gives me a physical goal to work towards.","phrases":[{"en":"work towards","meaning":"Make an effort to reach a goal."}],"question":"Do you enjoy participating in any sports?","html":"Yes, especially exercise I can do by myself and relaxed games with friends. Being active makes me feel happier and gives me a physical goal to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">work towards</strong>."},{"text":"Lifting weights is my favourite. It helps me stay healthy, stand better and keep moving well as I get older. I also enjoy seeing small improvements over time.","phrases":[{"en":"over time","meaning":"Gradually, as time passes."}],"question":"What is your favourite sports activity?","html":"Lifting weights is my favourite. It helps me stay healthy, stand better and keep moving well as I get older. I also enjoy seeing small improvements <strong class=\"key-phrase\">over time</strong>."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-071-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-071-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-071-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-071-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Sports played in your country and local facilities","prompt":"What sports do you like?\nWhat sports are played in your country?\nWhat are the sporting facilities like in your hometown?\nWhat is your favourite sport?","answer":"Q: What sports do you like?\nA: I like badminton and swimming because they&#x27;re both <strong class=\"key-phrase\">accessible and technically demanding</strong>. I also do strength training, although I see that more as structured exercise than a <strong class=\"key-phrase\">competitive sport</strong>.\n\nQ: What sports are played in your country?\nA: Football, badminton, volleyball and running are all common. Football attracts the largest audiences, while badminton&#x27;s easy to play in schools, parks and community spaces, making it <strong class=\"key-phrase\">open to almost anyone</strong>.\n\nQ: What are the sporting facilities like in your hometown?\nA: Facilities have improved, with more private gyms and sports centres than before. Public spaces are still <strong class=\"key-phrase\">unevenly distributed</strong>, so affordable access remains <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a practical concern</strong>.\n\nQ: What is your favourite sport?\nA: Badminton&#x27;s probably my favourite sport because it&#x27;s fast, social and easy to play without expensive equipment. It also <strong class=\"key-phrase\">rewards timing and technique</strong> rather than physical size alone.","topic":"Sports","phrases":[{"en":"accessible and technically demanding","context":"Q: What sports do you like?\nA: I like badminton and swimming because they're both accessible and technically demanding. I also do strength training, although I see that more as structured exercise than a competitive sport."},{"en":"competitive sport","context":"Q: What sports do you like?\nA: I like badminton and swimming because they're both accessible and technically demanding. I also do strength training, although I see that more as structured exercise than a competitive sport."},{"en":"open to almost anyone","context":"Q: What sports are played in your country?\nA: Football, badminton, volleyball and running are all common. Football attracts the largest audiences, while badminton's easy to play in schools, parks and community spaces, making it open to almost anyone."},{"en":"unevenly distributed","context":"Q: What are the sporting facilities like in your hometown?\nA: Facilities have improved, with more private gyms and sports centres than before. Public spaces are still unevenly distributed, so affordable access remains a practical concern."},{"en":"a practical concern","context":"Q: What are the sporting facilities like in your hometown?\nA: Facilities have improved, with more private gyms and sports centres than before. Public spaces are still unevenly distributed, so affordable access remains a practical concern."},{"en":"rewards timing and technique","context":"Q: What is your favourite sport?\nA: Badminton's probably my favourite sport because it's fast, social and easy to play without expensive equipment. It also rewards timing and technique rather than physical size alone."}],"subtype":"Part 1","summary":"Sports","visual":null,"id":"speaking-part-1-072","_displayNo":"#071","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-072-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-072-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-072-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-072-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"I like badminton and swimming because many people can try them, but learning to do them well takes skill. I also lift weights, although I think of that more as exercise.","phrases":[{"en":"takes skill","meaning":"Requires ability developed through practice."}],"question":"What sports do you like?","html":"I like badminton and swimming because many people can try them, but learning to do them well <strong class=\"key-phrase\">takes skill</strong>. I also lift weights, although I think of that more as exercise."},{"text":"Football, badminton, volleyball and running are common. Football has the most spectators, while badminton is easy to play in schools, parks and local spaces, so many people can join in.","phrases":[{"en":"spectators","meaning":"People who watch a sport or event."}],"question":"What sports are played in your country?","html":"Football, badminton, volleyball and running are common. Football has the most <strong class=\"key-phrase\">spectators</strong>, while badminton is easy to play in schools, parks and local spaces, so many people can join in."},{"text":"There are more gyms and sports centres than before, so facilities have improved. However, public places to exercise are not equally available everywhere, and some options are still too expensive for people.","phrases":[{"en":"facilities","meaning":"Places and equipment provided for a particular activity."}],"question":"What are the sporting facilities like in your hometown?","html":"There are more gyms and sports centres than before, so <strong class=\"key-phrase\">facilities</strong> have improved. However, public places to exercise are not equally available everywhere, and some options are still too expensive for people."},{"text":"Badminton is probably my favourite. It is fast and fun to play with others, and you don't need costly equipment. Good timing and skill matter, not just being big or strong.","phrases":[{"en":"equipment","meaning":"The things needed to do a particular activity."}],"question":"What is your favourite sport?","html":"Badminton is probably my favourite. It is fast and fun to play with others, and you don&#x27;t need costly <strong class=\"key-phrase\">equipment</strong>. Good timing and skill matter, not just being big or strong."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-072-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-072-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-072-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-072-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Studying alone or with others, and where","prompt":"Do you like studying?\nDo you prefer to study alone or with others?\nWhere do you prefer to go when you need to study?\nHow do you feel if someone disturbs you when you are studying?","answer":"Q: Do you like studying?\nA: Yes, I like studying because it&#x27;s the best way to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">gain a deeper insight into</strong> any subject. I like reading, learning from others, and trying to understand difficult concepts.\n\nQ: Do you prefer to study alone or with others?\nA: I prefer to study alone because I need to be able to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">concentrate fully</strong>. Other people are a distraction.\n\nQ: Where do you prefer to go when you need to study?\nA: I like to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">find a quiet corner</strong> in my local library; being in an old building and surrounded by books seems to help me to focus on my work.\n\nQ: How do you feel if someone disturbs you when you are studying?\nA: It frustrates me because it <strong class=\"key-phrase\">breaks my concentration</strong>. I prefer to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">avoid distractions</strong> by going somewhere where nobody will interrupt me.","topic":"Study & Education","phrases":[{"en":"gain a deeper insight into","context":"Q: Do you like studying?\nA: Yes, I like studying because it's the best way to gain a deeper insight into any subject. I like reading, learning from others, and trying to understand difficult concepts."},{"en":"concentrate fully","context":"Q: Do you prefer to study alone or with others?\nA: I prefer to study alone because I need to be able to concentrate fully. Other people are a distraction."},{"en":"find a quiet corner","context":"Q: Where do you prefer to go when you need to study?\nA: I like to find a quiet corner in my local library; being in an old building and surrounded by books seems to help me to focus on my work."},{"en":"breaks my concentration","context":"Q: How do you feel if someone disturbs you when you are studying?\nA: It frustrates me because it breaks my concentration. I prefer to avoid distractions by going somewhere where nobody will interrupt me."},{"en":"avoid distractions","context":"Q: How do you feel if someone disturbs you when you are studying?\nA: It frustrates me because it breaks my concentration. I prefer to avoid distractions by going somewhere where nobody will interrupt me."}],"subtype":"","summary":"Study & Education","id":"speaking-part-1-073","_displayNo":"#072","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-073-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-073-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-073-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-073-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"Yes, I enjoy learning because it helps me understand a subject more fully. I like reading, hearing other people's ideas and trying to make sense of difficult topics.","phrases":[{"en":"make sense of","meaning":"Understand something that seems difficult or confusing."}],"question":"Do you like studying?","html":"Yes, I enjoy learning because it helps me understand a subject more fully. I like reading, hearing other people&#x27;s ideas and trying to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">make sense of</strong> difficult topics."},{"text":"I prefer studying alone because I can give the work all my attention. Having other people around can distract me, so I usually learn better on my own.","phrases":[{"en":"on my own","meaning":"Alone, without other people."}],"question":"Do you prefer to study alone or with others?","html":"I prefer studying alone because I can give the work all my attention. Having other people around can distract me, so I usually learn better <strong class=\"key-phrase\">on my own</strong>."},{"text":"I prefer a quiet corner in my local library. The old building and all the books around me create a setting where I find it easier to focus.","phrases":[{"en":"setting","meaning":"The place and surroundings where something happens."}],"question":"Where do you prefer to go when you need to study?","html":"I prefer a quiet corner in my local library. The old building and all the books around me create a <strong class=\"key-phrase\">setting</strong> where I find it easier to focus."},{"text":"I feel annoyed because it makes me lose focus. That is why I try to study somewhere quiet where people are unlikely to interrupt me.","phrases":[{"en":"interrupt","meaning":"Stop someone while they are doing something."}],"question":"How do you feel if someone disturbs you when you are studying?","html":"I feel annoyed because it makes me lose focus. That is why I try to study somewhere quiet where people are unlikely to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">interrupt</strong> me."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-073-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-073-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-073-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-073-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Your time at school and the subjects you liked","prompt":"Do you enjoy your time at school?\nWould you recommend your school to others?\nWhat subject did you find most interesting when you were at school?\nApart from classes, what else did you enjoy at school?","answer":"Q: Do you enjoy your time at school?\nA: Overall, yes. School gave me close friendships and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a strong academic foundation</strong>, although the exam pressure wasn&#x27;t always easy to handle. Looking back, it was <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a valuable learning experience</strong>.\n\nQ: Would you recommend your school to others?\nA: I&#x27;d recommend it, mainly because the teachers were committed and the environment was disciplined without being hostile. No school&#x27;s perfect, but it offered <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a supportive environment</strong>.\n\nQ: What subject did you find most interesting when you were at school?\nA: English was the most interesting subject for me because it opened access to books, films and people from other countries. It felt like <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a practical skill</strong> I&#x27;d keep using, not just something for exams.\n\nQ: Apart from classes, what else did you enjoy at school?\nA: I enjoyed clubs, school trips and informal time with classmates. Those activities developed confidence and teamwork in ways that ordinary lessons couldn&#x27;t <strong class=\"key-phrase\">fully replicate</strong>.","topic":"Study & Education","phrases":[{"en":"a strong academic foundation","context":"Q: Do you enjoy your time at school?\nA: Overall, yes. School gave me close friendships and a strong academic foundation, although the exam pressure wasn't always easy to handle. Looking back, it was a valuable learning experience."},{"en":"a valuable learning experience","context":"Q: Do you enjoy your time at school?\nA: Overall, yes. School gave me close friendships and a strong academic foundation, although the exam pressure wasn't always easy to handle. Looking back, it was a valuable learning experience."},{"en":"a supportive environment","context":"Q: Would you recommend your school to others?\nA: I'd recommend it, mainly because the teachers were committed and the environment was disciplined without being hostile. No school's perfect, but it offered a supportive environment."},{"en":"a practical skill","context":"Q: What subject did you find most interesting when you were at school?\nA: English was the most interesting subject for me because it opened access to books, films and people from other countries. It felt like a practical skill I'd keep using, not just something for exams."},{"en":"fully replicate","context":"Q: Apart from classes, what else did you enjoy at school?\nA: I enjoyed clubs, school trips and informal time with classmates. Those activities developed confidence and teamwork in ways that ordinary lessons couldn't fully replicate."}],"subtype":"Part 1","summary":"Study & Education","visual":null,"id":"speaking-part-1-074","_displayNo":"#073","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-074-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-074-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-074-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-074-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"Overall, I enjoyed school. I made close friends and learned useful knowledge and skills. Exams were stressful sometimes, but looking back, I think school was a valuable experience.","phrases":[{"en":"looking back","meaning":"Thinking about something that happened in the past."}],"question":"Do you enjoy your time at school?","html":"Overall, I enjoyed school. I made close friends and learned useful knowledge and skills. Exams were stressful sometimes, but <strong class=\"key-phrase\">looking back</strong>, I think school was a valuable experience."},{"text":"Yes, mainly because the teachers worked hard and supported us. The school had clear rules, but it wasn't an unfriendly place. It had problems like any school, but I would still recommend it.","phrases":[{"en":"recommend","meaning":"Suggest that something is a good choice."}],"question":"Would you recommend your school to others?","html":"Yes, mainly because the teachers worked hard and supported us. The school had clear rules, but it wasn&#x27;t an unfriendly place. It had problems like any school, but I would still <strong class=\"key-phrase\">recommend</strong> it."},{"text":"English interested me most. It helped me understand books and films and communicate with people from other countries. I could see how I would use it outside school as well as in exams.","phrases":[{"en":"communicate","meaning":"Share information, ideas or feelings with other people."}],"question":"What subject did you find most interesting when you were at school?","html":"English interested me most. It helped me understand books and films and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">communicate</strong> with people from other countries. I could see how I would use it outside school as well as in exams."},{"text":"I enjoyed clubs, trips and spending time with classmates outside lessons. These experiences helped me become more confident and learn to work with others in a different way.","phrases":[{"en":"classmates","meaning":"Other students in the same class as you."}],"question":"Apart from classes, what else did you enjoy at school?","html":"I enjoyed clubs, trips and spending time with <strong class=\"key-phrase\">classmates</strong> outside lessons. These experiences helped me become more confident and learn to work with others in a different way."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-074-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-074-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-074-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-074-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"What you studied and your favourite subject","prompt":"What have you studied?\nWhat was your major?\nWhat kind of school did you attend?\nWhat was your favourite subject?","answer":"Q: What have you studied?\nA: I&#x27;ve studied English language and teaching. The course combined linguistics, classroom methods and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">practical training</strong>, so it gave me both theory and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">practical experience</strong>.\n\nQ: What was your major?\nA: My major was English education. I&#x27;d always been interested in language, and I wanted a career where communication would <strong class=\"key-phrase\">play a central role</strong>.\n\nQ: What kind of school did you attend?\nA: I attended a state school with a fairly traditional structure — classes were teacher-led, but that didn&#x27;t stop good teachers from encouraging questions and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">critical thinking</strong>.\n\nQ: What was your favourite subject?\nA: English was my favourite subject because progress was practical and visible. Each new skill gave me access to more books, conversations and professional opportunities <strong class=\"key-phrase\">well beyond the classroom</strong>.","topic":"Study & Education","phrases":[{"en":"practical training","context":"Q: What have you studied?\nA: I've studied English language and teaching. The course combined linguistics, classroom methods and practical training, so it gave me both theory and practical experience."},{"en":"practical experience","context":"Q: What have you studied?\nA: I've studied English language and teaching. The course combined linguistics, classroom methods and practical training, so it gave me both theory and practical experience."},{"en":"play a central role","context":"Q: What was your major?\nA: My major was English education. I'd always been interested in language, and I wanted a career where communication would play a central role."},{"en":"critical thinking","context":"Q: What kind of school did you attend?\nA: I attended a state school with a fairly traditional structure — classes were teacher-led, but that didn't stop good teachers from encouraging questions and critical thinking."},{"en":"well beyond the classroom","context":"Q: What was your favourite subject?\nA: English was my favourite subject because progress was practical and visible. Each new skill gave me access to more books, conversations and professional opportunities well beyond the classroom."}],"subtype":"Part 1","summary":"Study & Education","visual":null,"id":"speaking-part-1-075","_displayNo":"#074","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-075-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-075-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-075-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-075-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"I studied English and teaching. My course included how language works, ways to teach a class and practical training, so I learned ideas and had chances to use them.","phrases":[{"en":"practical training","meaning":"Learning by practising the skills needed for real work."}],"question":"What have you studied?","html":"I studied English and teaching. My course included how language works, ways to teach a class and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">practical training</strong>, so I learned ideas and had chances to use them."},{"text":"I majored in English education. I had always liked languages and wanted a job where speaking with people and explaining ideas would be important parts of my work.","phrases":[{"en":"majored in","meaning":"Studied a subject as the main part of a university course."}],"question":"What was your major?","html":"I <strong class=\"key-phrase\">majored in</strong> English education. I had always liked languages and wanted a job where speaking with people and explaining ideas would be important parts of my work."},{"text":"I went to a state school. Lessons were usually led by the teacher, but good teachers still encouraged us to ask questions and think carefully about ideas.","phrases":[{"en":"state school","meaning":"A school funded and run through the government."}],"question":"What kind of school did you attend?","html":"I went to a <strong class=\"key-phrase\">state school</strong>. Lessons were usually led by the teacher, but good teachers still encouraged us to ask questions and think carefully about ideas."},{"text":"English was my favourite because I could use each new skill in real life. As I improved, I could read more, have more conversations and see more possibilities for future work.","phrases":[{"en":"possibilities","meaning":"Things that may happen or choices that may become available."}],"question":"What was your favourite subject?","html":"English was my favourite because I could use each new skill in real life. As I improved, I could read more, have more conversations and see more <strong class=\"key-phrase\">possibilities</strong> for future work."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-075-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-075-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-075-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-075-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"How often you call and who you talk to","prompt":"How often do you make telephone calls?\nWho do you spend most time talking to on the telephone?\nWhen do you think you'll next make a telephone call?\nDo you sometimes prefer to send a text message instead of telephoning?","answer":"Q: How often do you make telephone calls?\nA: I probably make three or four phone calls every day, usually just to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">make arrangements with</strong> work colleagues or to speak to family and friends.\n\nQ: Who do you spend most time talking to on the telephone?\nA: I think it would be one of my closest work colleagues. We often call each other rather than meeting <strong class=\"key-phrase\">face-to-face</strong>.\n\nQ: When do you think you&#x27;ll next make a telephone call?\nA: My family are expecting me to phone them as soon as I finish this exam. They&#x27;ll want to know <strong class=\"key-phrase\">how it went</strong>.\n\nQ: Do you sometimes prefer to send a text message instead of telephoning?\nA: Yes. For a simple arrangement, a text message is <strong class=\"key-phrase\">more efficient than a phone call</strong> because both people can <strong class=\"key-phrase\">deal with it in their own time</strong>. I still call when it&#x27;s urgent or needs a proper discussion.","topic":"Telephoning","phrases":[{"en":"make arrangements with","context":"Q: How often do you make telephone calls?\nA: I probably make three or four phone calls every day, usually just to make arrangements with work colleagues or to speak to family and friends."},{"en":"face-to-face","context":"Q: Who do you spend most time talking to on the telephone?\nA: I think it would be one of my closest work colleagues. We often call each other rather than meeting face-to-face."},{"en":"how it went","context":"Q: When do you think you'll next make a telephone call?\nA: My family are expecting me to phone them as soon as I finish this exam. They'll want to know how it went."},{"en":"more efficient than a phone call","context":"Q: Do you sometimes prefer to send a text message instead of telephoning?\nA: Yes. For a simple arrangement, a text message is more efficient than a phone call because both people can deal with it in their own time. I still call when it's urgent or needs a proper discussion."},{"en":"deal with it in their own time","context":"Q: Do you sometimes prefer to send a text message instead of telephoning?\nA: Yes. For a simple arrangement, a text message is more efficient than a phone call because both people can deal with it in their own time. I still call when it's urgent or needs a proper discussion."}],"subtype":"","summary":"Telephoning","id":"speaking-part-1-076","_displayNo":"#075","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-076-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-076-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-076-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-076-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"I make about three or four calls a day. Most are to arrange things with people at work or to speak to family and friends, so they are usually part of everyday life.","phrases":[{"en":"arrange things","meaning":"Make plans or organise what needs to happen."}],"question":"How often do you make telephone calls?","html":"I make about three or four calls a day. Most are to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">arrange things</strong> with people at work or to speak to family and friends, so they are usually part of everyday life."},{"text":"Probably one of my closest colleagues. We often phone each other instead of meeting in person, so I spend more time on the phone with that person than with most others.","phrases":[{"en":"colleagues","meaning":"People you work with."}],"question":"Who do you spend most time talking to on the telephone?","html":"Probably one of my closest <strong class=\"key-phrase\">colleagues</strong>. We often phone each other instead of meeting in person, so I spend more time on the phone with that person than with most others."},{"text":"I'll probably call my family as soon as this exam finishes. They are expecting to hear from me because they want to know how it went.","phrases":[{"en":"expecting","meaning":"Thinking or waiting for something to happen."}],"question":"When do you think you'll next make a telephone call?","html":"I&#x27;ll probably call my family as soon as this exam finishes. They are <strong class=\"key-phrase\">expecting</strong> to hear from me because they want to know how it went."},{"text":"Yes, for simple plans I prefer texting because each person can reply when they are free. I still phone if something is urgent or we need to discuss it properly.","phrases":[{"en":"urgent","meaning":"Needing attention or action very soon."}],"question":"Do you sometimes prefer to send a text message instead of telephoning?","html":"Yes, for simple plans I prefer texting because each person can reply when they are free. I still phone if something is <strong class=\"key-phrase\">urgent</strong> or we need to discuss it properly."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-076-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-076-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-076-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-076-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"How much television you watch, and your favourite programme","prompt":"Do you watch a lot of TV?\nTell me about television in your country?\nWhat is your favourite TV programme?\nIs TV more important to you now than in the past?","answer":"Q: Do you watch a lot of TV?\nA: No, not much. I&#x27;d rather watch selected programmes online than follow a fixed television schedule, because that way I can choose content and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">avoid passive viewing</strong>.\n\nQ: Tell me about television in your country?\nA: Television&#x27;s still got a broad audience for news, sport and major entertainment programmes, but younger viewers increasingly stream content, so broadcasters are adapting to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">changing viewing habits</strong>.\n\nQ: What is your favourite TV programme?\nA: I enjoy well-produced documentaries about science and society. They&#x27;ve got strong visuals and reliable explanations, and they often <strong class=\"key-phrase\">put complex issues into perspective</strong>.\n\nQ: Is TV more important to you now than in the past?\nA: It&#x27;s less important to me now because I can access information and entertainment on demand. Television&#x27;s become just one option among many rather than <strong class=\"key-phrase\">the centre of home entertainment</strong>.","topic":"Television","phrases":[{"en":"avoid passive viewing","context":"Q: Do you watch a lot of TV?\nA: No, not much. I'd rather watch selected programmes online than follow a fixed television schedule, because that way I can choose content and avoid passive viewing."},{"en":"changing viewing habits","context":"Q: Tell me about television in your country?\nA: Television's still got a broad audience for news, sport and major entertainment programmes, but younger viewers increasingly stream content, so broadcasters are adapting to changing viewing habits."},{"en":"put complex issues into perspective","context":"Q: What is your favourite TV programme?\nA: I enjoy well-produced documentaries about science and society. They've got strong visuals and reliable explanations, and they often put complex issues into perspective."},{"en":"the centre of home entertainment","context":"Q: Is TV more important to you now than in the past?\nA: It's less important to me now because I can access information and entertainment on demand. Television's become just one option among many rather than the centre of home entertainment."}],"subtype":"Part 1","summary":"Television","visual":null,"id":"speaking-part-1-077","_displayNo":"#076","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-077-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-077-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-077-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-077-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"No, I don't watch much. I prefer choosing programmes online and watching when I want, rather than following a TV schedule or watching whatever happens to be on.","phrases":[{"en":"schedule","meaning":"A plan showing when programmes or activities happen."}],"question":"Do you watch a lot of TV?","html":"No, I don&#x27;t watch much. I prefer choosing programmes online and watching when I want, rather than following a TV <strong class=\"key-phrase\">schedule</strong> or watching whatever happens to be on."},{"text":"Many people still watch TV for news, sport and big entertainment shows. Younger people often choose programmes online, so television companies are changing how they provide their content.","phrases":[{"en":"content","meaning":"Programmes, videos or other material that people watch or read."}],"question":"Tell me about television in your country?","html":"Many people still watch TV for news, sport and big entertainment shows. Younger people often choose programmes online, so television companies are changing how they provide their <strong class=\"key-phrase\">content</strong>."},{"text":"I especially enjoy documentaries about science and society. Good pictures and clear, trustworthy explanations help me understand complicated subjects and see why they matter.","phrases":[{"en":"trustworthy","meaning":"Able to be believed or relied on."}],"question":"What is your favourite TV programme?","html":"I especially enjoy documentaries about science and society. Good pictures and clear, <strong class=\"key-phrase\">trustworthy</strong> explanations help me understand complicated subjects and see why they matter."},{"text":"No, it is less important now. I can find information and entertainment online whenever I want. Television is still useful, but it is only one of several choices at home.","phrases":[{"en":"whenever I want","meaning":"At any time I choose."}],"question":"Is TV more important to you now than in the past?","html":"No, it is less important now. I can find information and entertainment online <strong class=\"key-phrase\">whenever I want</strong>. Television is still useful, but it is only one of several choices at home."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-077-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-077-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-077-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-077-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"The toys you played with as a child","prompt":"Did you play with toys when you were a child?\nWhat kinds of toys did you like?\nIn your country, do boys and girls play with the same types of toys?\nDo you think that toys help children to learn?","answer":"Q: Did you play with toys when you were a child?\nA: Yes, of course. I loved <strong class=\"key-phrase\">playing with toys</strong> when I was a child; I think all children do.\n\nQ: What kinds of toys did you like?\nA: <strong class=\"key-phrase\">As far as I remember</strong>, I mostly played with toy cars, planes and action figures from films or cartoons. I also liked building things with Lego.\n\nQ: In your country, do boys and girls play with the same types of toys?\nA: Not really. I think boys like the kinds of toys that I mentioned before, whereas girls play with dolls. My niece, for example, doesn&#x27;t like toy cars; she prefers dressing dolls in <strong class=\"key-phrase\">different outfits</strong>.\n\nQ: Do you think that toys help children to learn?\nA: Yes, I do. All toys encourage children to use their <strong class=\"key-phrase\">imagination and creativity</strong>. Even with simple toys, children imagine situations and invent games and rules.","topic":"Toys","phrases":[{"en":"playing with toys","context":"Q: Did you play with toys when you were a child?\nA: Yes, of course. I loved playing with toys when I was a child; I think all children do."},{"en":"As far as I remember","context":"Q: What kinds of toys did you like?\nA: As far as I remember, I mostly played with toy cars, planes and action figures from films or cartoons. I also liked building things with Lego."},{"en":"different outfits","context":"Q: In your country, do boys and girls play with the same types of toys?\nA: Not really. I think boys like the kinds of toys that I mentioned before, whereas girls play with dolls. My niece, for example, doesn't like toy cars; she prefers dressing dolls in different outfits."},{"en":"imagination and creativity","context":"Q: Do you think that toys help children to learn?\nA: Yes, I do. All toys encourage children to use their imagination and creativity. Even with simple toys, children imagine situations and invent games and rules."}],"subtype":"","summary":"Toys","id":"speaking-part-1-078","_displayNo":"#077","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-078-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-078-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-078-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-078-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"Yes, I loved playing with toys as a child. They were an enjoyable part of my childhood, and I think many other children feel the same way.","phrases":[{"en":"childhood","meaning":"The time in your life when you were a child."}],"question":"Did you play with toys when you were a child?","html":"Yes, I loved playing with toys as a child. They were an enjoyable part of my <strong class=\"key-phrase\">childhood</strong>, and I think many other children feel the same way."},{"text":"I remember playing mostly with toy cars, planes and figures from films or cartoons. I also liked Lego because I could use the pieces to build different things.","phrases":[{"en":"figures","meaning":"Small models shaped like people or characters."}],"question":"What kinds of toys did you like?","html":"I remember playing mostly with toy cars, planes and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">figures</strong> from films or cartoons. I also liked Lego because I could use the pieces to build different things."},{"text":"Not always. Many boys choose cars or action figures, while some girls prefer dolls. For example, my niece likes putting different clothes on dolls rather than playing with toy cars, although every child is different.","phrases":[{"en":"action figures","meaning":"Small toy models of characters from films, games or stories."}],"question":"In your country, do boys and girls play with the same types of toys?","html":"Not always. Many boys choose cars or <strong class=\"key-phrase\">action figures</strong>, while some girls prefer dolls. For example, my niece likes putting different clothes on dolls rather than playing with toy cars, although every child is different."},{"text":"Yes, toys can help children use their imagination and make new things. Even simple toys let them create situations and invent their own games and rules.","phrases":[{"en":"invent","meaning":"Think of or create something new."}],"question":"Do you think that toys help children to learn?","html":"Yes, toys can help children use their imagination and make new things. Even simple toys let them create situations and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">invent</strong> their own games and rules."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-078-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-078-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-078-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-078-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Public transport where you live","prompt":"Do you use public transport?\nWhich type of public transport do you prefer?\nHow good is the public transport where you live?\nDo you think people should use public transport more?","answer":"Q: Do you use public transport?\nA: These days I mostly drive, and the main reason is that my usual journeys are much faster by car. For example, the half-hour drive that I do twice a week would take me <strong class=\"key-phrase\">three times as long</strong> by train and bus.\n\nQ: Which type of public transport do you prefer?\nA: I definitely prefer the train. I like being able to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">stroll up and down</strong>, and on some trains I can book a seat with a table and a socket, so that I can do some work.\n\nQ: How good is the public transport where you live?\nA: It&#x27;s quite good. There&#x27;s a train station not far from my house, and it&#x27;s <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a direct line</strong> straight into the city centre. There are lots of bus routes too, and there&#x27;s even a tram network in the centre of Manchester.\n\nQ: Do you think people should use public transport more?\nA: Yes, as long as it&#x27;s convenient for them. Public transport is obviously more <strong class=\"key-phrase\">environmentally friendly</strong> than private cars, so we could <strong class=\"key-phrase\">reduce air pollution</strong> by using it more.","topic":"Transport","phrases":[{"en":"three times as long","context":"Q: Do you use public transport?\nA: These days I mostly drive, and the main reason is that my usual journeys are much faster by car. For example, the half-hour drive that I do twice a week would take me three times as long by train and bus."},{"en":"stroll up and down","context":"Q: Which type of public transport do you prefer?\nA: I definitely prefer the train. I like being able to stroll up and down, and on some trains I can book a seat with a table and a socket, so that I can do some work."},{"en":"a direct line","context":"Q: How good is the public transport where you live?\nA: It's quite good. There's a train station not far from my house, and it's a direct line straight into the city centre. There are lots of bus routes too, and there's even a tram network in the centre of Manchester."},{"en":"environmentally friendly","context":"Q: Do you think people should use public transport more?\nA: Yes, as long as it's convenient for them. Public transport is obviously more environmentally friendly than private cars, so we could reduce air pollution by using it more."},{"en":"reduce air pollution","context":"Q: Do you think people should use public transport more?\nA: Yes, as long as it's convenient for them. Public transport is obviously more environmentally friendly than private cars, so we could reduce air pollution by using it more."}],"subtype":"","summary":"Transport","id":"speaking-part-1-079","_displayNo":"#078","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-079-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-079-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-079-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-079-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"I mainly drive now because it is faster for my usual trips. A journey I make twice a week takes half an hour by car but about three times longer by train and bus.","phrases":[{"en":"usual trips","meaning":"The journeys you normally make."}],"question":"Do you use public transport?","html":"I mainly drive now because it is faster for my <strong class=\"key-phrase\">usual trips</strong>. A journey I make twice a week takes half an hour by car but about three times longer by train and bus."},{"text":"I prefer trains because I can get up and walk around. On some, I can reserve a seat with a table and a power socket, which lets me work during the journey.","phrases":[{"en":"reserve a seat","meaning":"Arrange in advance to have a particular place to sit."}],"question":"Which type of public transport do you prefer?","html":"I prefer trains because I can get up and walk around. On some, I can <strong class=\"key-phrase\">reserve a seat</strong> with a table and a power socket, which lets me work during the journey."},{"text":"It is quite good. A nearby station has trains straight to the city centre, and there are many bus routes. Central Manchester also has trams, so there are several ways to travel.","phrases":[{"en":"trams","meaning":"Passenger vehicles that travel on rails along city streets."}],"question":"How good is the public transport where you live?","html":"It is quite good. A nearby station has trains straight to the city centre, and there are many bus routes. Central Manchester also has <strong class=\"key-phrase\">trams</strong>, so there are several ways to travel."},{"text":"Yes, if it is convenient for their journeys. Using buses and trains instead of separate cars can reduce pollution, so I think it is a good choice when people can manage it.","phrases":[{"en":"convenient","meaning":"Easy and suitable for your needs."}],"question":"Do you think people should use public transport more?","html":"Yes, if it is <strong class=\"key-phrase\">convenient</strong> for their journeys. Using buses and trains instead of separate cars can reduce pollution, so I think it is a good choice when people can manage it."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-079-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-079-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-079-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-079-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"The transport system and traffic in your hometown","prompt":"Can you describe the transport system in your hometown?\nWhat is the most common means of transport in your country?\nDo traffic jams often occur in your city?\nHow can we solve this problem?","answer":"Q: Can you describe the transport system in your hometown?\nA: Hanoi relies heavily on motorbikes, buses, cars and an expanding metro system. The network&#x27;s improving, but transfers between different modes still need to become <strong class=\"key-phrase\">more seamless</strong>.\n\nQ: What is the most common means of transport in your country?\nA: Motorbikes are still the most common personal vehicle because they&#x27;re flexible in dense streets. Buses and the metro are increasingly important for people who want to avoid <strong class=\"key-phrase\">the cost of driving</strong>.\n\nQ: Do traffic jams often occur in your city?\nA: Yes, especially during morning and evening peaks. Rapid urban growth and high private-vehicle use have placed <strong class=\"key-phrase\">considerable pressure</strong> on roads that weren&#x27;t built to handle this many vehicles.\n\nQ: How can we solve this problem?\nA: The city needs frequent public transport, safe walking routes and better traffic management. Restrictions on private vehicles won&#x27;t work unless people have <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a reliable alternative</strong>.","topic":"Transport","phrases":[{"en":"more seamless","context":"Q: Can you describe the transport system in your hometown?\nA: Hanoi relies heavily on motorbikes, buses, cars and an expanding metro system. The network's improving, but transfers between different modes still need to become more seamless."},{"en":"the cost of driving","context":"Q: What is the most common means of transport in your country?\nA: Motorbikes are still the most common personal vehicle because they're flexible in dense streets. Buses and the metro are increasingly important for people who want to avoid the cost of driving."},{"en":"considerable pressure","context":"Q: Do traffic jams often occur in your city?\nA: Yes, especially during morning and evening peaks. Rapid urban growth and high private-vehicle use have placed considerable pressure on roads that weren't built to handle this many vehicles."},{"en":"a reliable alternative","context":"Q: How can we solve this problem?\nA: The city needs frequent public transport, safe walking routes and better traffic management. Restrictions on private vehicles won't work unless people have a reliable alternative."}],"subtype":"Part 1","summary":"Transport","visual":null,"id":"speaking-part-1-080","_displayNo":"#079","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-080-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-080-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-080-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-080-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"People in Hanoi use motorbikes, buses and cars, and the metro is growing. Transport is improving, but changing from one type to another still needs to become easier.","phrases":[{"en":"metro","meaning":"A city train system, often partly underground or above street level."}],"question":"Can you describe the transport system in your hometown?","html":"People in Hanoi use motorbikes, buses and cars, and the <strong class=\"key-phrase\">metro</strong> is growing. Transport is improving, but changing from one type to another still needs to become easier."},{"text":"Motorbikes are still very common because they are easy to use in crowded streets. Buses and the metro are becoming important too, especially for people who want to spend less on travel.","phrases":[{"en":"crowded streets","meaning":"Roads with many people or vehicles using them."}],"question":"What is the most common means of transport in your country?","html":"Motorbikes are still very common because they are easy to use in <strong class=\"key-phrase\">crowded streets</strong>. Buses and the metro are becoming important too, especially for people who want to spend less on travel."},{"text":"Yes, especially when people travel to work and home again. The city has grown quickly and there are many private vehicles, while the roads do not have enough space for them all.","phrases":[{"en":"private vehicles","meaning":"Cars or motorbikes used by individuals rather than shared public services."}],"question":"Do traffic jams often occur in your city?","html":"Yes, especially when people travel to work and home again. The city has grown quickly and there are many <strong class=\"key-phrase\">private vehicles</strong>, while the roads do not have enough space for them all."},{"text":"We need buses and trains that run often, safe places to walk and better control of traffic. Before limiting private vehicles, the city should give people other dependable ways to travel.","phrases":[{"en":"dependable","meaning":"Able to be trusted to work well when needed."}],"question":"How can we solve this problem?","html":"We need buses and trains that run often, safe places to walk and better control of traffic. Before limiting private vehicles, the city should give people other <strong class=\"key-phrase\">dependable</strong> ways to travel."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-080-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-080-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-080-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-080-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Holidays: travelling or staying at home","prompt":"Do you like holidays?\nDo you prefer to travel or stay at home during holiday periods?\nWhat do most people do during their holidays in your country?\nWhen do you prefer to take your holidays?","answer":"Q: Do you like holidays?\nA: Yes, I love holidays because I get the chance to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">take a break</strong> from work, to relax and unwind, and to spend time with my family.\n\nQ: Do you prefer to travel or stay at home during holiday periods?\nA: If I can I prefer to travel. It&#x27;s nice to get away from everything and to have <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a change of scenery</strong>. Also, I like visiting new places and doing some sightseeing.\n\nQ: What do most people do during their holidays in your country?\nA: During the summer especially, I think most British people go somewhere hot and sunny, to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">escape from the British weather</strong>!\n\nQ: When do you prefer to take your holidays?\nA: I like taking my holidays just <strong class=\"key-phrase\">outside the main summer season</strong>, which is July and August. If you go on holiday in May, June or September, everything is cheaper and places aren&#x27;t so crowded with tourists.","topic":"Travel & Holidays","phrases":[{"en":"take a break","context":"Q: Do you like holidays?\nA: Yes, I love holidays because I get the chance to take a break from work, to relax and unwind, and to spend time with my family."},{"en":"a change of scenery","context":"Q: Do you prefer to travel or stay at home during holiday periods?\nA: If I can I prefer to travel. It's nice to get away from everything and to have a change of scenery. Also, I like visiting new places and doing some sightseeing."},{"en":"escape from the British weather","context":"Q: What do most people do during their holidays in your country?\nA: During the summer especially, I think most British people go somewhere hot and sunny, to escape from the British weather!"},{"en":"outside the main summer season","context":"Q: When do you prefer to take your holidays?\nA: I like taking my holidays just outside the main summer season, which is July and August. If you go on holiday in May, June or September, everything is cheaper and places aren't so crowded with tourists."}],"subtype":"","summary":"Travel & Holidays","id":"speaking-part-1-081","_displayNo":"#080","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-081-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-081-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-081-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-081-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"Yes, I love holidays. They give me time away from work to relax and spend time with my family, which helps me feel refreshed before returning to my routine.","phrases":[{"en":"refreshed","meaning":"Feeling rested and ready to do things again."}],"question":"Do you like holidays?","html":"Yes, I love holidays. They give me time away from work to relax and spend time with my family, which helps me feel <strong class=\"key-phrase\">refreshed</strong> before returning to my routine."},{"text":"I prefer travelling if I can. Visiting new places gives me a break from my usual surroundings, and I enjoy looking around and seeing interesting sights.","phrases":[{"en":"surroundings","meaning":"The places and things around you."}],"question":"Do you prefer to travel or stay at home during holiday periods?","html":"I prefer travelling if I can. Visiting new places gives me a break from my usual <strong class=\"key-phrase\">surroundings</strong>, and I enjoy looking around and seeing interesting sights."},{"text":"I think many British people like going somewhere warm and sunny, especially in summer. They enjoy taking a break from the weather at home during their holidays.","phrases":[{"en":"taking a break from","meaning":"Spending some time away from something you usually experience."}],"question":"What do most people do during their holidays in your country?","html":"I think many British people like going somewhere warm and sunny, especially in summer. They enjoy <strong class=\"key-phrase\">taking a break from</strong> the weather at home during their holidays."},{"text":"I prefer May, June or September, just before or after the busiest summer months. Prices are usually lower and there are fewer tourists, so the trip feels more relaxed.","phrases":[{"en":"tourists","meaning":"People visiting a place for pleasure."}],"question":"When do you prefer to take your holidays?","html":"I prefer May, June or September, just before or after the busiest summer months. Prices are usually lower and there are fewer <strong class=\"key-phrase\">tourists</strong>, so the trip feels more relaxed."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-081-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-081-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-081-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-081-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"How you travel and what you do while travelling","prompt":"What form of transport do you prefer to use?\nHow much time do you spend travelling on a normal day?\nWhat do you do while you are travelling?\nDo you ever have problems with transport?","answer":"Q: What form of transport do you prefer to use?\nA: I prefer to travel by car because it means that I <strong class=\"key-phrase\">have my own space</strong>. Also, the buses and trains in my city are usually <strong class=\"key-phrase\">packed out</strong>; my car&#x27;s much more comfortable.\n\nQ: How much time do you spend travelling on a normal day?\nA: I probably spend about an hour and a half travelling to and from work. I travel during <strong class=\"key-phrase\">the rush hour</strong>, so there&#x27;s quite a lot of traffic.\n\nQ: What do you do while you are travelling?\nA: I usually listen to the radio or a CD. In the morning I like to listen to the news to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">find out what is happening</strong> in the world.\n\nQ: Do you ever have problems with transport?\nA: Yes, as I said, I <strong class=\"key-phrase\">get stuck in traffic</strong> on my way to and from work. I used to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">get annoyed by</strong> traffic jams, but now I&#x27;m used to them.","topic":"Travel & Holidays","phrases":[{"en":"have my own space","context":"Q: What form of transport do you prefer to use?\nA: I prefer to travel by car because it means that I have my own space. Also, the buses and trains in my city are usually packed out; my car's much more comfortable."},{"en":"packed out","context":"Q: What form of transport do you prefer to use?\nA: I prefer to travel by car because it means that I have my own space. Also, the buses and trains in my city are usually packed out; my car's much more comfortable."},{"en":"the rush hour","context":"Q: How much time do you spend travelling on a normal day?\nA: I probably spend about an hour and a half travelling to and from work. I travel during the rush hour, so there's quite a lot of traffic."},{"en":"find out what is happening","context":"Q: What do you do while you are travelling?\nA: I usually listen to the radio or a CD. In the morning I like to listen to the news to find out what is happening in the world."},{"en":"get stuck in traffic","context":"Q: Do you ever have problems with transport?\nA: Yes, as I said, I get stuck in traffic on my way to and from work. I used to get annoyed by traffic jams, but now I'm used to them."},{"en":"get annoyed by","context":"Q: Do you ever have problems with transport?\nA: Yes, as I said, I get stuck in traffic on my way to and from work. I used to get annoyed by traffic jams, but now I'm used to them."}],"subtype":"","summary":"Travel & Holidays","id":"speaking-part-1-082","_displayNo":"#081","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-082-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-082-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-082-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-082-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"I prefer travelling by car because I have my own space and feel more comfortable. The buses and trains in my city are often very crowded, which makes them less pleasant for me.","phrases":[{"en":"my own space","meaning":"An area where I can feel comfortable without being crowded by others."}],"question":"What form of transport do you prefer to use?","html":"I prefer travelling by car because I have <strong class=\"key-phrase\">my own space</strong> and feel more comfortable. The buses and trains in my city are often very crowded, which makes them less pleasant for me."},{"text":"I spend about an hour and a half going to work and coming home each day. I travel at busy times, so traffic adds quite a lot to the journey.","phrases":[{"en":"busy times","meaning":"Periods when many people are doing the same activity or travelling."}],"question":"How much time do you spend travelling on a normal day?","html":"I spend about an hour and a half going to work and coming home each day. I travel at <strong class=\"key-phrase\">busy times</strong>, so traffic adds quite a lot to the journey."},{"text":"I usually listen to the radio or a CD while travelling. In the morning, I like hearing the news so I know what is happening in the world.","phrases":[{"en":"the news","meaning":"Reports about recent events."}],"question":"What do you do while you are travelling?","html":"I usually listen to the radio or a CD while travelling. In the morning, I like hearing <strong class=\"key-phrase\">the news</strong> so I know what is happening in the world."},{"text":"Yes, I often get delayed by traffic on my way to and from work. It used to annoy me a lot, but it happens so often that I'm used to it now.","phrases":[{"en":"used to it","meaning":"Familiar with something so it no longer feels unusual or surprising."}],"question":"Do you ever have problems with transport?","html":"Yes, I often get delayed by traffic on my way to and from work. It used to annoy me a lot, but it happens so often that I&#x27;m <strong class=\"key-phrase\">used to it</strong> now."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-082-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-082-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-082-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-082-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Travelling alone or with friends","prompt":"Do you like travelling? Why?\nDo you like to travel alone or with your friends?\nWhich other places have you travelled to?\nWhat do you usually do when you first arrive in a new place?","answer":"Q: Do you like travelling? Why?\nA: Yes, because it&#x27;s a break from my usual routine and it exposes me to different ways of living. Even a short trip can <strong class=\"key-phrase\">broaden my horizons</strong> if I <strong class=\"key-phrase\">pay attention to</strong> the place rather than simply taking photographs.\n\nQ: Do you like to travel alone or with your friends?\nA: I prefer travelling with one or two people I get on with well. It&#x27;s safer and more enjoyable that way, and a small group still leaves room for <strong class=\"key-phrase\">personal flexibility</strong>.\n\nQ: Which other places have you travelled to?\nA: I&#x27;ve travelled to several places in Vietnam, including Hue, Da Nang and Ho Chi Minh City. Each trip was different, but Hue was especially memorable because of its historic sites and slower <strong class=\"key-phrase\">pace of life</strong>.\n\nQ: What do you usually do when you first arrive in a new place?\nA: I usually check the neighbourhood on foot, learn the basic transport routes and identify a few practical places nearby — it doesn&#x27;t take long, and it helps me <strong class=\"key-phrase\">feel at ease</strong> for the rest of the trip.","topic":"Travel & Holidays","phrases":[{"en":"broaden my horizons","context":"Q: Do you like travelling? Why?\nA: Yes, because it's a break from my usual routine and it exposes me to different ways of living. Even a short trip can broaden my horizons if I pay attention to the place rather than simply taking photographs."},{"en":"pay attention to","context":"Q: Do you like travelling? Why?\nA: Yes, because it's a break from my usual routine and it exposes me to different ways of living. Even a short trip can broaden my horizons if I pay attention to the place rather than simply taking photographs."},{"en":"personal flexibility","context":"Q: Do you like to travel alone or with your friends?\nA: I prefer travelling with one or two people I get on with well. It's safer and more enjoyable that way, and a small group still leaves room for personal flexibility."},{"en":"pace of life","context":"Q: Which other places have you travelled to?\nA: I've travelled to several places in Vietnam, including Hue, Da Nang and Ho Chi Minh City. Each trip was different, but Hue was especially memorable because of its historic sites and slower pace of life."},{"en":"feel at ease","context":"Q: What do you usually do when you first arrive in a new place?\nA: I usually check the neighbourhood on foot, learn the basic transport routes and identify a few practical places nearby — it doesn't take long, and it helps me feel at ease for the rest of the trip."}],"subtype":"Part 1","summary":"Travel & Holidays","visual":null,"id":"speaking-part-1-083","_displayNo":"#082","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-083-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-083-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-083-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-083-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"Yes, travelling gives me a break from normal life and helps me see how other people live. Even a short trip can teach me something if I pay attention to the place.","phrases":[{"en":"pay attention to","meaning":"Notice and think carefully about something."}],"question":"Do you like travelling? Why?","html":"Yes, travelling gives me a break from normal life and helps me see how other people live. Even a short trip can teach me something if I <strong class=\"key-phrase\">pay attention to</strong> the place."},{"text":"I prefer travelling with one or two friends I get along with. It feels safer and more enjoyable, while a small group still lets us change our plans fairly easily.","phrases":[{"en":"get along with","meaning":"Have a friendly and comfortable relationship with someone."}],"question":"Do you like to travel alone or with your friends?","html":"I prefer travelling with one or two friends I <strong class=\"key-phrase\">get along with</strong>. It feels safer and more enjoyable, while a small group still lets us change our plans fairly easily."},{"text":"I've visited several places in Vietnam, including Hue, Da Nang and Ho Chi Minh City. Hue stands out because of its historic places and more relaxed way of life.","phrases":[{"en":"stands out","meaning":"Is especially noticeable or memorable compared with other things."}],"question":"Which other places have you travelled to?","html":"I&#x27;ve visited several places in Vietnam, including Hue, Da Nang and Ho Chi Minh City. Hue <strong class=\"key-phrase\">stands out</strong> because of its historic places and more relaxed way of life."},{"text":"I usually walk around the area, find out how the transport works and look for useful places nearby. Doing that helps me feel comfortable for the rest of my stay.","phrases":[{"en":"find out","meaning":"Learn information you did not know before."}],"question":"What do you usually do when you first arrive in a new place?","html":"I usually walk around the area, <strong class=\"key-phrase\">find out</strong> how the transport works and look for useful places nearby. Doing that helps me feel comfortable for the rest of my stay."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-083-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-083-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-083-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-083-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"The benefits of visiting other countries","prompt":"What are the benefits of visiting different countries?\nWhat are the negative effects of tourism?\nWhat do you need to do before you go abroad on holiday?\nWhat type of problems can people have on holiday?","answer":"Q: What are the benefits of visiting different countries?\nA: Visiting other countries can challenge assumptions, improve communication and provide first-hand knowledge you just can&#x27;t get from books. It&#x27;s especially valuable when travellers <strong class=\"key-phrase\">engage with local life</strong> rather than staying in a tourist bubble.\n\nQ: What are the negative effects of tourism?\nA: Uncontrolled tourism can raise housing costs, overcrowd public spaces and damage natural sites. The problem isn&#x27;t tourism itself — it&#x27;s growth that ignores <strong class=\"key-phrase\">local carrying capacity</strong>.\n\nQ: What do you need to do before you go abroad on holiday?\nA: I check entry rules, insurance, transport, accommodation and basic local customs. Careful preparation means I don&#x27;t get caught out, while still leaving enough freedom for <strong class=\"key-phrase\">spontaneous experiences</strong>.\n\nQ: What type of problems can people have on holiday?\nA: Common holiday problems include delayed transport, illness, lost documents and unexpected costs, but they&#x27;re much easier to manage with travel insurance, digital copies of documents and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a realistic backup plan</strong>.","topic":"Travel & Holidays","phrases":[{"en":"engage with local life","context":"Q: What are the benefits of visiting different countries?\nA: Visiting other countries can challenge assumptions, improve communication and provide first-hand knowledge you just can't get from books. It's especially valuable when travellers engage with local life rather than staying in a tourist bubble."},{"en":"local carrying capacity","context":"Q: What are the negative effects of tourism?\nA: Uncontrolled tourism can raise housing costs, overcrowd public spaces and damage natural sites. The problem isn't tourism itself — it's growth that ignores local carrying capacity."},{"en":"spontaneous experiences","context":"Q: What do you need to do before you go abroad on holiday?\nA: I check entry rules, insurance, transport, accommodation and basic local customs. Careful preparation means I don't get caught out, while still leaving enough freedom for spontaneous experiences."},{"en":"a realistic backup plan","context":"Q: What type of problems can people have on holiday?\nA: Common holiday problems include delayed transport, illness, lost documents and unexpected costs, but they're much easier to manage with travel insurance, digital copies of documents and a realistic backup plan."}],"subtype":"Part 1","summary":"Travel & Holidays","visual":null,"id":"speaking-part-1-084","_displayNo":"#083","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-084-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-084-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-084-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-084-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"Travelling abroad can help us question our ideas, communicate better and learn through real experiences. It is especially useful when we spend time with local people and see how they live.","phrases":[{"en":"abroad","meaning":"In or to another country."}],"question":"What are the benefits of visiting different countries?","html":"Travelling <strong class=\"key-phrase\">abroad</strong> can help us question our ideas, communicate better and learn through real experiences. It is especially useful when we spend time with local people and see how they live."},{"text":"Too many tourists can make housing more expensive, crowd public places and damage nature. Tourism becomes a problem when visitor numbers grow beyond what an area can comfortably support.","phrases":[{"en":"beyond","meaning":"Further or more than a particular limit."}],"question":"What are the negative effects of tourism?","html":"Too many tourists can make housing more expensive, crowd public places and damage nature. Tourism becomes a problem when visitor numbers grow <strong class=\"key-phrase\">beyond</strong> what an area can comfortably support."},{"text":"I check the rules for entering the country, insurance, travel, a place to stay and local customs. Planning helps me avoid problems, but I still leave time for unexpected activities.","phrases":[{"en":"customs","meaning":"The usual traditions and ways of behaving in a place."}],"question":"What do you need to do before you go abroad on holiday?","html":"I check the rules for entering the country, insurance, travel, a place to stay and local <strong class=\"key-phrase\">customs</strong>. Planning helps me avoid problems, but I still leave time for unexpected activities."},{"text":"People may face travel delays, illness, lost passports or costs they did not expect. Insurance, copies of documents and a sensible second plan can make those problems easier to handle.","phrases":[{"en":"delays","meaning":"Situations in which something happens later than planned."}],"question":"What type of problems can people have on holiday?","html":"People may face travel <strong class=\"key-phrase\">delays</strong>, illness, lost passports or costs they did not expect. Insurance, copies of documents and a sensible second plan can make those problems easier to handle."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-084-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-084-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-084-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-084-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Trees in your hometown and why they matter","prompt":"Are there many trees in your hometown?\nWhat are the benefits of planting more trees?\nDo cities have enough trees?","answer":"Q: Are there many trees in your hometown?\nA: Some older parts of my hometown have mature trees, but the newer districts often don&#x27;t have as many. It&#x27;s pretty uneven, so how much greenery you get depends a lot on <strong class=\"key-phrase\">where people live</strong>.\n\nQ: What are the benefits of planting more trees?\nA: Trees reduce heat, absorb some pollution, manage rainwater and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">make streets more pleasant</strong>. They&#x27;re good for urban wildlife too, and overall they <strong class=\"key-phrase\">improve quality of life</strong>.\n\nQ: Do cities have enough trees?\nA: Many cities don&#x27;t have enough healthy, well-maintained trees. Planting campaigns help, but <strong class=\"key-phrase\">long-term care</strong> and protection during construction are <strong class=\"key-phrase\">equally important</strong>.","topic":"Trees","phrases":[{"en":"where people live","context":"Q: Are there many trees in your hometown?\nA: Some older parts of my hometown have mature trees, but the newer districts often don't have as many. It's pretty uneven, so how much greenery you get depends a lot on where people live."},{"en":"make streets more pleasant","context":"Q: What are the benefits of planting more trees?\nA: Trees reduce heat, absorb some pollution, manage rainwater and make streets more pleasant. They're good for urban wildlife too, and overall they improve quality of life."},{"en":"improve quality of life","context":"Q: What are the benefits of planting more trees?\nA: Trees reduce heat, absorb some pollution, manage rainwater and make streets more pleasant. They're good for urban wildlife too, and overall they improve quality of life."},{"en":"long-term care","context":"Q: Do cities have enough trees?\nA: Many cities don't have enough healthy, well-maintained trees. Planting campaigns help, but long-term care and protection during construction are equally important."},{"en":"equally important","context":"Q: Do cities have enough trees?\nA: Many cities don't have enough healthy, well-maintained trees. Planting campaigns help, but long-term care and protection during construction are equally important."}],"subtype":"","summary":"Trees","id":"speaking-part-1-085","_displayNo":"#084","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-085-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-085-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-085-q03.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"There are many large, older trees in some parts of my hometown. Newer areas often have fewer, so the amount of green space depends on which neighbourhood you are in.","phrases":[{"en":"green space","meaning":"An area with trees, grass or other plants."}],"question":"Are there many trees in your hometown?","html":"There are many large, older trees in some parts of my hometown. Newer areas often have fewer, so the amount of <strong class=\"key-phrase\">green space</strong> depends on which neighbourhood you are in."},{"text":"Trees provide shade, make places cooler, take in some pollution and help with rainwater. They also support wildlife and make streets nicer, which helps people enjoy living in the city.","phrases":[{"en":"wildlife","meaning":"Animals and other living things that live naturally in an area."}],"question":"What are the benefits of planting more trees?","html":"Trees provide shade, make places cooler, take in some pollution and help with rainwater. They also support <strong class=\"key-phrase\">wildlife</strong> and make streets nicer, which helps people enjoy living in the city."},{"text":"I don't think many cities have enough healthy trees. Planting new ones helps, but cities also need to care for them over time and protect them when building work happens nearby.","phrases":[{"en":"protect","meaning":"Keep something safe from harm or damage."}],"question":"Do cities have enough trees?","html":"I don&#x27;t think many cities have enough healthy trees. Planting new ones helps, but cities also need to care for them over time and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">protect</strong> them when building work happens nearby."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-085-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-085-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-085-q03.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Volunteering, and whether schools should encourage it","prompt":"Have you ever done volunteer work?\nWhy do people volunteer?\nShould schools encourage volunteering?","answer":"Q: Have you ever done volunteer work?\nA: Yes, I&#x27;ve helped with small educational and community activities. The work was modest, but it showed me that regular <strong class=\"key-phrase\">practical support</strong> can <strong class=\"key-phrase\">make a meaningful contribution</strong>.\n\nQ: Why do people volunteer?\nA: People volunteer to support a cause, gain experience or <strong class=\"key-phrase\">feel connected to their community</strong>. Usually it&#x27;s a combination of empathy and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a sense of purpose</strong> that motivates people most.\n\nQ: Should schools encourage volunteering?\nA: Yes, provided the work is age-appropriate and genuinely useful. Volunteering can develop responsibility and empathy, but it shouldn&#x27;t become <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a box-ticking exercise</strong>.","topic":"Volunteer Work","phrases":[{"en":"practical support","context":"Q: Have you ever done volunteer work?\nA: Yes, I've helped with small educational and community activities. The work was modest, but it showed me that regular practical support can make a meaningful contribution."},{"en":"make a meaningful contribution","context":"Q: Have you ever done volunteer work?\nA: Yes, I've helped with small educational and community activities. The work was modest, but it showed me that regular practical support can make a meaningful contribution."},{"en":"feel connected to their community","context":"Q: Why do people volunteer?\nA: People volunteer to support a cause, gain experience or feel connected to their community. Usually it's a combination of empathy and a sense of purpose that motivates people most."},{"en":"a sense of purpose","context":"Q: Why do people volunteer?\nA: People volunteer to support a cause, gain experience or feel connected to their community. Usually it's a combination of empathy and a sense of purpose that motivates people most."},{"en":"a box-ticking exercise","context":"Q: Should schools encourage volunteering?\nA: Yes, provided the work is age-appropriate and genuinely useful. Volunteering can develop responsibility and empathy, but it shouldn't become a box-ticking exercise."}],"subtype":"","summary":"Volunteer Work","id":"speaking-part-1-086","_displayNo":"#085","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-086-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-086-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-086-q03.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"Yes, I've helped with small activities related to education and the local community. They were not big projects, but they showed me how regular, practical help can make a difference.","phrases":[{"en":"make a difference","meaning":"Have a useful or positive effect."}],"question":"Have you ever done volunteer work?","html":"Yes, I&#x27;ve helped with small activities related to education and the local community. They were not big projects, but they showed me how regular, practical help can <strong class=\"key-phrase\">make a difference</strong>."},{"text":"People volunteer because they want to help, gain experience or feel part of their community. Often, they care about others and want to do something that has a purpose.","phrases":[{"en":"gain experience","meaning":"Learn and develop skills by doing something."}],"question":"Why do people volunteer?","html":"People volunteer because they want to help, <strong class=\"key-phrase\">gain experience</strong> or feel part of their community. Often, they care about others and want to do something that has a purpose."},{"text":"Yes, if the tasks suit the children's age and provide real help. Volunteering can teach responsibility and understanding, but it should mean more than simply completing a requirement.","phrases":[{"en":"responsibility","meaning":"Being willing to do what you should and accept the results of your actions."}],"question":"Should schools encourage volunteering?","html":"Yes, if the tasks suit the children&#x27;s age and provide real help. Volunteering can teach <strong class=\"key-phrase\">responsibility</strong> and understanding, but it should mean more than simply completing a requirement."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-086-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-086-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-086-q03.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Walking in the city and in the countryside","prompt":"Do you like walking?\nDo you think walking is important?\nDo you think walking in the countryside is better than walking in the city?\nWhat could be done to improve the experience of walking in cities?","answer":"Q: Do you like walking?\nA: I&#x27;m <strong class=\"key-phrase\">not one for</strong> <strong class=\"key-phrase\">going on really long walks</strong> in the countryside, but I don&#x27;t mind walking when I&#x27;m in a town or city, for example when I&#x27;m sightseeing in a new place.\n\nQ: Do you think walking is important?\nA: Yes, I think it&#x27;s important to be active, and walking is <strong class=\"key-phrase\">the most basic physical activity</strong> that we can do.\n\nQ: Do you think walking in the countryside is better than walking in the city?\nA: Personally, no. As I said before, I like walking in the city, especially if it&#x27;s somewhere with <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a lot of history</strong> like London or Paris.\n\nQ: What could be done to improve the experience of walking in cities?\nA: I suppose the main issues are space and safety. Pavements need to be wide enough to accommodate lots of pedestrians, and we need <strong class=\"key-phrase\">safe places to cross the street</strong>.","topic":"Walking","phrases":[{"en":"not one for","context":"Q: Do you like walking?\nA: I'm not one for going on really long walks in the countryside, but I don't mind walking when I'm in a town or city, for example when I'm sightseeing in a new place."},{"en":"going on really long walks","context":"Q: Do you like walking?\nA: I'm not one for going on really long walks in the countryside, but I don't mind walking when I'm in a town or city, for example when I'm sightseeing in a new place."},{"en":"the most basic physical activity","context":"Q: Do you think walking is important?\nA: Yes, I think it's important to be active, and walking is the most basic physical activity that we can do."},{"en":"a lot of history","context":"Q: Do you think walking in the countryside is better than walking in the city?\nA: Personally, no. As I said before, I like walking in the city, especially if it's somewhere with a lot of history like London or Paris."},{"en":"safe places to cross the street","context":"Q: What could be done to improve the experience of walking in cities?\nA: I suppose the main issues are space and safety. Pavements need to be wide enough to accommodate lots of pedestrians, and we need safe places to cross the street."}],"subtype":"","summary":"Walking","id":"speaking-part-1-087","_displayNo":"#086","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-087-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-087-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-087-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-087-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"I don't really enjoy very long country walks. However, I like walking around towns and cities, especially when I'm visiting a new place and looking at the sights.","phrases":[{"en":"the sights","meaning":"Interesting or famous places that visitors go to see."}],"question":"Do you like walking?","html":"I don&#x27;t really enjoy very long country walks. However, I like walking around towns and cities, especially when I&#x27;m visiting a new place and looking at <strong class=\"key-phrase\">the sights</strong>."},{"text":"Yes, walking is a simple way to keep moving and stay active. It is one of the easiest forms of exercise to include in everyday life.","phrases":[{"en":"stay active","meaning":"Keep moving your body regularly."}],"question":"Do you think walking is important?","html":"Yes, walking is a simple way to keep moving and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">stay active</strong>. It is one of the easiest forms of exercise to include in everyday life."},{"text":"Not for me. I prefer walking in cities, especially places with interesting history, such as London or Paris. There is more that I personally enjoy looking at there.","phrases":[{"en":"personally","meaning":"In my own opinion or experience."}],"question":"Do you think walking in the countryside is better than walking in the city?","html":"Not for me. I prefer walking in cities, especially places with interesting history, such as London or Paris. There is more that I <strong class=\"key-phrase\">personally</strong> enjoy looking at there."},{"text":"Cities should give people more space and make walking safer. Wider pavements would help when streets are busy, and we need safe places to cross the road.","phrases":[{"en":"pavements","meaning":"Paths at the side of a road for people to walk on."}],"question":"What could be done to improve the experience of walking in cities?","html":"Cities should give people more space and make walking safer. Wider <strong class=\"key-phrase\">pavements</strong> would help when streets are busy, and we need safe places to cross the road."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-087-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-087-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-087-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-087-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Your name and its meaning","prompt":"Could you tell me your full name please?\nWhat is your name?\nDoes your name have any special meaning?\nWhy do many people change their names?","answer":"Q: Could you tell me your full name please?\nA: My full name is Nguyen Nhat Dien, although people usually call me Dien. It&#x27;s <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a straightforward name</strong>, so I rarely need to explain or shorten it.\n\nQ: What is your name?\nA: My name&#x27;s Nguyen Nhat Dien, but almost everyone just calls me Dien — it&#x27;s the name I answer to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">without even thinking</strong>.\n\nQ: Does your name have any special meaning?\nA: It&#x27;s got a positive meaning in Vietnamese, and it was chosen by my family. I value it mainly because it connects me with them and gives me <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a sense of identity</strong>.\n\nQ: Why do many people change their names?\nA: People may change their names because of marriage, migration, personal identity or professional reasons. A new name can make communication easier, although changing it isn&#x27;t always simple — it usually involves <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a great deal of paperwork</strong>.","topic":"Warm-Up","phrases":[{"en":"a straightforward name","context":"Q: Could you tell me your full name please?\nA: My full name is Nguyen Nhat Dien, although people usually call me Dien. It's a straightforward name, so I rarely need to explain or shorten it."},{"en":"without even thinking","context":"Q: What is your name?\nA: My name's Nguyen Nhat Dien, but almost everyone just calls me Dien — it's the name I answer to without even thinking."},{"en":"a sense of identity","context":"Q: Does your name have any special meaning?\nA: It's got a positive meaning in Vietnamese, and it was chosen by my family. I value it mainly because it connects me with them and gives me a sense of identity."},{"en":"a great deal of paperwork","context":"Q: Why do many people change their names?\nA: People may change their names because of marriage, migration, personal identity or professional reasons. A new name can make communication easier, although changing it isn't always simple — it usually involves a great deal of paperwork."}],"subtype":"Part 1","summary":"Warm-Up","visual":null,"id":"speaking-part-1-088","_displayNo":"#087","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-088-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-088-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-088-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-088-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"My full name is Nguyen Nhat Dien, but most people call me Dien. It is quite easy to use, so I rarely have to explain it or make it shorter.","phrases":[{"en":"full name","meaning":"Your complete name, including all its parts."}],"question":"Could you tell me your full name please?","html":"My <strong class=\"key-phrase\">full name</strong> is Nguyen Nhat Dien, but most people call me Dien. It is quite easy to use, so I rarely have to explain it or make it shorter."},{"text":"My name is Nguyen Nhat Dien. Most people just call me Dien, so that is the name I'm most used to hearing in everyday conversations.","phrases":[{"en":"used to hearing","meaning":"Familiar with hearing something often."}],"question":"What is your name?","html":"My name is Nguyen Nhat Dien. Most people just call me Dien, so that is the name I&#x27;m most <strong class=\"key-phrase\">used to hearing</strong> in everyday conversations."},{"text":"Yes, it has a positive meaning in Vietnamese. My family chose it, and it is important to me because it reminds me of them and feels like part of who I am.","phrases":[{"en":"positive","meaning":"Expressing something good or hopeful."}],"question":"Does your name have any special meaning?","html":"Yes, it has a <strong class=\"key-phrase\">positive</strong> meaning in Vietnamese. My family chose it, and it is important to me because it reminds me of them and feels like part of who I am."},{"text":"People change names for marriage, moving countries, personal reasons or work. A different name can be easier to use, but making the change official often means completing many forms.","phrases":[{"en":"official","meaning":"Formally accepted or recorded by the relevant authorities."}],"question":"Why do many people change their names?","html":"People change names for marriage, moving countries, personal reasons or work. A different name can be easier to use, but making the change <strong class=\"key-phrase\">official</strong> often means completing many forms."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-088-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-088-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-088-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-088-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"The weather where you live and your favourite season","prompt":"What's the weather like in your country?\nDoes the weather affect your mood?\nWhat's your favourite season of the year?\nWhat do you usually do in winter?","answer":"Q: What&#x27;s the weather like in your country?\nA: Vietnam has a varied climate, but Hanoi has hot, humid summers and cooler, drier winters. The transition seasons can be pleasant, although the weather&#x27;s becoming <strong class=\"key-phrase\">less predictable</strong>.\n\nQ: Does the weather affect your mood?\nA: Yes, slightly. Bright, mild weather gives me more energy, while long periods of humidity can make daily tasks feel tiring. I try not to let it <strong class=\"key-phrase\">determine my whole day</strong>.\n\nQ: What&#x27;s your favourite season of the year?\nA: Autumn is my favourite because the temperature is comfortable and the air is usually clearer. It&#x27;s the easiest season for walking, working and spending time <strong class=\"key-phrase\">outdoors comfortably</strong>.\n\nQ: What do you usually do in winter?\nA: In winter I exercise indoors, drink hot tea and spend more time reading. I also enjoy walking on dry, cool days because the city feels <strong class=\"key-phrase\">quieter and calmer</strong>.","topic":"Weather","phrases":[{"en":"less predictable","context":"Q: What's the weather like in your country?\nA: Vietnam has a varied climate, but Hanoi has hot, humid summers and cooler, drier winters. The transition seasons can be pleasant, although the weather's becoming less predictable."},{"en":"determine my whole day","context":"Q: Does the weather affect your mood?\nA: Yes, slightly. Bright, mild weather gives me more energy, while long periods of humidity can make daily tasks feel tiring. I try not to let it determine my whole day."},{"en":"outdoors comfortably","context":"Q: What's your favourite season of the year?\nA: Autumn is my favourite because the temperature is comfortable and the air is usually clearer. It's the easiest season for walking, working and spending time outdoors comfortably."},{"en":"quieter and calmer","context":"Q: What do you usually do in winter?\nA: In winter I exercise indoors, drink hot tea and spend more time reading. I also enjoy walking on dry, cool days because the city feels quieter and calmer."}],"subtype":"Part 1","summary":"Weather","visual":null,"id":"speaking-part-1-089","_displayNo":"#088","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-089-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-089-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-089-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-089-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"The weather varies across Vietnam. Hanoi has hot, wet summers and cooler, drier winters. Spring and autumn can be pleasant, although it is becoming harder to know what weather to expect.","phrases":[{"en":"varies","meaning":"Is different in different places or situations."}],"question":"What's the weather like in your country?","html":"The weather <strong class=\"key-phrase\">varies</strong> across Vietnam. Hanoi has hot, wet summers and cooler, drier winters. Spring and autumn can be pleasant, although it is becoming harder to know what weather to expect."},{"text":"Yes, a little. Sunny weather that is not too hot gives me more energy, while long periods of damp heat make me tired. I still try not to let it control my day.","phrases":[{"en":"damp heat","meaning":"Warm conditions with a lot of moisture in the air."}],"question":"Does the weather affect your mood?","html":"Yes, a little. Sunny weather that is not too hot gives me more energy, while long periods of <strong class=\"key-phrase\">damp heat</strong> make me tired. I still try not to let it control my day."},{"text":"Autumn is my favourite because it is neither too hot nor too cold, and the air often feels clearer. I find it comfortable for walking, working and spending time outside.","phrases":[{"en":"neither too hot nor too cold","meaning":"Having a comfortable temperature between the two extremes."}],"question":"What's your favourite season of the year?","html":"Autumn is my favourite because it is <strong class=\"key-phrase\">neither too hot nor too cold</strong>, and the air often feels clearer. I find it comfortable for walking, working and spending time outside."},{"text":"I exercise inside, drink hot tea and read more in winter. I also enjoy walking when it is cool and dry because the city seems quieter and more peaceful.","phrases":[{"en":"peaceful","meaning":"Calm and quiet."}],"question":"What do you usually do in winter?","html":"I exercise inside, drink hot tea and read more in winter. I also enjoy walking when it is cool and dry because the city seems quieter and more <strong class=\"key-phrase\">peaceful</strong>."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-089-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-089-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-089-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-089-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Your job and your plans for your career","prompt":"Can you tell me about the job you do?\nWhat do you like or dislike about it?\nWhat plans do you have for your career in the future?\nHow serious is unemployment in your country?","answer":"Q: Can you tell me about the job you do?\nA: I work as an English teacher. My job involves planning lessons, explaining tricky points, and giving feedback that helps students <strong class=\"key-phrase\">make steady progress</strong>.\n\nQ: What do you like or dislike about it?\nA: I like seeing students become more confident and independent. The hard part&#x27;s the amount of preparation and marking, especially when a few deadlines <strong class=\"key-phrase\">fall in the same week</strong>.\n\nQ: What plans do you have for your career in the future?\nA: I&#x27;d like to develop my teaching skills further and get better at using technology in my classes. Longer term, I&#x27;d love to create learning materials that are <strong class=\"key-phrase\">both practical and rigorous</strong>.\n\nQ: How serious is unemployment in your country?\nA: It varies a lot by sector, but young graduates often struggle to find work that matches what they&#x27;ve trained for. It&#x27;s not just about the number of jobs available — it&#x27;s also <strong class=\"key-phrase\">the mismatch of skills</strong>.","topic":"Work","phrases":[{"en":"make steady progress","context":"Q: Can you tell me about the job you do?\nA: I work as an English teacher. My job involves planning lessons, explaining tricky points, and giving feedback that helps students make steady progress."},{"en":"fall in the same week","context":"Q: What do you like or dislike about it?\nA: I like seeing students become more confident and independent. The hard part's the amount of preparation and marking, especially when a few deadlines fall in the same week."},{"en":"both practical and rigorous","context":"Q: What plans do you have for your career in the future?\nA: I'd like to develop my teaching skills further and get better at using technology in my classes. Longer term, I'd love to create learning materials that are both practical and rigorous."},{"en":"the mismatch of skills","context":"Q: How serious is unemployment in your country?\nA: It varies a lot by sector, but young graduates often struggle to find work that matches what they've trained for. It's not just about the number of jobs available — it's also the mismatch of skills."}],"subtype":"Part 1","summary":"Job","visual":null,"id":"speaking-part-1-046","_displayNo":"#089","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-046-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-046-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-046-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-046-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"I'm an English teacher. I plan lessons, explain difficult language and give students advice on their work. My main aim is to help them improve step by step.","phrases":[{"en":"step by step","meaning":"Gradually, through a series of small stages."}],"question":"Can you tell me about the job you do?","html":"I&#x27;m an English teacher. I plan lessons, explain difficult language and give students advice on their work. My main aim is to help them improve <strong class=\"key-phrase\">step by step</strong>."},{"text":"I like seeing students become more confident and able to learn by themselves. However, preparing lessons and checking work takes a lot of time, especially when several tasks are due together.","phrases":[{"en":"due","meaning":"Needing to be finished or handed in by a particular time."}],"question":"What do you like or dislike about it?","html":"I like seeing students become more confident and able to learn by themselves. However, preparing lessons and checking work takes a lot of time, especially when several tasks are <strong class=\"key-phrase\">due</strong> together."},{"text":"I want to become a better teacher and use technology more effectively in class. Later, I'd like to make learning materials that are useful, clear and carefully checked.","phrases":[{"en":"effectively","meaning":"In a way that produces the result you want."}],"question":"What plans do you have for your career in the future?","html":"I want to become a better teacher and use technology more <strong class=\"key-phrase\">effectively</strong> in class. Later, I&#x27;d like to make learning materials that are useful, clear and carefully checked."},{"text":"It depends on the type of work. Many young graduates find it hard to get jobs related to their studies. Sometimes jobs exist, but applicants do not have the skills employers need.","phrases":[{"en":"graduates","meaning":"People who have completed a university course."}],"question":"How serious is unemployment in your country?","html":"It depends on the type of work. Many young <strong class=\"key-phrase\">graduates</strong> find it hard to get jobs related to their studies. Sometimes jobs exist, but applicants do not have the skills employers need."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-046-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-046-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-046-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-046-q04.mp3"]},{"section":"speaking-part-1","title":"Your job, and working alone or with others","prompt":"Do you work or are you a student?\nDo you enjoy your job?\nWhat's the best thing about your job?\nDo you prefer working alone or with others?","answer":"Q: Do you work or are you a student?\nA: I&#x27;m <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a qualified doctor</strong>, but at the moment I&#x27;m studying English so that I can work in this country.\n\nQ: Do you enjoy your job?\nA: Yes. I&#x27;ve wanted to become a doctor since childhood, and I still find the work meaningful because it allows me to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">help people recover</strong> and make difficult periods more manageable.\n\nQ: What&#x27;s the best thing about your job?\nA: The best thing about my job is that I can <strong class=\"key-phrase\">make a difference</strong> in people&#x27;s lives. It&#x27;s a great feeling when patients and their families feel reassured just because we took the time to explain things clearly.\n\nQ: Do you prefer working alone or with others?\nA: In a hospital you have to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">work as part of a team</strong>. I&#x27;ve got used to working with others, and I think you can <strong class=\"key-phrase\">achieve a lot more as a team</strong> than you would alone.","topic":"Work","phrases":[{"en":"a qualified doctor","context":"Q: Do you work or are you a student?\nA: I'm a qualified doctor, but at the moment I'm studying English so that I can work in this country."},{"en":"help people recover","context":"Q: Do you enjoy your job?\nA: Yes. I've wanted to become a doctor since childhood, and I still find the work meaningful because it allows me to help people recover and make difficult periods more manageable."},{"en":"make a difference","context":"Q: What's the best thing about your job?\nA: The best thing about my job is that I can make a difference in people's lives. It's a great feeling when patients and their families feel reassured just because we took the time to explain things clearly."},{"en":"work as part of a team","context":"Q: Do you prefer working alone or with others?\nA: In a hospital you have to work as part of a team. I've got used to working with others, and I think you can achieve a lot more as a team than you would alone."},{"en":"achieve a lot more as a team","context":"Q: Do you prefer working alone or with others?\nA: In a hospital you have to work as part of a team. I've got used to working with others, and I think you can achieve a lot more as a team than you would alone."}],"subtype":"","summary":"Work","id":"speaking-part-1-090","_displayNo":"#090","qaAudio":["audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-090-q01.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-090-q02.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-090-q03.mp3","audio/ava-us/qa/speaking-part-1-090-q04.mp3"],"simpleAnswers":[{"text":"I'm a trained doctor, but I'm currently studying English. I want to improve my English so I can work as a doctor in this country.","phrases":[{"en":"trained","meaning":"Having learned the skills and knowledge needed for a job."}],"question":"Do you work or are you a student?","html":"I&#x27;m a <strong class=\"key-phrase\">trained</strong> doctor, but I&#x27;m currently studying English. I want to improve my English so I can work as a doctor in this country."},{"text":"Yes, I do. I've wanted to be a doctor since I was a child. Helping people get better and supporting them during difficult times still makes the work feel important to me.","phrases":[{"en":"get better","meaning":"Recover or become healthier."}],"question":"Do you enjoy your job?","html":"Yes, I do. I&#x27;ve wanted to be a doctor since I was a child. Helping people <strong class=\"key-phrase\">get better</strong> and supporting them during difficult times still makes the work feel important to me."},{"text":"The best part is helping patients and their families. Sometimes, explaining a situation clearly makes them feel less worried. It is rewarding to know that my work can improve their lives.","phrases":[{"en":"rewarding","meaning":"Giving you a feeling of satisfaction because you have done something useful."}],"question":"What's the best thing about your job?","html":"The best part is helping patients and their families. Sometimes, explaining a situation clearly makes them feel less worried. It is <strong class=\"key-phrase\">rewarding</strong> to know that my work can improve their lives."},{"text":"I work with others because hospital work depends on a team. I'm used to it now, and I think we can do more together than one person could achieve alone.","phrases":[{"en":"achieve","meaning":"Succeed in doing something you have worked towards."}],"question":"Do you prefer working alone or with others?","html":"I work with others because hospital work depends on a team. I&#x27;m used to it now, and I think we can do more together than one person could <strong class=\"key-phrase\">achieve</strong> alone."}],"simpleQaAudio":["audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-090-q01.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-090-q02.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-090-q03.mp3","audio/simple/speaking-part-1/speaking-part-1-090-q04.mp3"]}]);
